SCO 39-42, Sector 82','',28,507,'160062','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.05pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:\r\n9.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; The applicant vide their application dated 02.04.2013 applied for an apartment and\r\naccordingly 4 BHK Apartment i.e. No. E-401, 4</span><sup><span style=\"font-size: 6.5pt; font-family: Arial;\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;Floor,\r\nwing E, Facing Green, Falcon View, Phase-II, (wrongly mentioned as Phase-I, in\r\nallotment letter dated 02.08.2013, Annexure C-1) Sector 66-A, Mohali, Punjab,\r\nmeasuring 3007 sq. ft., @Rs.3,600/- per sq. ft., was allotted in favor of the\r\napplicant vide Allotment Letter dated 02.08.2013, alongwith details of plot and\r\nthe total sale consideration amount was fixed as Rs.1,08,25,200/-. Copy of\r\nallotment letter is&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Annexure C-1.</span></b></span></p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">\r\n\r\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.05pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">That as\r\nper the demands raised by the respondents, the applicant kept on making payment\r\nto the respondents and the applicant paid the following amount to the\r\nrespondents copies of all the receipts are&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">Annexure C-2 to C-11</span></b></span></p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">\r\n\r\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.05pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">That as\r\nper Clause no.2.24 of the allotment letter dated 02.08.2013 (annexure C-1) the\r\npossession of the said apartment complete in all respects shall be delivered to\r\nthe applicant by 01.02.2016, i.e. 30 months from the date of allotment letter\r\ni.e. 02.08.2013.</span></span></p><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">\r\n\r\n</span><p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 8.5pt;\">That\r\nin-spite of the receipt of substantial amount against the said apartment the\r\nrespondents have failed to complete the said apartment and further failed to\r\noffer the possession of the said apartment upto 01.02.2016. The applicant in\r\nMay, 2016, approached the respondents and inquired about the dated of the\r\ndelivery of possession but the respondents have failed to give\r\nany&nbsp;satisfactory&nbsp;response and started lingered-on, the matter on one\r\npretext or the other. However the applicant was assured that the possession of\r\nthe said apartment shall be delivered upto July, 2016, positively and\r\nshockingly the possession of the apartment was not offered by the respondents\r\nto the applicant in July, 2016, as promised by the respondents.</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 16.1px;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 18.4px; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">o<o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 16.1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 18.4px; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">In&nbsp;&nbsp;view&nbsp;&nbsp;of&nbsp;&nbsp;the&nbsp;&nbsp;facts&nbsp;&nbsp;mentioned&nbsp;&nbsp;in&nbsp;&nbsp;paragraph&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;above,&nbsp;&nbsp;the&nbsp;&nbsp;applicant prays&nbsp;&nbsp;for&nbsp;&nbsp;the following compensation(s)<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">That as the respondents have failed to comply with the terms and conditions of the allotment letter dated 02.08.2013 (Annexure C-1) and have failed to deliver the possession of the apartment/flat within the stipulated time. Therefore, the applicant as per section 18 of the RERA Act. 2016, is entitled for<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Refund principal amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">10,580,830/-&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">of the applicant&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">along</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;with interest @ 18% P.a. from the date of actual payment till realization.<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000/- to the applicant for mental harassment, mental agony<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Any other relief which this Hon’ble authority deems fit may also be passed in favor of the applicant.</span></p>',10825200.00,10580830.00,'2016-02-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-08-02 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat no E401,Falcon View, sector 66A, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'GVstarLLP','2018-08-29 14:37:26.000','GVstarLLP','2018-08-29 14:37:26.000'),(56,1027,'1027',1068,'21687434-1c56-4184-a26c-ec561c2f2dcd','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sandeep Mann','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','1','2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0033','Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Developers Pvt. Ltd','Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Pvt. Ltd','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor, Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh','',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor, Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh','',28,507,'140901','1','<p>Please see attachment</p>','<p>Please see attachment</p>',5396503.00,5266702.00,'2013-06-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-11-03 00:00:00','2011-08-25 00:00:00','OCEA/II/374','','',2,0,0,0,'smann','2018-08-29 21:28:11.000','smann','2018-08-29 21:28:11.000'),(57,1028,'1028',1085,'416c72a3-a2db-42db-9e91-50fe152da8ff','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-08-31 10:13:14.000','Mohinder Jit Kaur','mishrasatty7@gmail.com',9888757966,7888356908,325501434204,'224 A, LAST LANE, SHASTRI NAGAR','Mani Majra',6,128,'160101','1','224 A, LAST LANE, SHASTRI NAGAR','Mani Majra',6,128,'160101','Satish Mishra','advocatesatish7@gmail.com',9988817966,7888356908,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','Punjab Urban Planning & Development Authority (PUDA)','Punjab Urban Planning & Development Authority (PUDA)','helpdesk@puda.gov.in',1722215202,1722215202,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160055','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1 That the respondent issued Letter of Intent (LOI) to applicant for residential Plot no. 165/Park Facing measuring 400 Sq. Yard, Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali- 160055 dated 24.8.2015 in reference to application Form No. 10457. The Letter of Intent (LOI) is hereby appended as Annexure A-1. \r\n</p><p>2 That in furtherance of Letter of Intent (LOI), Allotment Letter appended as Annexure A-2 dated 26.8.2016 was issued to applicant. The tentative price of the plot is Rs. 88,20,000/- at the rate of Rs. 21,000/- Rs/Sq. Yard.  \r\n</p><p>3 That in pursuance to Allotment Letter, Applicant made following payments as per the payment schedule and financial conditions stated in letter:\r\n</p><p>S.no	Date	Mode	Type	Amount\r\n</p><p>1	15.1.2015	Bank Transfer	Earnest Money	8,40,000/-\r\n</p><p>2	18.3.2016	DD	Allotment Money	12,60,000/-\r\n</p><p>3	21.3.2016	DD	Installment	1,52,000/-\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;Cancer Cess 2%	1,68,000/-\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;Total Amt.	24,20,000/-\r\n</p><p>Thus, till date Rs. 24,20,000/- has been paid by Applicant to the respondent as per statement of account appended as Annexure A-3. \r\n</p><p>&nbsp;4 That as per the Allotment Letter dated 26.8.2016, the possession of the said plot in question was to be given within 18 months from the date of issuance of allotment which is already over i.e. 26.2.2018 Thus, the respondent has failed to handover possession within the stipulated time as written in the allotment letter agreed between the parties. \r\n</p><p>5 The respondent has yet to give reply to Applicant whether they have got the Occupancy Certificate/Completion Certificate for the said plot or not? Respondent has been avoiding this question for too long since the Allotment letter was issued. \r\n</p><p>6 That the said project promoted by respondent lacks basic infrastructure like roads, poor connectivity, drains, electricity, water supply, green cover and parks, street lights missing, roads without berm, no provision of security nor any existence of police post. All these factors further make plot unfit for habitation and construction.\r\n</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1 Refund of the\r\nAmount i.e. Rs. 24,20,000/- with same interest as stated by respondent for the buyer\r\nin the agreement plus Compensation for delay in possession under </span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Section\r\n18</span></b></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> in contravention to\r\nAllotment Letter and in consonance with provisions of RERA Act which is SBI\r\nMCLR plus 2%. <o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2 Compensation for\r\ninability/failure to discharge obligations as per Allotment Letter and RERA Act\r\nunder </span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Section 18 (3)</span></i></b></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> lacking in basic services which was initially\r\npromised and no disclosure about status of Completion Certificate/Occupancy\r\nCertificate before handing over the possession.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">3\r\nCompensation on account of mental agony, pain and litigation expenses upto Rs.\r\n2 lakh as illustrated in the Section 72 of the RERA Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">4 Any other appropriate remedy or\r\nrelief which this court may deem fit in the present circumstances may also be\r\nawarded in the favour of Applicant.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',8820000.00,2420000.00,'2018-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot no. 165, Park  Facing Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'Satish','2018-08-30 17:53:29.000','Satish','2018-08-30 17:53:29.000'),(58,1029,'1029',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-09-05 15:08:33.000','avneet kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,0,'house no 60B','Model town, Phagwara',28,300,'144401','1','house no 60B','Model town, Phagwara',28,300,'144401','VIKRAM SINGH CHAHAL','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','Mohali Hill Augusta Green, Sector 109, Mohali','EMAAR MGF LAND PVT LTD','',0,0,'ECE HOUSE LEVEL I','28 KASTURBA GANDHI MARG',10,120,'110001','1','ECE HOUSE LEVEL I','28 KASTURBA GANDHI MARG',10,120,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the\r\ncomplainant/allottee after shown rosy picture by the respondents&nbsp;</span>decided to buy the plot in the\r\nproject of respondents and&nbsp;plot buyer agreement was\r\nsigned and executed at Chandigarh on 04.07.2007 for Plot No&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">104 measuring 400 sq yds. in Augusta Greens in Sector 109&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">on BSP of Rs. 46,00,000/- at the rate of 11,500/- per\r\nsq. yd. and the total sale price of the plot in question was fixed at Rs.\r\n54,00,472/-. P</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">ossession of the plot was to be given within a\r\nmaximum time period of 3 years as per clause no. 8 of Annexure C-1 by\r\n03.07.2010. The complaint has&nbsp;availed&nbsp;loan from HDFC bank for the payment of the\r\nconsideration and despite of 99% payment made by the complainant to the\r\nrespondent, they have failed to give possession of the plot. Several emails\r\nwere exchanged but to the no effect of the respondents.&nbsp;the respondent no. 1 to 3 have directly given an amount of Rs,\r\n37,55,255/-drawn on HSBC Bank in&nbsp;&nbsp;favour of respondent No. 4 (HDFC Bank) without intimating the complainant\r\nby cancelling the allotment of the complainant without any reason what so ever.\r\nRespondent No. 1 to 3 had already&nbsp;cancelled the allotment and\r\nremitted the amount directly to respondent No. 4 without any intimation to the\r\ncomplainant and&nbsp;here it is to be seen that for the plot/land which is not even&nbsp;in the name of the respondent No. 1 to 3 till today how the cancellation\r\nof that plot can be there and that too without intimating the complainant\r\ntherefore through this complaint requesting this Hon\'ble Court for refund of\r\nthe amount along with other reliefs as prayed in the prayer clause.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">(i) The respondents be directed to refund sum of Rs 1801648 paid by the complainant out of his own sources, beside the EMI@ Rs 36744 for 9 years total amounting to Rs 25,71,909 with interest @14% per annum from the date of the payment till realization.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">ii) </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">The respondents be further directed to pay Rs.5,00,000/- </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">as compensation for causing mental torture,\r\nagony and physical </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">harassment and\r\nfurther Rs.50,000/- as litigation cost for </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">compelling\r\nthe complainant to approach this Hon\'ble Authority </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">for the redressal of her genuine grievance.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:21.6pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Or<br>\r\n<span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Any other relief which this Hon\'ble Authority\r\nmay deem fit and proper may pass in favour of the complainant, in the interest\r\nof justice</span>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5301648.00,4373557.00,'2010-07-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2007-08-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot no 104, Mohali Hill Augusta Green, Sector 109, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'P43982017','2018-08-30 19:14:59.000','P43982017','2018-08-30 19:14:59.000'),(59,1027,'1027',1068,'21687434-1c56-4184-a26c-ec561c2f2dcd','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sandeep Mann','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','1','2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0033','Phase-3 development of Mega Residential project\r\n','Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Pvt. Ltd','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor, Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh','',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor, Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh','',28,507,'140901','1','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;That\r\nthe present complaint is being filed before this Hon’ble Court for violation of\r\ninter alia Section 18 read with Section 19(4)of the Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2016 [“<b>Act</b>”] read\r\nwith Rule 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nRules, 2017 [“<b>Rules</b>”], against the\r\nRespondent for gross negligence in providing deficient services, by\r\nfraudulently alluring the Complainant to invest in a bogus Real Estate Project\r\ncalled “Omaxe Chandigarh Extension” [“<b>The\r\nProject</b>”]<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">a.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">The\r\nRespondent be directed to pay the Complainant interest as per Rule 16 of the\r\nPunjab RERA Rules at the marginal cost of lending rate as given by State Bank\r\nof India plus 2 percent forevery month of delayi.e from 6<sup>th</sup> January\r\n2013<a name=\"_GoBack\"></a>on the deposited amount till possession is given for\r\nviolation of Section 18 of the Act.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">b.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">1,50,000/- on account of mental\r\nharassment;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">c.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs .1,00,000/- as litigation\r\nexpenses;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">d.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Any other compensation /Order which\r\nthe Adjudicating Officer may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the\r\npresent case.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5396503.00,5266702.00,'2013-06-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-11-03 00:00:00','2011-08-25 00:00:00','OCEA/II/374','','',2,0,0,0,'smann','2018-08-31 10:48:48.000','smann','2018-08-31 10:48:48.000'),(60,1030,'1030',1081,'e4107d19-0392-40e6-9c1c-2bb0a6920e04','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rupinder Mannn','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426 Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','1','2426 Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0033','Phase-3 development of Mega\r\nResidential project','Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Pvt. Ltd','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">That\r\nthe present complaint is being filed before this Honble Court for violation of\r\ninter alia Section 18 read with Section 19(4) of the Real Estate (Regulation\r\nand Development) Act, 2016 [“<b>Act</b>”]\r\nread with Rule 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nRules, 2017 [“<b>Rules</b>”], against the\r\nRespondentfor gross negligence in providing deficient services, by fraudulently\r\nalluring the Complainant to invest in a bogus Real Estate Project called “Omaxe\r\nChandigarh Extension” [“<b>The Project</b>”]</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><o:p>Please check attachments for detailed Fact of the case.</o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-left: 72pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\">a. The\r\nRespondent be directed to pay the Complainant interest as per Rule 16 of the\r\nPunjab RERA Rules at the marginal cost of lending rate as given by State Bank\r\nof India plus 2 percent for every monthof </span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\">delayi.e from 6</span><sup style=\"text-indent: -18pt;\">th</sup><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\"> January 2013 on\r\nthe deposited amount till possession is given for violation of Section 18 of\r\nthe Act.</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">b.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Rs</span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">.</span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">1,50,000/- on account of mental\r\nharassment;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">c.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Rs .1,00,000/- as litigation\r\nexpenses;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">d.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Any other compensation /Order which\r\nthe Adjudicating Officer may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the\r\npresent case.</span></p>',5396703.00,4814456.00,'2013-01-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-11-03 00:00:00','2011-08-25 00:00:00','OCEA/II/373 ','','',2,0,0,0,'rmann','2018-08-31 11:24:07.000','rmann','2018-08-31 11:24:07.000'),(61,1031,'1031',1022,'33a0ed60-04ed-4ddd-b47a-6c6e5113bf37','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Nikhil Juneja','nikhil_sp1@yahoo.com',8699499940,0,0,'128, Shakti Nagar','',28,261,'144001','1','128, Shakti Nagar','',28,261,'144001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-JAL33-PM0077','Old Jail Site, Jalandhar','PUNJAB URBAN PLANNING AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA BHAWAN SECTOR- 62','SAS NAGAR MOHAL',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA BHAWAN SECTOR- 62','SAS NAGAR MOHAL',28,507,'160062','1','<p>\r\n		\r\n	\r\n	\r\n		</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n			<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n				<div class=\"column\">\r\n					<p><span style=\"font-size: 11.000000pt; font-family: \'Helvetica\'\">I purchased plot number 65C at Old Jail site, Jalandhar on 22/04/2016 via PUDA auction. On 17/08/2016\r\nI received the allotment letter in which it was mentioned that the possession shall be handed over within 1\r\nyear of the Auction. The possession has been delayed by over 2 years. I was offered possession on\r\n26/06/2018, and the possession letter stated that the electricity works is completed. On 09/07/2018 I\r\nvisited the site and while inspection I found out that electricity works on the site were not complete. PUDA\r\nhas offered possession without completing necessary works. Even the MLA of the area had expressed his\r\nconcern regarding the development of the site. I have made lump sum payment for the plot on 19/04/2018\r\nby arranging a loan from Punjab National Bank and applied for No Due Certificate on 02/05/2018. But still\r\nPUDA hasn\'t issued the NO Due Certificate. Lastly I went to visit site again on 01/08/2018 and found that\r\nthe contractor for the site were using JCB machine and tipper trucks to steal soil from the plots and were\r\ndumping waste construction material (Malba) to level the plots. I immediately went to see my plot and\r\nfound out that same had been done with my plot. I have a video of this incident and can share the video\r\nwith the authorities.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n				</div>\r\n			</div>\r\n		</div>','<p>\r\n		\r\n	\r\n	\r\n		</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n			<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n				<div class=\"column\">\r\n					<p><span style=\"font-size: 11.000000pt; font-family: \'Helvetica\'\">PUDA should complete all the pending works at the site and issue possession letter again after\r\ncompletion of works. The existing possession letter should be declared void as the work mentioned in the\r\nletter is not complete. PUDA should pay me penalty for delaying the possession @18% PA on the\r\nmonthly compounding basis this interest should be applicable from the date os payment made by me and\r\ntill the issue of new possession letter post completion of all necessary work like electricity work, as PUDA\r\nwould charges @18% PA interest from me in case there is a payment default at my end. Now they should\r\nbe penalised for the delay in similar order. PUDA should extract all the construction waste (Malba) from\r\nthe plot and put proper soil and take necessary security measures to prevent the theft from the plot.\r\nBecause of the delay in giving in the possession I am being forced to pay interest even with out getting\r\npossession. This has put me in significant financial constraints and mental stress. Now they should be\r\npenalised with mental harassment fee of 15 Lakhs.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n				</div>\r\n			</div>\r\n		</div>',11402358.00,11406647.61,'2017-04-22 00:00:00.000','2018-06-26 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-17 00:00:00','2016-04-22 00:00:00','65C Old Jail Site, Jalandhar.','','',2,0,0,0,'nikhil_sp1','2018-08-31 12:15:17.000','nikhil_sp1','2018-08-31 12:15:17.000'),(62,1032,'1032',1068,'21687434-1c56-4184-a26c-ec561c2f2dcd','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-08-31 18:02:32.000','Sandeep Mann','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','1','2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0007','India Trade Tower','Bhanuinfrabuild Pvt. Ltd. ','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">That the present complaint is being filed before this\r\nHonble Court for violation of inter alia Section 18 read with Section 14 of\r\nthe Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 “<b>Act</b>” read with Rule 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation\r\nand Development) Rules, 2017 “<b>Rules</b>”,\r\nagainst the Respondent Lessee for gross negligence in providing deficient\r\nservices, by fraudulently alluring the Complainant to invest in a bogus Real\r\nEstate Project called “India Trade Tower” as a part of integrated township\r\nProject situated at Omaxe New Chandigarh, District SAS Nagar, Punjab.“<b>The Project</b>”</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><o:p>For detailed Facts of the case please refer attachments.</o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">As per\r\nSection 18(1)(a) read with Section 19(4) of the Act, the Promoter is under an\r\nobligation to fulfill his responsibilities in accordance with the terms of the\r\nLease Agreement. As per the Lease Agreement, the Lessee was under an obligation\r\nto allot </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">Allotted </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Commercial Space/Office Space bearing No.\r\nITTC/FOURTEENTH/OFFICE-1401B in Commercial Complex India Trade Tower as part of\r\nintegrated township project “Omaxe New Chandigarh” measuring 1408.76 Sq. Ft\r\nor 130.88 Sq.Mtr but they have without the consent of the Lessor offered\r\n1053.38 Sq. Ft or 97.86 Sq. Mtr which is in complete violation of Section 14 of\r\nthe Act.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri\">Direct the Lessee to allot Lessee the Unit as was agreed measuring\r\n1408.76 Sq. Ft or in the Alternative refund the excess amount of Rs. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">7,32,077.54\r\nalongwith interes</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">Direct the Lessee to comply with clause 7.1.2 of the Lease\r\nAgreement and issue cheques amounting to Rs. 52,124.12 i.e. (1408.76 </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Sq. Ft\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">x<font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\">&nbsp;</font></span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">37) or in the Alternative issue cheques amounting to Rs.38,975.06 i.e. (</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">1053.38Sq.\r\nFt x </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">37)</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">&nbsp;till the termination of the Lease Agreement.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">Direct the Lessee to compensate the Lessor at the present\r\nmarket value of the reduced </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Sq. Ft </span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">area that\r\nis measuring 355.38 </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Sq. Ft less than the Lease Agreement mentioned\r\n1408.76 Sq. Ft, </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">as the same was done in complete\r\nviolation of Section 14 read with Section 18 of the Act.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs. 1,50,000/-\r\non account of mental harassment;</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs.1,00,000/-\r\nas litigation expenses;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Any other\r\ncompensation /Order which the Adjudicating Officer&nbsp; may deem fit in the facts and circumstances\r\nof the present case.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',6397075.00,6242194.00,'2018-03-28 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-03-28 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','ITTC/14/OFFICE - 1401B','','',1,1,0,0,'smann','2018-08-31 12:27:40.000','smann','2018-08-31 12:27:40.000'),(63,1033,'1033',1087,'f0699c79-12ce-4516-a05e-81ed9bb0a3a4','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-08-31 18:03:57.000','Manjit Mann','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426 Phase 10','Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','2426 Phase 10','Mohali',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0007','India Trade Tower','Bhanu Infrabuild Pvt Ltd','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That the present complaint is being filed before\r\nthis Honble Court for violation of inter alia Section 18 read with Section 14 of\r\nthe Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 “<b>Act</b>” read with Rule 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation\r\nand Development) Rules, 2017 “<b>Rules</b>”,\r\nagainst the Respondent Lessee for gross negligence in providing deficient\r\nservices, by fraudulently alluring the Complainant to invest in a bogus Real\r\nEstate Project called “India Trade Tower” as a part of integrated township\r\nProject situated at Omaxe New Chandigarh, District SAS Nagar, Punjab.“<b>The Project</b>”</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><br></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Please see attachment for detailed facts<br></span><br></p>','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">As per\r\nSection 18(1)(a) read with Section 19(4) of the Act, the Promoter is under an\r\nobligation to fulfill his responsibilities in accordance with the terms of the\r\nLease Agreement. As per the Lease Agreement, the Lessee was under an obligation\r\nto allot </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">Allotted </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Commercial Space/Office Space bearing No.\r\nITTC/FOURTEENTH/OFFICE-1401B in Commercial Complex India Trade Tower as part of\r\nintegrated township project “Omaxe New Chandigarh” measuring 1443.37 Sqft or\r\n134.09 Sq.mtr but they have without the consent of the Lessor offered 1080.29\r\nSq. Ft/100.36 Sq. Mtrwhich is in complete violation of Section 14 of the Act.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri\">Direct the Lessee to allot Lessee the Unit as was agreed measuring\r\n1408.76 Sq. Ft or in the Alternative refund the excess amount of Rs. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">5,63,117.31\r\nalongwith interest.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">Direct the Lessee to comply with clause 7.1.2 of the Lease\r\nAgreement and issue cheques amounting to Rs. 53,404.69 i.e.1443.37</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Sq. Ft\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">x37 or in the Alternative issue cheques amounting to\r\nRs.39,970 i.e. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">1080.29Sq. Ft x 37</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">&nbsp;till the termination of the Lease Agreement.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">Direct the Lessee to compensate the Lessor at the present\r\nmarket value of the reduced </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Sq. Ft </span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">area that\r\nis measuring 363.08</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri\">Sq. Ft less than the one mentioned in the\r\nLease Agreement&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">as the same was done in complete\r\nviolation of Section 14 read with Section 18 of the Act.</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs.\r\n1,50,000/- on account of mental harassment;</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs.1,00,000/-\r\nas litigation expenses;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Any other\r\ncompensation /Order which the Adjudicating Officer&nbsp; may deem fit in the facts and circumstances\r\nof the present case.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5607604.00,5489751.00,'2018-03-28 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-07-17 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','ITTC/11/OFFICE 1101B','','',1,1,0,0,'mkmann','2018-08-31 13:08:36.000','mkmann','2018-08-31 13:08:36.000'),(64,1034,'1034',1044,'589d4fee-d68b-42d9-b2e0-ac22cc09f3cb','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-08-31 18:33:02.000','Aman Kumar Sharma','jurisaxisrera@yahoo.com',9729902009,0,0,'D-73,Spangle Condos.','Gazipur,Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','D-73,Spangle Condos.','Gazipur,Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@yahoo.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','Sushma Crescent','Sushma Buildtech Limited','',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area Phase-1, Chandigarh-160002.','',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area Phase-1, Chandigarh-160002.','',6,128,'160002','1','<p>That the Respondent is a Private Limited Company which is duly incorporated under the provisions of the Companies Act, 1956, and is fully responsible for the acts, conduct business and carry on day to day affairs through its Managing Director or Chairman or Directors.\r\n</p><p>\r\nThat the Respondent No. 1 is in the business of  Real Estate Development business, in their usual course of business, purchase the land, enter into joint ventures, enter in collaboration agreement, enters into marketing and development agreements etc. with various stakeholders including but not limited to land owners. Respondent is in the business of development, marketing and sale of the residential and commercial projects.&nbsp;</p><p>\r\nThe “SUSHMA CRESCENT” is a Residential Group Housing Colony Project (the “Project”) being developed by Respondent on a parcel of land admeasuring 26 Bigha 15 Biswa situated in the revenue estate MC Zirakpur, District Mohali, Punjab, (hereinafter referred to as the “Land”).&nbsp;</p><p>That the Complainant relied heavily on the representations, affirmations and commitments made by the Respondent’s staff and representatives and only on their asking has approached the Respondent no.1 for purchase of  flat/apartment in the said Project having an approximate 2380 sq. foot. The complainant had made payment to the tune of INR 6,66,000/- at the time of allotment i.e. till 08/11/2012. The Complainant had been allotted Duplex Apartment no. A-1103 admeasuring 2380 sq. feet super area on 11th Floor in Tower A in the complex vide application form dated 08/11/2012. \r\n</p><p>\r\nThe Respondent also executed an Apartment Buyer Agreement (“ABA”) with instant complainants vide agreement dated 18th  Feb.,2013,  wherein general terms and conditions of allotment were prescribed. The copy of such ABA is annexed herewith as Annexure C-1.&nbsp;</p><p>\r\nIt has been specifically mentioned in para 4.2 of ABA, that the complainant has already paid booking amount (inclusive of service tax) of Rs. 6,66,000/-&nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To give\r\nnecessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu\r\nof unit/apartment till date along with 18 percent interest from the date of\r\nexecution of Builder/Apartment Buyer Agreement till realization as per the\r\nprovisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(RnD)Rules,2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To impose\r\npenalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act\r\nfor willful default committed by them.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To impose\r\npenalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act\r\nfor contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To issue\r\ndirections to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with HRER Rules,2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To recommend\r\ncriminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating,\r\nfraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian\r\nPenal Code.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To issue\r\ndirection to pay the cost of litigation.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To issue\r\ndirection to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his\r\nmental agony, pain and harassment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-left: 1.5in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -1.5in; line-height: 200%;\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Any other\r\nrelief which this Honble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of this complaint.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.5in;mso-text-indent-alt:-.25in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>',6660000.00,6888605.00,'2016-02-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-08-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','A-1103, Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur, Punjab','','',1,1,0,0,'JURISAXIS','2018-08-31 15:16:07.000','JURISAXIS','2018-08-31 15:16:07.000'),(65,1027,'1027',1068,'21687434-1c56-4184-a26c-ec561c2f2dcd','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-08-31 18:03:22.000','Sandeep Mann','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','1','2426, Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0033','Phase-3 development of Mega Residential project\r\n','Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Developers Pvt. Ltd','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor, Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh','',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor, Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh','',28,507,'140901','1','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;That\r\nthe present complaint is being filed before this Hon’ble Court for violation of\r\ninter alia Section 18 read with Section 19(4)of the Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2016 [“<b>Act</b>”] read\r\nwith Rule 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nRules, 2017 [“<b>Rules</b>”], against the\r\nRespondent for gross negligence in providing deficient services, by\r\nfraudulently alluring the Complainant to invest in a bogus Real Estate Project\r\ncalled “Omaxe Chandigarh Extension” [“<b>The\r\nProject</b>”]<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">a.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">The\r\nRespondent be directed to pay the Complainant interest as per Rule 16 of the\r\nPunjab RERA Rules at the marginal cost of lending rate as given by State Bank\r\nof India plus 2 percent forevery month of delayi.e from 6<sup>th</sup> January\r\n2013<a name=\"_GoBack\"></a>on the deposited amount till possession is given for\r\nviolation of Section 18 of the Act.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">b.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">1,50,000/- on account of mental\r\nharassment;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">c.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Rs .1,00,000/- as litigation\r\nexpenses;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">d.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Any other compensation /Order which\r\nthe Adjudicating Officer may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the\r\npresent case.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5396503.00,5266702.00,'2013-06-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-11-03 00:00:00','2011-08-25 00:00:00','OCEA/II/374','','',1,1,0,0,'smann','2018-08-31 15:22:24.000','smann','2018-08-31 15:22:24.000'),(66,1030,'1030',1081,'e4107d19-0392-40e6-9c1c-2bb0a6920e04','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-08-31 18:04:37.000','Rupinder Mannn','smann637@gmail.com',9876766732,0,0,'2426 Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','1','2426 Phase 10','',28,507,'160062','Amitabh Tewari','',9814016469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0033','Phase-3 development of Mega\r\nResidential project','Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Developers Pvt. Ltd','',0,0,'India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','India Trade Tower, First Floor','Madhya Marg Extension, New Chandigarh',28,507,'140901','1','<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">That\r\nthe present complaint is being filed before this Honble Court for violation of\r\ninter alia Section 18 read with Section 19(4) of the Real Estate (Regulation\r\nand Development) Act, 2016 [“<b>Act</b>”]\r\nread with Rule 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nRules, 2017 [“<b>Rules</b>”], against the\r\nRespondentfor gross negligence in providing deficient services, by fraudulently\r\nalluring the Complainant to invest in a bogus Real Estate Project called “Omaxe\r\nChandigarh Extension” [“<b>The Project</b>”]</span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><o:p>Please check attachments for detailed Fact of the case.</o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-left: 72pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\">a. The\r\nRespondent be directed to pay the Complainant interest as per Rule 16 of the\r\nPunjab RERA Rules at the marginal cost of lending rate as given by State Bank\r\nof India plus 2 percent for every monthof </span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\">delayi.e from 6</span><sup style=\"text-indent: -18pt;\">th</sup><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt;\"> January 2013 on\r\nthe deposited amount till possession is given for violation of Section 18 of\r\nthe Act.</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">b.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Rs</span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">.</span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">1,50,000/- on account of mental\r\nharassment;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">c.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Rs .1,00,000/- as litigation\r\nexpenses;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"Normal1\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">d.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Any other compensation /Order which\r\nthe Adjudicating Officer may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the\r\npresent case.</span></p>',5396703.00,4814456.00,'2013-01-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-11-03 00:00:00','2011-08-25 00:00:00','OCEA/II/373 ','','',1,1,0,0,'rmann','2018-08-31 15:23:24.000','rmann','2018-08-31 15:23:24.000'),(67,1031,'1031',1022,'33a0ed60-04ed-4ddd-b47a-6c6e5113bf37','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Nikhil Juneja','nikhil_sp1@yahoo.com',8699499940,0,0,'128, Shakti Nagar','',28,261,'144001','1','128, Shakti Nagar','',28,261,'144001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-JAL33-PM0077','Old Jail Site, Jalandhar','PUNJAB URBAN PLANNING AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA BHAWAN SECTOR- 62','SAS NAGAR MOHAL',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA BHAWAN SECTOR- 62','SAS NAGAR MOHAL',28,507,'160062','1','<p>\r\n		\r\n	\r\n	\r\n		</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n			<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n				<div class=\"column\">\r\n					<p><span style=\"font-size: 11.000000pt; font-family: \'Helvetica\'\">I purchased plot number 65C at Old Jail site, Jalandhar on 22/04/2016 via PUDA auction. On 17/08/2016\r\nI received the allotment letter in which it was mentioned that the possession shall be handed over within 1\r\nyear of the Auction. The possession has been delayed by over 2 years. I was offered possession on\r\n26/06/2018.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n				</div>\r\n			</div>\r\n		</div>','<p>\r\n		\r\n	\r\n	\r\n		</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n			<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n				<div class=\"column\">\r\n					<p><span style=\"font-size: 11.000000pt; font-family: \'Helvetica\'\">PUDA should pay me penalty for delaying the possession @18% PA on the\r\nmonthly compounding basis this interest Because of the delay in giving in the possession I am being forced to pay interest even with out getting\r\npossession. This has put me in significant financial constraints and mental stress. Now they should be\r\npenalised with mental harassment fee of 15 Lakhs.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n				</div>\r\n			</div>\r\n		</div>',11402358.00,11406647.61,'2017-04-22 00:00:00.000','2018-06-26 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-17 00:00:00','2016-04-22 00:00:00','65C Old Jail Site, Jalandhar.','','',2,0,0,0,'nikhil_sp1','2018-08-31 17:56:27.000','nikhil_sp1','2018-08-31 17:56:27.000'),(68,1035,'1035',1088,'80eb346b-56ae-4240-95f2-961ea8ec8fd1','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 12:18:48.000','Jarnail Singh','neerusingla463@gmail.com',9915501161,0,429326009239,'House no. 1161 sector 34.C ','',6,128,'160022','1','House no. 1161 sector 34. C ','',6,128,'160022','Neeru singla ','singlaneeru@rocketmail.com',9876317173,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0003','Janta  land promoters Ltd ','janta land promoters ','',0,0,'sco.no.39-42,sector .82 ','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64 ',28,507,'160055','1','sco.no.39-42,sector .82 ','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64 ',28,507,'160055','1','<p>THE APPLICANT HAD APPLIED FOR THE ALLOTMENT OF A PLOT MEASURING 250.SQ.YARDS IN SECTOR 94 SAS NAGAR MOHALI. THE TOTAL OF WHICH WAS RS. 2500000 AND OUT OF THE TOTAL COST THE APPLICANT HAD PAID A SUM OF RS. 1375000 ON 27.12.2005. THE BRIEF FACTS DOCUMENTS ARE ATTACHED HEREWITH.</p>','<ol><li>TO RETURN BACK THE AMOUNT OF RS. 1375000 PAID BY THE APPLICANT ON 27.12.2005, TO THE RESPONDENT.&nbsp;</li><li>INTEREST AT THE AGREED RATE OF 18% P.A ON THE ABOVE SAID AMOUNT OF 1375000 FROM 27.12.2005 TILL DATE UNDER THE PROVISION OF SECTION 18(3) OF THE RERA ACT.&nbsp;</li><li>AS PER THE PROVISION OF SECTION 18(3) OF THE RERA ACT. COMPENSATION FOR HARASSMENT, MENTAL AGONY AND FOR NON- FULFILLMENT OF THE ALLOTMENT OF RESIDENTIAL PLOT OF 250 SQ. YARDS IN SECTOR 94 SAS NAGAR MOHALI.&nbsp;</li><li>THE APPLICANT IS ALSO ENTITLED FOR COMPENSATION ON ACCOUNT OF UNDUE ENRICHMENT AS TO THE KNOWLEDGE OF THE APPLICANT, THE RESPONDENT HAS SOLD SIMILAR PLOTS AR A MUCH HIGHER RATE.</li><li>LITIGATION EXPENSES TO THE TUNE OF RS. 50,000.&nbsp;</li></ol>',2500000.00,1375000.00,'2005-12-27 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-01-02 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','residential plot of 250.sq.yards mega II in sector 94 Mohali.','','',1,0,0,0,'Neerusingla@12345','2018-09-01 10:58:44.000','Neerusingla@12345','2018-09-01 10:58:44.000'),(69,1036,'1036',1092,'506ad359-88c1-4045-ba35-1eef15c3e32e','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Darshan  Singh','advbswalia@gmail.com',9814685406,1722625103,497110579868,'5405, Sector 38 West ','',6,128,'160014','1','5405, Sector 38 West ','',6,128,'160014','B.S. Walia','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','Punjab Urban Planning and Development authority','PUDA','',0,0,'PUDA  Bhawan , Sector 62 , S.A.S Nagar , Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA  Bhawan , Sector 62 , S.A.S Nagar , Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>That the respondent issued allotment Letter of intent (LOI) to applicant for residential plot  no. 94 measuring 545 Sq. Yard, Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali- 160055 dated 14.1.2016  in reference to application form no. 832. That in furtherance  of letter of Intent , allotment letter&nbsp; dated 9-8-2016 was issued to applicant . The tentative price of the plot is Rs. 11445000/- at the rate of Rs. 21,000/- Rs/Sq. Yard. In pursuance to Allotment Letter, Applicant paid full and final lump sum payment of Rs.1,14,45,000/- .</p><p>Thus, till date Rs. 11445000/- has been paid by Applicant to the respondent as per statement of account. As per the Allotment Letter dated 9.8.2016, the possession of the said plot in question was to be given within 18 months from the date of issuance of allotment which is already over i.e. 8.2.2018 Thus, the respondent has failed to handover possession within the stipulated time as written in the allotment letter agreed between the parties. The respondent has yet to give reply to Applicant whether they have got the Occupancy Certificate/Completion Certificate for the said plot or not? Respondent has been avoiding this question for too long since the Allotment letter was issued. That the said project promoted by respondent lacks basic infrastructure like roads, poor connectivity, drains, electricity, water supply, green cover and parks, street lights missing, roads without berm, no provision of security nor any existence of police post. All these factors further make plot unfit for habitation and construction.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Applicant has given a letter on 30-11-2017\r\nregarding possession of plot no. 94 , Sector 118-119 , Gateway City Mohali. Even today</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">, <span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the development works at the said ‘Gateway\r\nCity’ are not complete, which means the possession of plot is no sooner\r\nexpected than 2019 from respondent. Thus, there is a clear delay on the part of\r\nrespondent.</span></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In\r\nview of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> </span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">prays\r\nfor the following compensation(s):- </span><o:p></o:p></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1 </span></span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant\r\npay 12% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> 11445000</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;letter-spacing:1.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">/-</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">from date of possession .</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> </span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2 Compensation for inability/failure to discharge obligations\r\nas per Allotment Letter and RERA Act under </span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">Section\r\n18 (3)</span></i></b></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> lacking in basic\r\nservices which was initially promised and no disclosure about status of Completion\r\nCertificate/Occupancy Certificate before handing over the possession.</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3\r\nCompensation on account of mental agony, pain and litigation expenses upto Rs.\r\n2 lakh as illustrated in the Section 72 of the RERA Act. </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4 Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may deem\r\nfit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of\r\nApplicant.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>',11445000.00,11445000.00,'2018-02-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','#94, Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'bswalia','2018-09-04 22:19:35.000','bswalia','2018-09-04 22:19:35.000'),(70,1037,'1037',1084,'48ec20f3-4e23-420e-bf04-2d185c7d7017','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-09-06 15:18:30.000','Ambika khullar','julie.23ambika@yahoo.com',9041176988,0,0,'898','phase 7',28,507,'140603','1','898','Phase VII',28,507,'140603','Rachit Kaushal','rkaushal009@gmail.com',9464500306,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','Sushma Crescent','Sushma Buildtech Limited','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, Industrial Area Phase I','',6,128,'160002','1','B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, Industrial Area Phase I','',6,128,'160002','1','<p>﻿1.&nbsp; &nbsp; That Complainant has filed the present complainant before this Hon\'ble Authority ﻿ seeking possession of the allotted unit no C-201, 2nd Floor, Tower C, Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur at a BSP of Rs. 41,38,810/-. The complainant had made payment of the unit on 07.09.2011 and till 16.10.2013 (date of buyers\' agreement C-1), had made a payment of Rs. 21,61,347/-. Between 07.09.2011 and 16.10.2013, no buyers\' agreement was executed between the parties despite the clear mandate of PAPRA Act and other applicable laws despite taking 52% of the payment by the Respondent. Allotment letter was sent to the complainant dated 25.10.2013.</p><p><br></p><p>2.&nbsp; &nbsp; That had the buyers\' agreement been executed in september 2011 itself, as per the agreement, the possession of the unit was to be handed to the complainant by March 2015. However, since the Buyers\' Agreement was executed on 16.10.2013, the possession fell due on 16.04.2017. Offer of Possession was offered vide letter dated 20.03.2018 (C-5) and vide another letter of same date (C-6), an illegal demand of Rs. 5,65,707/- was demanded by the respondents.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>3.&nbsp; &nbsp; That the Complainants had also availed of a loan facility vide loan sanction letter dated 10.10.2013 (C-3) and out of sanctioned loan amount of Rs. 22,52,000/-, complainants have had the bank disburse an amount of Rs. 20,64,443/-. Since 12.11.2013, the complainants are paying a monthly EMI of Rs. 19,196/- per month till date.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4.&nbsp; &nbsp; That the Complainants have paid a total payment of Rs. 47,22,836/- and the only demand of the respondents pertains to the interest on \"delayed payments\" by the complainants.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>5.&nbsp; &nbsp; That since the respondent is claiming undue amounts for giving possession, the complainants are constrained to move this Hon\'ble Authority for getting possession of the unit allotted along with other reliefs as mentioned in the complaint attached herewith.</p>','<p>1. To hand over physical possessionof the unit allotted;</p><p><br></p><p>2. To direct the respondent to waive off the illegal demand of interest (C-9);</p><p><br></p><p>3.&nbsp; &nbsp;To direct the respondent to pay interest for keeping an amount of the complainants for almost two years without executing the Buyers\' Agreement @24% P.A. FROM RESPECTIVE DATES OF DEPOSITS till date of execution of agreement;</p><p><br></p><p>4. To direct the respondent to compensate the complainants for delay in offer of possession @24% P.A interest on the amounts deposited by the complainants till actual physical possession;</p><p><br></p><p>5. To direct the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 5 lacs for mental harassment;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>6. To direct the respondent to pay to the complainant no 1, the amount of rent incurred by her from the date the possession was to fall due had the buyers\' agreement was executed on time;</p><p><br></p><p>7.&nbsp; &nbsp;To grant litigation cost of Rs. 1 lac to the Complainants;</p><p><br></p><p>8. Any other relief as the Authority deems appropriate.</p>',4138810.00,4722836.00,'2017-04-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-10-25 00:00:00','2013-10-16 00:00:00','flat no 201, 2nd Floor, Tower C, Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur','','',1,1,0,0,'RKA99','2018-09-05 19:37:09.000','RKA99','2018-09-05 19:37:09.000'),(71,1038,'1038',1088,'80eb346b-56ae-4240-95f2-961ea8ec8fd1','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jarnail Singh','neerusingla463@gmail.com',9915501161,0,429326009254,'House no. 1161 sector 34.C ','',6,128,'160022','1','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64','',28,39,'160055','Neeru singla ','',9876317173,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD ','janta land promoters ','',0,0,'sco.no.39-42,sector .82','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64',28,507,'160055','1','sco.no.39-42,sector .82','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64',28,507,'160055','1','<ol><li>THE APPLICANT HAD APPLIED FOR THE ALLOTMENT OF A INDUSTRIAL PLOT MEASURING 500 SQ. YARDS IN SECTOR 82 SAS NAGAR MOHALI. THE TOTAL OF WHICH WAS RS. 6000000 AND OUT OF THE TOTAL COST THE APPLICANT HAD PAID A SUM OF RS. 4500000. THE DOCUMENTS ARE ATTACHED HEREWITH.</li></ol>','<ol><li>INTEREST AT THE ATE OF 18 %</li><li>COMPENSATION FOR HARASSMENT, MENTAL AGONY</li><li>UNDUE ENRICHMENT</li><li>LITIGATION EXPENSES&nbsp;</li></ol>',6000000.00,4500000.00,'2011-01-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-04-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','industrial plot of 500 sq. yards in sector 82 mohali. ','','',2,0,0,0,'Neerusingla@12345','2018-09-06 12:42:21.000','Neerusingla@12345','2018-09-06 12:42:21.000'),(72,1038,'1038',1088,'80eb346b-56ae-4240-95f2-961ea8ec8fd1','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 12:19:03.000','Jarnail Singh','neerusingla463@gmail.com',9915501161,0,429326009254,'House no. 1161 sector 34.C ','',6,128,'160022','1','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64','',28,507,'160055','Neeru singla ','',9876317173,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD ','janta land promoters ','',0,0,'sco.no.39-42,sector .82','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64',28,507,'160055','1','sco.no.39-42,sector .82','SCO.NO.538 PHASE 10 SECTOR 64',28,507,'160055','1','<ol><li>THE APPLICANT HAD APPLIED FOR THE ALLOTMENT OF A INDUSTRIAL PLOT MEASURING 500 SQ. YARDS IN SECTOR 82 SAS NAGAR MOHALI. THE TOTAL OF WHICH WAS RS. 6000000 AND OUT OF THE TOTAL COST THE APPLICANT HAD PAID A SUM OF RS. 4500000. THE DOCUMENTS ARE ATTACHED HEREWITH.</li></ol>','<ol><li>INTEREST AT THE ATE OF 18 %</li><li>COMPENSATION FOR HARASSMENT, MENTAL AGONY</li><li>UNDUE ENRICHMENT</li><li>LITIGATION EXPENSES&nbsp;</li></ol>',6000000.00,4500000.00,'2011-01-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-04-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','industrial plot of 500 sq. yards in sector 82 mohali. ','','',1,0,0,0,'Neerusingla@12345','2018-09-06 12:51:37.000','Neerusingla@12345','2018-09-06 12:51:37.000'),(73,1039,'1039',1089,'f089a27c-f769-417d-ad07-bc3896fb8d9c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-09-08 09:44:37.000','Rattan  Chand','sourav1003@gmail.com',9417427188,0,0,'H. No 1007  Sector 35 B Chandigarh','',6,128,'160022','1','H. No 1007  Sector 35 B Chandigarh','',6,128,'160022','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0253','Bajwa Developers Ltd.','Bajwa Developers Ltd','',0,0,'SCO 17-18, Ludhiana - Chandigarh State Highway, ','Sector 125, Sunny Enclave, Kharar, ',28,507,'140301','1','SCO 17-18, Ludhiana - Chandigarh State Highway, ','Sector 125, Sunny Enclave, Kharar, ',28,507,'140301','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 7pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;My wife Rakesh Lata had\r\npurchased Plot No. 1008 (measuring 0-5 Marla (150 sq yds) from Khewat Nos.\r\n5/5,6,7 &amp; 55/1, khasra no 25/16/1/2 etc. out of 68 kanal, 17 marlas of\r\nvillage Harlalpur, no. 181 tehsil Kharar and Distt SAS Nagar, Mohali which is\r\nsituated in Sunny Enclave) from M/s Balwa Developers Limited. A sale deed No.\r\n3608 dated 16.09.2013 was registered in the office of the Sub Registrar, Kharar\r\nin the presence of Sub-Registrar, Kharar.&nbsp;An&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\">amended Sale Deed of Plot No. 929 area 0-5 Marlas (152.72 sq\r\nyds) in lieu of earlier transavtions dated 10.06.2016 bearing Serial No 2260\r\nwas made by Sh. Ankit Sidana s/o Sh Dinesh Sidana authorised authority of Bajwa\r\nDevelopers. This amended deed was registered in lieu of old Plot No 1008 in\r\nwhich the full and final payment was made to the M/s Bajwa Developers. So, the\r\nPlot no. 929 was given against the old Plot via showing that seller have\r\nreceived all of the consideration amount (Rs 24,75,000/-) of the present\r\nplot.The authorised signatory of M/s Bajwa Developers had offered possession to\r\nPlot no 929 size 152.72 sq yds in Sec 124, Global City Distt. SAS Nagar, Mohali\r\non 09.03.2017 through his letter and stated that they are giving possession of\r\nthis Plot after six months.</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 7pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\">Smt. Rakesh Lata have several times approached M/s Bajwa\r\nDevelopers and concerned persons for handing over the possession of Plot No.\r\n929, Sector 124 in their office Desu Majra, SCO 17-18, Sunny Enclave, Kharar\r\nand they have failed to hand over the possession of the said plot. On\r\n21.12.2017, my wife Rakesh Lata was expired after shock of not getting the\r\npossession of her plot after 5 years. T</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-family: &quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\">he total amount of Rs 27,50,000(Including registration &amp; without loan interest) from my hard earned money is received by the developers and plot was\r\nnot given in lieu of said consideration. We have also got transferred the\r\nownership of this plot in revenue record and the same is stand in my name\r\nRattan Chand and my two sons Gaurav Sharma and Sourav.</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify\">It is\r\ntherefore requested that necessary directions for giving possession of Plot no.\r\n929 measuring 152.72 sq yds, Global City, Sector 124, Tehsil Kharar, Distt.\r\nMohali shall be given to M/s Bajwa Developers Limited, Sunny Enclave, SCO\r\n17-18, Desu Majra and a complaint against this developer may be accepted for\r\nnot giving possession of the Plot in question and causing death of my wife Smt\r\nRakesh Lata.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify\">We have also took a Loan against this property and are paying it since Dec\'2013. We want to get our all our Interest till date.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify\">Also because of this forgery my Wife went into complete shock and died on 21/12/2017 we want mental trauma compensation.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify\"><br></p>',2450000.00,2750000.00,'2017-09-09 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-12-28 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1008 Sector 124 SAS Nagar & 929 Sector 124 SAS Nagar Global City.','','',1,1,0,0,'sourav1003','2018-09-07 14:22:37.000','sourav1003','2018-09-07 14:22:37.000'),(74,1025,'1025',1074,'173c8217-5ec2-4b34-b6c8-f76219a18b97','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','gurkirat bajwa','gbajwa9@rediffmail.com',9814031105,1612455111,762822836892,'220 -A','sarabha nagar',28,366,'141001','1','220 -A','sarabha nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0004','Ireo Waterfront ludhiana','M/S ireo Waterfront Ludhiana','iwp@ireo.in',9810237279,1613040290,'5, Dhanraj Chambers,','satbari',10,557,'110074','1','5, Dhanraj Chambers,','satbari',10,557,'110074','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">1.        That you had entered into contract dated 27/06/2014 with us (gurkirat singh bajwa &amp; navjot kaur) for the sale of House/Villa No.L-550 of Type-L, having built up area of 1600 Sq. Ft. over the plot measuring 249.96 Sq. Yds. after construction&nbsp; and furnishing as per specifications mentioned in the contract in 24 months.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">2.        That the total sale consideration of the villa was Rs.1,06,84,207/-. Out of which 25% was to be paid as earnest money and remaining amount was to be paid at the time of delivery of possession. WE&nbsp; have deposited with you Rs.33,56,212/- and Rs.1,23,596/- as club membership charges against receipts.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">3.        That it was agreed by you in the contract that the construction shall be completed and possession will be given within 24 months from the date of execution of the contract. Therefore, you had promised to complete the construction and furnish the villa within 24 months. It was also agreed by you that after completion of the villa you will serve the completion notice on us within this period. In the contract it was also provided that you could avail six months more to complete the construction as a grace period if the delay was beyond the control of the company. Therefore, the company was bound to complete the construction and deliver possession to us before 27/12/2017 by all means.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">4.        That it was agreed by you in the contract that in case you fail to deliver possession&nbsp; within the period mentioned above the company will pay compensation @ Rs.7.50 per sq. Ft. of built up area. It was also agreed therein that my clients shall be entitled to terminate the contract and get refund in case of failure on your part to perform the contract in specified time.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">5.        That we already have apprised you many times our necessity for the house/villa and requested you to complete the construction and deliver possession in time as agreed. But you have not completed the construction till date.</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 28px;\">You</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">had also agreed to furnish and develop parks and club etc. in the colony and provide all amenities in and for the use of villa within agreed time. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Now that we have exhausted all efforts to get the villa completed and to get possession from the company within given time, there is no other option </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1)except to terminate the contract and </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">2)get back the refund with interest.&nbsp; Refund of money paid to you with interest @ 12 PA from the date of payment.</span></p>',10684207.00,3489808.00,'2016-06-26 00:00:00.000','2016-06-26 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-27 00:00:00','2014-06-27 00:00:00','L-550 of Type-L,','','',2,0,0,0,'gurkirasinghbajwanavjotkaurbajwa','2018-09-07 14:46:45.000','gurkirasinghbajwanavjotkaurbajwa','2018-09-07 14:46:45.000'),(75,1025,'1025',1074,'173c8217-5ec2-4b34-b6c8-f76219a18b97','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','gurkirat bajwa','gbajwa9@rediffmail.com',9814031105,1612455111,762822836892,'220 -A','sarabha nagar',28,366,'141001','1','220 -A','sarabha nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0004','IREO Water\r\nFront, Pocket-2\r\n(Phase-I)','M/S ireo Waterfront Ludhiana','iwp@ireo.in',9810237279,1613040290,'5, Dhanraj Chambers,','satbari',10,557,'110074','1','5, Dhanraj Chambers,','satbari',10,557,'110074','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">1.        That you had entered into contract dated 27/06/2014 with us (gurkirat singh bajwa &amp; navjot kaur) for the sale of House/Villa No.L-550 of Type-L, having built up area of 1600 Sq. Ft. over the plot measuring 249.96 Sq. Yds. after construction&nbsp; and furnishing as per specifications mentioned in the contract in 24 months.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">2.        That the total sale consideration of the villa was Rs.1,06,84,207/-. Out of which 25% was to be paid as earnest money and remaining amount was to be paid at the time of delivery of possession. WE&nbsp; have deposited with you Rs.33,56,212/- and Rs.1,23,596/- as club membership charges against receipts.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">3.        That it was agreed by you in the contract that the construction shall be completed and possession will be given within 24 months from the date of execution of the contract. Therefore, you had promised to complete the construction and furnish the villa within 24 months. It was also agreed by you that after completion of the villa you will serve the completion notice on us within this period. In the contract it was also provided that you could avail six months more to complete the construction as a grace period if the delay was beyond the control of the company. Therefore, the company was bound to complete the construction and deliver possession to us before 27/12/2017 by all means.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">4.        That it was agreed by you in the contract that in case you fail to deliver possession&nbsp; within the period mentioned above the company will pay compensation @ Rs.7.50 per sq. Ft. of built up area. It was also agreed therein that my clients shall be entitled to terminate the contract and get refund in case of failure on your part to perform the contract in specified time.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">5.        That we already have apprised you many times our necessity for the house/villa and requested you to complete the construction and deliver possession in time as agreed. But you have not completed the construction till date.</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 28px;\">You</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">had also agreed to furnish and develop parks and club etc. in the colony and provide all amenities in and for the use of villa within agreed time. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Now that we have exhausted all efforts to get the villa completed and to get possession from the company within given time, there is no other option </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1)except to terminate the contract and </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">2)get back the refund with interest.&nbsp; Refund of money paid to you with interest @ 12 PA from the date of payment.</span></p>',10684207.00,3489808.00,'2016-06-26 00:00:00.000','2016-06-26 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-27 00:00:00','2014-06-27 00:00:00','L-550 of Type-L,','','',2,0,0,0,'gurkirasinghbajwanavjotkaurbajwa','2018-09-07 14:48:30.000','gurkirasinghbajwanavjotkaurbajwa','2018-09-07 14:48:30.000'),(76,1025,'1025',1074,'173c8217-5ec2-4b34-b6c8-f76219a18b97','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','gurkirat bajwa','gbajwa9@rediffmail.com',9814031105,1612455111,762822836892,'220 -A','sarabha nagar',28,366,'141001','1','220 -A','sarabha nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0004','IREO Water\r\nFront, Pocket-2\r\n(Phase-I)','M/S ireo Waterfront Ludhiana','iwp@ireo.in',9810237279,1613040290,'5, Dhanraj Chambers,','satbari',10,557,'110074','1','5, Dhanraj Chambers,','satbari',10,557,'110074','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">1.	You had entered into contract dated 27/06/2014 with Navjot kaur and Gurkirat Singh Bajwa for the sale of House/Villa No.L-550 of Type-L, having built up area of 1600 Sq. Ft. over the plot measuring 249.96 Sq. Yds. after construction and furnishing as per the contract.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">2.	 That the total sale consideration of the villa was Rs.106,842,07/-. Out of which 25% was to be paid as earnest money and remaining amount was to be paid at the time of delivery of possession. We  have deposited with you Rs.33,56,262/- and Rs.1,23,596/- as membership charges of  Angsana club and spa, ireo waterfront  against receipts.&nbsp;\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">3.	That it was agreed by you in the contract that the construction shall be completed and possession will be given within 24 mth from the date of the contract. It was also agreed by you that after completion of the villa you will serve the completion notice  within this period. Even after availing 6 mth more grace period the company was bound to complete the construction and deliver possession to us  before 27/06/2016 by all means.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%; margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; padding: 10px 0px; text-align: justify; line-height: 22px; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><s