ndent also did not take appropriate steps to complete the project and hand over the unit within a stipulated period. As a result over a period of time the project lost its sheen and trust over the investors. It was early this year, when the complainant visited the project and found no one to give a concrete answer in terms of the delay of the project, not only this, the material applied in the unit is of sub-standard quality and not upto mark. The complainant then decided to withdraw his and his father\'s hard earned money from the project and hence the present complaint is being filed. That great prejudice has been caused to the complainant, not only in terms of Interest on money Invested, but in terms of&nbsp; Return on Investment for period of last ten years till date.&nbsp;</p>','<p>That the complainant prays for refund of the amount with interest @18% from the date of deposit till realisation along with additional compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- (Rs.Ten Lakhs), and litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 55000/- (Rs. Fifty Five Thousand) and any other relief which this Ho\'nble Court deems fit for the complainant as per the facts of the complaint stated therein. That the complainant is seeking the refund till date, not only prejudice has been caused to the complainant in terms of the interest on the Investment, if it would have been invested somewhere else, where it would have fetched a handsome amount, but also a handsome Return on Investment, which is blocked with the respondent company for the last Ten Years, as it seems that no Law is applicable on such type of respondents, who not only make lame excuses, but also try to keep their investors in dark, meaning thereby it seems that the investors have not only made a wrong decision in terms of investment, but also have been cheated on account of negligence and deficiency in service on part of the respondent.<br><br></p>',5118516.00,4840807.00,'2011-01-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-01-31 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','H1-F09-903, Tower H, The Views,  Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar Mohali - 140306.\r\n','','',1,1,0,0,'GILL.Harpreet2809','2018-09-28 20:31:54.000','GILL.Harpreet2809','2018-09-28 20:31:54.000'),(98,1050,'1050',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-10 16:54:14.000','Amarjit Kaur','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','1','House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','THE PALM','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,0,'SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n106%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That\r\nthe husband of the applicant initially booked four plots with the respondent\r\nhaving different sizes, two of them measuring 500 Square yards each @ Rs. 18,500/-\r\nin the project “Palm Garden” and two of them measuring 250 Square Yards each @ Rs.\r\n18,000 per Sq. yard in the project “Palm Spring”, Mullanpur (New Chandigarh),\r\nnear Chandigarh being developed by the respondent.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">The booking amount against the plots was directly paid to\r\nthe company by the applicant. Before purchasing these plots, the applicant\r\ncontacted the respondent who assured them that it was having all the approvals\r\nand sanctions for the said project and possession of the plot will be delivered\r\nwithin 2 years.&nbsp; It was assured to the\r\napplicant that the possession of the plots will be delivered within 2 years and\r\nthe buyer’s agreement will be executed within 3-4 months.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">That thereafter the husband of the applicant visited the\r\nproject site in the month of June, 2013 and was shocked to see that only open\r\nfields were there and the respondent had not started any development. On the\r\nsame day the applicant visited the office of respondent who assured the\r\napplicant that development will be started soon and the further payment would\r\nbe demanded when the development work would be started.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That\r\nthereafter the husband of the applicant died in September, 2016 and the Plots\r\nwere transferred in the name of applicant.&nbsp;</span><b style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Century Gothic&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">That the applicant after the death of her husband, visited\r\nthe site of the project and saw no development at the site and asked the\r\nrespondent to refund the amount but respondents showed their inability to\r\nrefund the amount and persuaded the applicant that she should get the deposited\r\namount adjusted into a single plot.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That\r\nthereafter, the amount of the applicant was adjusted against the one plot and\r\nPlot no. 418 measuring 402.32 Sq. yds. (Approx.) was allotted to the applicant\r\non 24.05.2018. That the respondent thereafter in June, 2018 offered Plot Buyer’s Agreement for execution.</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Refund of principle amount i.e. Rs. 95,62,500/- along with compound\r\ninterest @ 10 % P.A. (as per Rule 16 of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation\r\nand Development) Rules, 2017) from the date of respective deposits along with\r\ncompensation of Rs. 10 lacs relying upon the provision of Section 18 of Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>',8472457.00,9562500.00,'2014-02-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-05-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','418','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2018-09-29 10:43:11.000','BeeG','2018-09-29 10:43:11.000'),(99,1051,'1051',1133,'6c60c5a1-9072-497b-9240-435da1d8fb69','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-04 10:27:59.000','Harpreet Singh Gill','gill.harpreet2809@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 65,  sector 05,','Chandigarh',6,128,'160015','1','H.No. 65,  sector 05,','Chandigarh',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','The View, Mohali Hills,  Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.','Through Rajesh Gupta, Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Mohali.','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1725076144,'Emaar MGF Land Limited, Off. No. 40,  ','Central Plaza,  SAS Nagar Mohali.',28,507,'140603','1','Emaar MGF Land Limited, Off. No. 40,  ','Central Plaza,  SAS Nagar Mohali.',28,39,'140603','1','<p class=\"p\" style=\"margin-top:0.0000pt;margin-right:0.0000pt;margin-bottom:7.5000pt;margin-left:0.0000pt;text-indent:0.0000pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan;\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt;\">That the above said unit was purchased by the father of the complaint namely Sh. S.S.Gill and the complainant himself in the year January, 2008. That the complainant being NRI, invested in this project, keeping in view the goodwill of the company.&nbsp; The complainant and his father paid 95% of the consideration&nbsp; the tune of Rs. 4840807/- (Fourty Eight Lakhs Fourty Thousand Eight Hundred and Seven Rupees only) as down payment . The total consideration was Rs. 5118516/- (Fifty one Lakh Eighteen Thousand Five Hundred and Sixteen only). That thereafter a provisional allotment dated 31-01-2008 was issued by the respondent company and soon after and agreement dated 28-02-2008 was executed through the authorized signatory. That the agreement, as per clause 21, clearly stated about the possession of the unit. that the father of the complainant, who was of an old age, died in April, 2012, but till then the company was not able to hand over the physical possession of the unit as per the terms and conditions envisaged in the agreement.</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"p\" style=\"margin-top:0.0000pt;margin-right:0.0000pt;margin-bottom:7.5000pt;margin-left:0.0000pt;text-indent:0.0000pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan;\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; The complainant&nbsp;&nbsp;as and when visited to India. used to visit the project and always found that no work is being carried out qua the unit. The respondent also did not take appropriate steps to complete the project and hand over the unit within a stipulated period. As a result over a period of time the project lost its sheen and trust over the investors. It was early this year, when the complainant visited the project and found no one to give a concrete answer in terms of the delay of the project, not only this, the material applied in the unit is of sub-standard quality and not upto mark. The complainant then decided to withdraw his and his father\'s hard earned money from the project and hence the present complaint is being filed. That great prejudice has been caused to the complainant, not only in terms of Interest on money Invested, but in terms of&nbsp; Return on Investment for period of last ten years till date.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant prays for refund of the amount with interest @18% from the date of deposit till realisation along with additional compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- (Rs.Ten Lakhs), and litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 55000/- (Rs. Fifty Five Thousand) and any other relief which this Ho\'nble Court deems fit for the complainant as per the facts of the complaint stated therein. That the complainant is seeking the refund till date, not only prejudice has been caused to the complainant in terms of the interest on the Investment, if it would have been invested somewhere else, where it would have fetched a handsome amount, but also a handsome Return on Investment, which is blocked with the respondent company for the last Ten Years, as it seems that no Law is applicable on such type of respondents, who not only make lame excuses, but also try to keep their investors in dark, meaning thereby it seems that the investors have not only made a wrong decision in terms of investment, but also have been cheated on account of negligence and deficiency in service on part of the respondent.</span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:SimSun;mso-bidi-font-family:\'Times New Roman\';\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',5118516.00,4840807.00,'2011-01-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-01-31 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','J1-F10-1004, The View, Mohali Hills, SAS Nagar Mohali.\r\n','','',1,1,0,0,'gill.harpreet0110','2018-10-01 18:57:22.000','gill.harpreet0110','2018-10-01 18:57:22.000'),(100,1052,'1052',1134,'328afdd9-165f-49cb-902f-d1c957789d9f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-01 20:07:25.000','Barjinder Paul Singh Gill','gill.harpreet2809@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 65','Sector 05',6,128,'160015','1','H.No