EMAAR MGF Land Ltd.','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Office No. 40','Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'160062','1','Office No. 40','Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'160062','1','<p>That the respondent floated a scheme in the year 2008 to sell built up villas on a plot size 400 sq. Yrds. In sector 109, Mohali at Mohali Hills.The above said Villa Number 131, Augusta Park was purchased by Four allottees namely Sh. Swaran Singh Gill (Father) and his 3 sons namely Harpreet Singh Gill, Dalbir Singh Gill and Sh. Barjinderpaul Singh Gill. The Applicants at that time paid Rs. 15222198/- (Rs. One Crore Fifty Two Lakhs Twenty Two Thousand and One Hundred Ninety Eight only) against a total sale price of Rs. 16073472/- (Rs. One Crore Sixty Lakhs Seventy Three Thousand Four Hundered and Seventy Two only). That the complainants being NRIs, invested in this project, keeping in view the goodwill of the company.&nbsp;  This villa was a preferential location. That an allotment of the said villa was issued on 07-May-2008, but an agreement through the authorized signatory was executed on 04-Jan-2008. That the agreement, as per clause 08 on page number 04 of the agreement, clearly stated about the possession of the unit. that the father of the complainant, who was of an old age, died in April, 2012, but till then the company was not able to hand over the physical possession of the villa as per the terms and conditions envisaged in the agreement.\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The complainants&nbsp;&nbsp;as and when visited to India. used to visit the project and always found that no work is being carried out qua the villa. The respondent also did not take appropriate steps to complete the project and hand over the unit within a stipulated period. As a result, over a period of time the project lost its sheen and trust over the investors. It was early this year, when the complainants visited the project and found no one to give a concrete answer in terms of the delay of the project, not only this, the material applied in the villa is of sub-standard quality and not upto mark. The complainants then decided to withdraw their hard earned money from the project and hence the present complaint&nbsp;</p>','<p>compensation</p>',16073472.00,15222198.00,'2011-01-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-05-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Villa No 131, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills, Sector 109','','',2,0,0,0,'harpreetvarun.gill','2018-10-05 11:22:14.000','harpreetvarun.gill','2018-10-05 11:22:14.000'),(110,1053,'1053',1139,'a2526d36-a2b2-49be-8bb6-f70a1dcdfb83','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-06 08:56:09.000','Harpreet Singh Gill','gill.harpreet2809@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 65','Sector 05, Chandigarh',6,128,'160015','1','H.No. 65','Sector 05, Chandigarh',6,128,'160015','Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','Mohali Hills','Rajesh Gupta, Manager, EMAAR MGF Land Ltd.','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Office No. 40','Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'160062','1','Office No. 40','Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'160062','1','<p>That the respondent floated a scheme in the year 2008 to sell built up villas on a plot size 400 sq. Yrds. In sector 109, Mohali at Mohali Hills.The above said Villa Number 131, Augusta Park was purchased by Four allottees namely Sh. Swaran Singh Gill (Father) and his 3 sons namely Harpreet Singh Gill, Dalbir Singh Gill and Sh. Barjinderpaul Singh Gill. The Applicants at that time paid Rs. 15222198/- (Rs. One Crore Fifty Two Lakhs Twenty Two Thousand and One Hundred Ninety Eight only) against a total sale price of Rs. 16073472/- (Rs. One Crore Sixty Lakhs Seventy Three Thousand Four Hundered and Seventy Two only). That the complainants being NRIs, invested in this project, keeping in view the goodwill of the company.&nbsp;  This villa was a preferential location. That an allotment of the said villa was issued on 07-May-2008, but an agreement through the authorized signatory was executed on 04-Jan-2008. That the agreement, as per clause 08 on page number 04 of the agreement, clearly stated about the possession of the unit. that the father of the complainant, who was of an old age, died in April, 2012, but till then the company was not able to hand over the physical possession of the villa as per the terms and conditions envisaged in the agreement.\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The complainants&nbsp;&nbsp;as and when visited to India. used to visit the project and always found that no work is being carried out qua the villa. The respondent also did not take appropriate steps to complete the project and hand over the unit within a stipulated period. As a result, over a period of time the project lost its sheen and trust over the investors. It was early this year, when the complainants visited the project and found no one to give a concrete answer in terms of the delay of the project, not only this, the material applied in the villa is of sub-standard quality and not upto mark. The complainants then decided to withdraw their hard earned money from the project and hence the present complaint&nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">s</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> pray\r\nfor refund of the amount with interest at 18</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> percent\r\nfrom the date of deposit till reali</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">z</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">ation along with additional\r\ncompensation of Rs. 2</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">0,00,000\r\n- Rs.T</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">w</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">en</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">ty</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> Lakhs,\r\nand litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 55000</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">-Rs.\r\nFifty Five Thousand and any other relief which this Honble Court deems fit for\r\nthe complainant</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">s</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> as\r\nper the facts of the complaint stated therein. That the complainant</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">s</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> are</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> seeking the refund till date, not\r\nonly prejudice has been caused to the complainant</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">s</span><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"> in terms of the interest on the\r\nInvestment, if it would have been invested somewhere else, where it would have\r\nfetched a handsome amount, but also a handsome Return on Investment, which is\r\nblocked with the respondent company for the last Ten Years, as it seems that no\r\nLaw is applicable on such type of respondents, who not only make lame excuses,\r\nbut also try to keep their investors in dark, meaning thereby it seems that the\r\ninvestors have not only made a wrong decision in terms of investment, but also\r\nhave been cheated on account of negligence and deficiency in service on part of\r\nthe respondent.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',16073472.00,15222198.00,'2011-01-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-05-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Villa No 131, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills, Sector 109','','',1,0,0,0,'harpreetvarun.gill','2018-10-05 11:43:32.000','harpreetvarun.gill','2018-10-05 11:43:32.000'),(111,1054,'1054',1146,'7dfad30e-4afa-4859-8a26-94b85edcd0f5','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ashish kumar jain','sandeepjain.ambala@gmail.com',9815695783,0,495798240541,'5368-C, Nicholson Road,','Punjabi Mohalla, Ambala Cantt.',13,1,'133001','1','5368-C, Nicholson Road,','Punjabi Mohalla, Ambala Cantt.',13,1,'133001','Jarnail Singh Thakur, Advocate','jarnailthakur@yahoo.com',9815695783,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','fashion technology park formerly jade business park of chandigarh overseas pvt. ltd..','chandigarh overseas pvt. ltd','jbp@90.in',0,0,'sco 196-197, top floor, sector 34-A chandigarh through its Managing Director','',6,128,'160022','0','sco 196-197, top floor, sector 34-A chandigarh through its Managing Director','',6,128,'160022','1','The Respondents publicised a project known as Fashion Technology Park in sector 90 Mohali. The complainant booked 4 units of 100 sq ft and paid Rs.19.00 lacs of the total price of 20.00 lacs. Possession was to be given by 31.03.2009 which was never given. The complainant was offered buy back option vide letters dated 02.09.2006 and 22.06.2009, whereby they confirmed that the buy back option @Rs.7.5 lac has been offered and accepted by the respondents. They paid Rs.7.5 lac towards buy back of one unit only, but thereafter the respondents neither paid the buy back amount of Rs.22.50 lac for the remaining 3 units nor did they offer possession. They had also promised to pay Rs.50/- per sq ft per month which they paid only once on 31.03.2010 vide cheque for Rs.48388/- and nothing thereafter. It is reported that they have sold the project to some other party. The other respondents are Managing Director Sagar Setia and Director Tejinder Setia. The details are contained in the attached annexures as follows:. Annexures C-1 &nbsp;is information memorandum for small investors, &nbsp;C-2, booking amount receipt, C-3 frequently asked questions, C-4 (colly.) remaining amount receipts, C-5 developer buyer agreement, C-6 lease agreement, C-7 buy back letter dt 2.9.2006 , C-8 buy back letter dt 13.1.2010, C-9, respondents\' letter dt 29.6.2010 on project update, C-10, &nbsp;letter dt 20.2.2010 regarding payment for delay, C-11 power of attorney by complainant favouring sandeep jain and C-12, vakaltnama .&nbsp;','<p>1 the Hon\'ble Authority may please direct the respondents to pay Rs. 22.50 lac towards buyback of 3 units @ Rs.7.5 lac per unit and in terms of section 18 of the RERA Act, and&nbsp;</p><p>2. to pay &nbsp;Interest @ 18% p.a. since the date of payment till actual payment and&nbsp;</p><p>3. for &nbsp;Payment of Rs.50/- per sq ft per month for the delay and&nbsp;</p><p>4. to pay &nbsp;Rs. 10.00 lac as compensation for causing harassment, mental agony caused to the complainant.</p><p>.5. Or any other order in favour of complainant as This Hon\'ble Authority deems fit &nbsp;may please be passed in the interest of justice.</p><p>6. interim order to direct the respondents not to cancel, transfer, mortgage assign , sell, alienate the 4 units allotted to the complainant in design studio no. 6 in the project.</p>',2000000.00,1900000.00,'2009-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2006-12-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','design studio no. 6 containing 4 units of 100 sq ft each','','',1,0,0,0,'jarnailthakur','2018-10-09 13:47:59.000','jarnailthakur','2018-10-09 13:47:59.000'),(112,1008,'1008',1001,'abcbc615-56f0-487c-bd5a-d97762a711d4','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Iqbal Singh testdata','iqbalme@gmail.com',1212121212,0,