lass=\"m_5142867886888198341gmail-li1\" style=\"margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">Mental agony/Legal Fee\'s: We haver&nbsp;suffered severe mental agony and harassment and further had to incur the litigation expenses to pursue the present complaint. Therefore we&nbsp;are entitled to recover compensation to the tune of Rs.5,00,000/- towards mental agony and litigation expenses.</li><li class=\"m_5142867886888198341gmail-li1\" style=\"margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">Contractual Provision: As per Clause 6.3 of Buyer seller agreement i.e&nbsp; Rs 5 per month/per square feet of the Super Built-up Area (2400sqft.)</li></ol>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',2,0,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-10-15 17:01:00.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-10-15 17:01:00.000'),(121,1040,'1040',1094,'5307214d-513f-428e-a103-9ead98ac25bf','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-08 19:35:05.000','Karnail Singh Brar through Tejwant Singh','londonksreracomplainant@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'Village Jawahar Singh Wala','Teh. Nihal Singh Wala',28,393,'142055','1','Tejwant Singh, R/o H.No. 2619, Sector 70,','Sector 70, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'160071','ADv. Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','The Views, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.','M/s Emaar MGF Land Ltd through MD/Director/representative Sh. Rajesh Gupta ','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Limited, ECE House, ','28, Kasturba Gandhi Marg, New Delhi.',10,429,'110001','0','Emaar MGF Land Limited,','SCO 120-122, Sector 17 C, Chandigarh.',6,128,'160017','1','<ol><li>That the complainant/applicant had purchased unit no. H2-GF-GF02,&nbsp; \"THE VIEWS\", Mohali Hills, SAS Nagar Mohaliin the year March, 2008 and had paid a sum of Rs. 4005708/- in advance as an earnest money out of the total consideration amount of rs 4447059/-.</li><li>that M/s Emaar MGF had assured the complainant/applicant to deliver the possession of the said property on or before March,2011.</li><li>that in the agreement executed between the complainant/applicant and the defendant/respondent itself shows that the possession was to be delivered within 36 months of the date of agreement/allottment of the unit purchased.</li><li>that the defendant/respondent had failed to honor its commitment of giving possession to the purchaser till date, despite of the fact that the applicant/complainant purchaser had paid the agreed amount well in advance. Therefore&nbsp; the defendant/respondent developer has failed to honor his side of commitment.</li></ol>','<ol><li>That the defendant/respondent shall be ordered to pay the refund of the amount paid by the complainant/applicant to the defendant/respondent with penal interest @18% from the date of amounts paid respectively.</li><li>That the defendant/respondent be ordered to pay an amount of Rs. 1000000/- as compensation for the harassment caused to complainant/applicant, and any other appropriate relief that this Honorable Court deems fit to be paid by the defendant/respondent to the complainant/applicant.</li></ol>',4579400.00,4005706.00,'2011-05-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-04-01 00:00:00','2008-05-29 00:00:00','H2-GF-GF02, The Views. Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.\r\n','','',1,0,0,0,'london.ksrera','2018-10-15 20:24:17.000','london.ksrera','2018-10-15 20:24:17.000'),(122,1058,'1058',1158,'0c27aca9-8cc5-4938-a0f5-138a7568230c','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Naveen  Walia','vdharmani@gmail.com',9780041313,0,0,'R/O 24 Milk ','Milk (Part)(307)',13,1,'134203','1','534','Sector-10-D',6,128,'160011','Vipul Dharmani','vdharmani@gmail.com',9780041313,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0292','Palm Heights Private Limited','Harjinder Singh Rangi','mkdattachd74@mail.com',0,0,'HAIBATPUR ROAD, OPP. HANSA TUBES','TEH. DERA BASSI,',28,507,'140507','1','HAIBATPUR ROAD, OPP. HANSA TUBES','TEH. DERA BASSI,',28,507,'140507','1','<p>T<font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">he Complainant purchased the residential flat with Developer and the same was booked in 2016 wherein the possession was to be handed over in August 2016. However, the Complainant approached the promoter many times to seek information with regard to the\r\nprogress in construction and handing over of the possession of the said flat as\r\nthe work at the site had not started and moreover the\r\nentire construction work of the project has been stopped. In spite of the promise to handover the possession in August 2016, nothing is </span><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">offered</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;till today and there is nothing foreseen in view of the possession. Rather, the Demand Notice is slapped on the Complainant in spite of 65% payment. Hence, the Complainant has lost his interest to continue with the Developer.</span></font></p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nArial\">(i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Refund\r\nthe entire amount paid by the Complainant i.e. Rs.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-caps: small-caps;\">8,32,050/- </span>along with the interest @18% p.a. as per section\r\n18 of the RERA Act, from the respective date of deposits till the final\r\nrealization.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-indent: -36pt;\">(ii)</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-indent: -36pt;\">Impose\r\nthe penalty of an amount of Rs.5,00,000/-</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-indent: -36pt;\">&nbsp;\r\n</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-indent: -36pt;\">on developer for not complying under section 3 of RERA Act.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-indent: -36pt;\">(iii)</span>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Impose penalty on the\r\nDeveloper to pay heavy compensation to the Complainant on account of deficiency\r\nin services resulting in mental agony, harassment, humiliation and financial\r\nloss</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">(iv)</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -36pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Pay\r\nRs.55, 000/- towards the costs of the litigation.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',1290000.00,832050.00,'2016-08-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-02-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','631, IIIrd Floor, Palm Heights, Dera Bassi','','',1,0,0,0,'MukeshPandit','2018-10-17 11:14:23.000','MukeshPandit','2018-10-17 11:14:23.000'),(123,1059,'1059',1158,'0c27aca9-8cc5-4938-a0f5-138a7568230c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-22 14:58:53.000','Naveen  Walia','vdharmani@gmail.com',9780041313,0,0,'R/O 24 Milk ','Milk (Part)(307)',13,1,'134203','1','534','Sector-10-D',6,128,'160011','Vipul Dharmani','vdharmani@gmail.com',9780041313,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0292','Palm Heights Private Limited','Harjinder Singh Rangi','mkdattachd74@mail.com',0,0,'HAIBATPUR ROAD, OPP. HANSA TUBES','TEH. DERA BASSI,',28,507,'140507','1','HAIBATPUR ROAD, OPP. HANSA TUBES','TEH. DERA BASSI,',28,507,'140507','0','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">The developer of Palm Heights, Haibatpur Road, DeraBassi, Distt.\r\nSAS Nagar, Mohali approached the Complainant in the month of January&nbsp; 2016 persuading him to purchase a flat in its\r\nsaid project.</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;Complainant sought financial assistence from&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">DHFL,whereupon the NBFC</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;sanctioned loan in favour of the\r\nComplainants for a tune of Rs.11,72,989/- from which an amount of Rs.\r\n8,44,039/- as sale consideration has already been disbursed to the developer by the DHFL. Since thereon, the Complainant is </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">regularly paying the EMI to the Bank as per\r\nthe loan documents.</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">At present there is\r\nno construction work being carried out by the Developer and furthermore\r\nthere is no scope of the same being completed in the near future, till even two\r\nto three years. Moreover, even the development work of the entire project, with\r\nregard to the amenities to be provided has not even started, as was promised by\r\nthe Developer at the time of booking of the flat, way back in the year 2016. Whereas the Developer has slept one more Demand Notice to the Complainant in spite of the 65% of the Payment. Hence the Complainant lost the interest to continue with the Developer.</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nArial\">(i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Hand\r\nover the possession of the flat after completing the construction and other\r\ndevelopment work without any further delay. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nArial\">(ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Or\r\nrefund the entire amount paid by the Complainant i.e. Rs.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-caps: small-caps;\">8,32,050/- </span>along with the interest @18%\r\np.a.from the respective date of deposits till the final realization.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1;tab-stops:list 90.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nArial\">(iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Pay\r\nto the Complainant an amount of Rs.5,00,000/- as compensation to the\r\nComplainant on account of deficiency in services resulting in mental agony,\r\nharassment, humiliation and financial loss suffered due to deficient services\r\nand unfair trade practice of the Opposite Party;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; (iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Pay Rs.55, 000/- towards the costs of the\r\nlitigation</span><br></p>',1290000.00,832050.00,'2016-08-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-02-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','631, IIIrd Floor, Palm Heights,Dera Bassi','','',1,0,0,0,'MukeshPandit','2018-10-17 15:40:37.000','MukeshPandit','2018-10-17 15:40:37.000'),(124,1060,'1060',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','1','344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','Motia Developers, Private Limited','M/s Motia Developers, Private Limited','info@motiagroup.com',8558844525,0,'Chandigarh - Ambala Highway,','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Chandigarh - Ambala Highway,','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿</span><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">a</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">.\r\nApplicants are husband and wife and joint allottees of the unit 31B-3<sup>rd</sup>\r\nFloor as per Allotment Letter dated Feb 5,2016 (Annexure 1). They have made\r\nfull payment except for the amount due at the time of possession (for details Annexure\r\n2)</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">\r\nRespondent has committed to hand over possession of the unit on or before Feb\r\n4, 2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of allotment in the Buyers Agreement/Agreement\r\nof Sale (relevant page of agreement at Annexure 3) but has failed to deliver\r\npossession by the stipulated date which is evident from his letter dated Feb 7,\r\n2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">The project is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so\r\ncalled Completion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5)\r\nbut it certifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy (cf. ‘</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman;color:#231F20\">completion certificate’ and\r\n‘occupancy certificate’ definitions in the Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2016, <i>henceforth called\r\nthe Real Estate Act,</i> - Section 2, clause (q) and (zf) respectively).</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">The most important fact and bottom line is that Respondent\r\nhas not given possession by the stipulated date irrespective of his position on\r\ncompletion. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\"> Applicants have served a Legal\r\nNotice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent (Annexure 6) He has been requested\r\nto refund the received amount of Rs. 42, 50,362.00 with interest plus\r\ncompensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice. The notice was\r\nreceived on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> The project is an ongoing project and it is now\r\nwell settled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgements of\r\nthe Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer, Punjab.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿Section 18 of the Real Estate Act provides that, if the promoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession in terms of the agreement for sale by the date specified therein for any reason and the allottee (s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be liable to return the amount received by him along with interest and furthermore he shall be liable to pay compensation. \r\n</span><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Applicants are withdrawing from the project and claiming the following.\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">a. Refund of Principal Amount of Payments Received (Annexure2): \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;Amounts received up to July 7, 2015 = Rs 36,55,608#\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; Amount received on Feb 6, 2016      = Rs  5,94,754##\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">			\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;#Copies of Respondent’s Ledger Account at Annexure 7\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;## Copy of Applicants Cheque No. 045314 encashed on Feb 6, 2016  at Annexure 8\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">b. Payment of Interest: Interest is payable at SBI’s maximum MCLR + 2% (Rule 16 of Punjab Real Estate Rules, 2017). It is due from the date Respondent received the amount or any part thereof till the date the amount or part thereof and interest thereon is refunded (Section 2 of the Real State Act,  clause (za) and sub-clause (ii)).\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;Interest up to Sep 30, 2018 as per details in Annexure 2	 = Rs 20,67,369\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;Interest from Oct 1, 2018 to the date of refund, say		 =INT\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">c. Payment of Compensation:\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Applicants have not been able to utilise the allotted unit because of Respondent’s failure to deliver possession by the committed date and suffered considerable financial loss. Furthermore they have to modify and change their plans which have caused mental distress. It has involved a lot of work resulting in both physical and mental stress and pain. They are presently undergoing unnecessary litigation. It is difficult to quantify the claim on these counts. However we peg it at a reasonable amount of Rs. 2 lakh.\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">d. Total Claim: 				\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;(i)  Total Principal Amount Received 	= Rs 42,50,362\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; (ii)  Interest				= (Rs 20,67,369 + INT) \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;(iii) Compensation 			=  Rs  2,00,000 \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Total	= (Rs 65,17,731 + INT)</span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B - 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh - Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-10-18 13:34:53.000','kssidhu','2018-10-18 13:34:53.000'),(125,1060,'1060',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','1','344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','Motia Developers, Private Limited','M/s Motia Developers, Private Limited','info@motiagroup.com',8558844525,0,'Chandigarh - Ambala Highway,','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Chandigarh - Ambala Highway,','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿</span><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">a</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">.\r\nApplicants are husband and wife and joint allottees of the unit 31B-3<sup>rd</sup>\r\nFloor as per Allotment Letter dated Feb 5,2016 (Annexure 1). They have made\r\nfull payment except for the amount due at the time of possession (for details Annexure\r\n2)</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">\r\nRespondent has committed to hand over possession of the unit on or before Feb\r\n4, 2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of allotment in the Buyers Agreement/Agreement\r\nof Sale (relevant page of agreement at Annexure 3) but has failed to deliver\r\npossession by the stipulated date which is evident from his letter dated Feb 7,\r\n2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">The project is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so\r\ncalled Completion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5)\r\nbut it certifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy (cf. ‘</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman;color:#231F20\">completion certificate’ and\r\n‘occupancy certificate’ definitions in the Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2016, <i>henceforth called\r\nthe Real Estate Act,</i> - Section 2, clause (q) and (zf) respectively).</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">The most important fact and bottom line is that Respondent\r\nhas not given possession by the stipulated date irrespective of his position on\r\ncompletion. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\"> Applicants have served a Legal\r\nNotice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent (Annexure 6) He has been requested\r\nto refund the received amount of Rs. 42, 50,362.00 with interest plus\r\ncompensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice. The notice was\r\nreceived on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> The project is an ongoing project and it is now\r\nwell settled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgements of\r\nthe Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer, Punjab.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿Section 18 of the Real Estate Act provides that, if the promoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession in terms of the agreement for sale by the date specified therein for any reason and the allottee (s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be liable to return the amount received by him along with interest and furthermore he shall be liable to pay compensation. \r\n</span><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Applicants are withdrawing from the project and claiming the following.\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">a. Refund of Principal Amount of Payments Received (Annexure2): \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;Amounts received up to July 7, 2015 = Rs 36,55,608#\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; Amount received on Feb 6, 2016      = Rs  5,94,754##\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">			\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;#Copies of Respondent’s Ledger Account at Annexure 7\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;## Copy of Applicants Cheque No. 045314 encashed on Feb 6, 2016  at Annexure 8\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">b. Payment of Interest: Interest is payable at SBI’s maximum MCLR + 2% (Rule 16 of Punjab Real Estate Rules, 2017). It is due from the date Respondent received the amount or any part thereof till the date the amount or part thereof and interest thereon is refunded (Section 2 of the Real State Act,  clause (za) and sub-clause (ii)).\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;Interest up to Sep 30, 2018 as per details in Annexure 2	 = Rs 20,67,369\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;Interest from Oct 1, 2018 to the date of refund, say		 =INT\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">c. Payment of Compensation:\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Applicants have not been able to utilise the allotted unit because of Respondent’s failure to deliver possession by the committed date and suffered considerable financial loss. Furthermore they have to modify and change their plans which have caused mental distress. It has involved a lot of work resulting in both physical and mental stress and pain. They are presently undergoing unnecessary litigation. It is difficult to quantify the claim on these counts. However we peg it at a reasonable amount of Rs. 2 lakh.\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">d. Total Claim: 				\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;(i)  Total Principal Amount Received 	= Rs 42,50,362\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; (ii)  Interest				= (Rs 20,67,369 + INT) \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;(iii) Compensation 			=  Rs  2,00,000 \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Total	= (Rs 65,17,731 + INT)</span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B - 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh - Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-10-18 14:50:17.000','kssidhu','2018-10-18 14:50:17.000'),(126,1060,'1060',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,