y		 =INT\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">c. Payment of Compensation:\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Applicants have not been able to utilise the allotted unit because of Respondent’s failure to deliver possession by the committed date and suffered considerable financial loss. Furthermore they have to modify and change their plans which have caused mental distress. It has involved a lot of work resulting in both physical and mental stress and pain. They are presently undergoing unnecessary litigation. It is difficult to quantify the claim on these counts. However we peg it at a reasonable amount of Rs. 2 lakh.\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">d. Total Claim: 				\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;(i)  Total Principal Amount Received 	= Rs 42,50,362\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; (ii)  Interest				= (Rs 20,67,369 + INT) \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;(iii) Compensation 			=  Rs  2,00,000 \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Total	= (Rs 65,17,731 + INT)</span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B - 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh - Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-10-19 08:36:42.000','kssidhu','2018-10-19 08:36:42.000'),(129,1061,'1061',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134109','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/S MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE & CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'2013-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-02-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-10-20 16:00:53.000','Ramantakiar','2018-10-20 16:00:53.000'),(130,1061,'1061',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134109','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/S MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE & CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','The complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked (C-1) a 350 sq yards plot @ RS.18000/- per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC) from the respondent in the project Palm Spring, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured&nbsp; by the respondent that it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained within 2-3 months and the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2 years. A payment plan(C-2) was also provided to the applicant.\r\n<div>The applicant paid Rs. 1890000- i.e. 30% of total sale consideration along with the application. Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yards plot instead of 350 sq yards and accordingly requested(C-3) respondent to change the size of plot. The said request was accepted and respondent refunded the excess amount of Rs. 490000(C-4) in the process of completing 30% amount in respect of 250 sq yd plot Otherwise it ought to have refunded 540000 but promised to adjust Rs.1400000/- towards 250 sq yd plot.</div><div>The respondent issued an acknowledgement(C-5) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it arbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed between the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened the applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid. Also in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/- instead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust remaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.\r\n</div><div>Inspite of number of visits, repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-6) was also sent to it but to no avail.\r\n</div><div>The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since&nbsp; beginning and never informed him about the true picture . It had not even applied the permissions when the plot was sold. A list of approvals along with the dates when the same were applied and obtained is attached as C-7 and some important approvals as C-8 to C-</div>','<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(i) Directing the\r\nrespondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 1400000/- as per Section 18\r\nof RERA&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: 700;\">along with interest to be calculated at the rate as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017,&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">as the applicant has lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date and thus the applicant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The respondent collected the money from the applicant in 2011. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any sale agreement and issue a plot number till date and pressurizing the applicant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter and execution of buyer\'s agreement.</span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(ii) Directing the\r\nrespondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs for </span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">deficiency\r\nin services, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the applicant and for using the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long period. Inspite of repeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date.</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(iii)\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div><p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><br clear=\"all\" style=\"page-break-before:always;mso-break-type:section-break\"></span></p>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'2013-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-02-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-10-20 19:27:20.000','Ramantakiar','2018-10-20 19:27:20.000'),(131,1061,'1061',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-22 18:39:51.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134109','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/S MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE & CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','The complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked (C-1) a 350 sq yards plot @ RS.18000/- per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC) from the respondent in the project Palm Springs, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured&nbsp; by the respondent that it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained within 2-3 months and the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2 years.&nbsp;<div>The applicant paid Rs. 1890000 i.e. 30% of total sale consideration along with the application. Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yards plot instead of 350 sq yards and accordingly requested(C-2) respondent to change the size of plot. The said request was accepted and respondent refunded the excess amount of Rs. 490000(C-3) in the process of completing 30% amount in respect of 250 sq yd plot Otherwise it ought to have refunded 540000 but promised to adjust Rs.1400000/- towards 250 sq yd plot.</div><div>The respondent issued an acknowledgement(C-4) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it arbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed between the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened the applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid. Also in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/- instead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust remaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.\r\n</div><div>Inspite of number of visits, repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-5) was also sent to it but to no avail.\r\n</div><div>The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since&nbsp; beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and the development . It had not even applied the permissions when the plot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals along with the dates when the same were applied and obtained is attached as C-6 and some important approvals as C-7 &amp; C-8.</div>','<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(i) Directing the\r\nrespondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 1400000/- as per Section 18\r\nof RERA&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: 700;\">along with interest to be calculated at the rate as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017,&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">as the applicant has lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date and thus the applicant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The respondent collected the money from the applicant in 2011. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any sale agreement and issue a plot number till date and pressurizing the applicant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter and execution of buyer\'s agreement.</span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(ii) Directing the\r\nrespondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs for </span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">deficiency\r\nin services, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the applicant and for using the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long period. Inspite of repeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date.</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(iii)\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div><p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><br clear=\"all\" style=\"page-break-before:always;mso-break-type:section-break\"></span></p>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'2013-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-02-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-10-20 20:20:32.000','Ramantakiar','2018-10-20 20:20:32.000'),(132,1062,'1062',1169,'6d8e8eb2-35ca-4175-8d45-66d628f12955','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-26 12:16:08.000','Hope Clinics','hopeclinics@yahoo.com',9316517176,0,0,'H. No. 1184','Sector 21-B',6,128,'160022','1','H. No. 1184','Sector 21-B',6,128,'160022','Vijayinder Singh Rana','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0227','Sunny Enclave Sector 123','Bajwa Developers Ltd.','bajwadeveloperltd@gmail.com',0,0,'Sunny Business Centre, 5th Floor,','New Sunny Enclave, Greater Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','Sunny Business Centre, 5th Floor,','New Sunny Enclave, Greater Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','<p>1. The applicant purchased two adjoining showroom plots (No. 1066 and 1067) in promoter\'s project.\r\n</p><p>2. No dues certificate was issued on 31/03/2015 for both plots after full payment of Rs. 10200000 (Ann. A1-4).\r\n</p><p>3. Plots allotted on 06/04/2016 (Ann. A-5).\r\n</p><p>4. Plinth level certificate issued on 31/05/2016 (Ann. A-6).\r\n</p><p>5. Thereafter, construction of showroom buildings was completed by 01/09/2016. \r\n</p><p>6. However, the applicant has been repeatedly denied the occupancy certificate by the GMADA due to non completion of the development works by the promoter in the project (Ann. A-7, 9, 11).\r\n</p><p>7. The copies of representations made to promoter in this regard have been annexed as Ann. A-8 and 12.\r\n</p><p>8. The applicant informed the concerned housing authorities through various representations (Ann. A-10, 14, 15, 18).\r\n</p><p>9. That promoter has failed to complete the development works and because of this the applicant has not been able to occupy and utilise the completely constructed showroom buildings. Applicant is incurring heavy monetary losses by each passing day since 01/09/2016.\r\n</p><p>10. Apart from this the adjacent showrooms (SCO Nos. 1063-1065) are being constructed, in contravention of the sanctioned plans, with more number of floors than allowed. Even this was brought to the knowledge of the promoter and the competent authorities however no appropriate action has been taken.\r\n</p><p>11. That recently it has come to fore that a new unplanned showroom is being constructed adjacent to SCO No. 1063, which is not present in the plan. This has further adversely affected the value of applicant\'s property and future potential income.  \r\n</p><p>11. The applicant had earlier approached the Honourable Adjudicating Officer, Punjab RERA with the same matter vide AO 1 of 2017. However, as the project was not registered at that time, therefore on 26/12/2017, it was held to be not maintainable (Ann. A-13, 16 &amp; 17).\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Hence, the present application is being filed before the Honourable Adjudicating Officer.</p>','<p>It is respectfully prayed that the Honourable Authority may kindly summon the records of the case and after perusing the same, may kindly be pleased to impose:-\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; i)     Compensation for not completing the external and internal development works of the project and allowing unplanned construction in adjacent buildings, due to which the competent authority has refused to issue completion certificate. The promoter may be held liable for the loss incurred by applicant due to non utilisation of the completed showrooms since 01/09/2016. The amount calculated conservatively may be the rental income which may have been generated from the said two showrooms, which has been arrived at  Rs. 3120000 (Rs. 60000 per month per SCO = Rs. 120000 for 26 months).\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ii)    Compensation for changing the layout of the buildings. The competent authority and the promoter may be directed to permit the applicant to similarly claim the additional area as has been allowed to adjacent SCO Nos. 1063-65 and the expenses for the construction of the same may be ordered to be paid by the promoter. In my evaluation it must be more than Rs. 1500000.\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; iii)    Exemplary punitive compensation to act as a deterrent which may be an amount equal to Rs. 100000.\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; iv)    Compensation for mental harassment and agony caused due to non utilisation and unplanned adjacent development, which may be equal to Rs. 100000.\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; v)    Litigation charges for approaching the Honourable RERA twice, as the status of project registration had not been made public earlier by the promoter, amounting to Rs. 100000.\r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; vi)    Such other compensation as may be considered necessary for furtherance of justice. \r\n</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The total compensation amount that has been arrived, on the above mentioned grounds, is Rs. 4920000, which the Honourable Authority may impose upon the promoter for its failure to complete development works and allowing unsanctioned construction in the adjacent showroom buildings.</p>',7800000.00,10200000.00,'2016-04-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','0','','2015-03-31 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','SCO 1066-67 Aerodale Market Sunny Enclave Residential Township Sector 123 SAS Nagar 140301','','',1,1,0,0,'Hopeclinics','2018-10-24 11:08:14.000','Hopeclinics','2018-10-24 11:08:14.000'),(133,1063,'1063',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramesh Mittal','rameshmittal69@gmail.com',9934787251,0,0,'Mittal House, Main Road','Near Pankaj Cinema, Raxaul',5,188,'845305','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Spring','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>abc&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>','<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; bc<br></p>',5000000.00,1500000.00,'2015-10-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-10-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','no allotment yet','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-10-24 13:24:45.000','Ramantakiar','2018-10-24 13:24:45.000'),(134,1063,'1063',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramesh Mittal','rameshmittal69@gmail.com',9934787251,0,0,'Mittal House, Main Road','Near Pankaj Cinema, Raxaul',5,188,'845305','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Spring','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Applicant on 21.10.2013 booked(C1)250 sq yards plot @RS. 20000 per sq yd from the respondent in Palm Spring.Respondent assured that it has all approvals except layout which will be obtained within 2-3months and possession will be delivered in 2 years.A broacher(C2)was also provided to applicant before booking. Applicant paid Rs. 1500000 i.e 30% of sale consideration vide two cheques(C3)dated 21.10.13 &amp; 19.12.13. Insipte of repeated requests,respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement.Respondent had even concealed that it was not having CLU and it was in September,2014(C4)it informed the applicant that it has received the CLU now and allotment shall be made in Dec,2014.The applicant was shocked after knowing that as he was under impression that it was having all the approvals but since the respondent assured to make allotment in Dec, 2014 the applicant chose to have the plot since substantial amount was already paid by him.But the respondent did not issue any allotment letter even by the said date.The respondent even failed to start any development.Inspite of number of visits,repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement during year 2014 to 2018.Email was also sent to respondent on 17.08.18(C5)requesting the respondent to refund the amount since the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute agreement.Then the respondent telephonically informed the applicant that it will sell the plot at premium of Rs. 2000 per sq yd and refund the amount to him, And for that purpose also asked the bank detail,which was duly sent by the applicant vide email dated 21.08.18(C6).The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and development.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to applicant.A list of dates of approvals C7 and some important approvals as C8 &amp; C9 \r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; bc<br></p>',5000000.00,1500000.00,'2015-10-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-10-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','no allotment yet','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-10-24 13:52:08.000','Ramantakiar','2018-10-24 13:52:08.000'),(135,1063,'1063',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramesh Mittal','rameshmittal69@gmail.com',9934787251,0,0,'Mittal House, Main Road','Near Pankaj Cinema, Raxaul',5,188,'845305','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Spring','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Applicant on 21.10.2013 booked(C1)250 sq yards plot @RS. 20000 per sq yd from the respondent in Palm Spring.Respondent assured that it has all approvals except layout which will be obtained within 2-3months and possession will be delivered in 2 years.A broacher(C2)was also provided to applicant before booking. Applicant paid Rs. 1500000 i.e 30% of sale consideration vide two cheques(C3)dated 21.10.13 &amp; 19.12.13. Insipte of repeated requests,respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement.Respondent had even concealed that it was not having CLU and it was in September,2014(C4)it informed the applicant that it has received the CLU now and allotment shall be made in Dec,2014.The applicant was shocked after knowing that as he was under impression that it was having all the approvals but since the respondent assured to make allotment in Dec, 2014 the applicant chose to have the plot since substantial amount was already paid by him.But the respondent did not issue any allotment letter even by the said date.The respondent even failed to start any development.Inspite of number of visits,repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement during year 2014 to 2018.Email was also sent to respondent on 17.08.18(C5)requesting the respondent to refund the amount since the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute agreement.Then the respondent telephonically informed the applicant that it will sell the plot at premium of Rs. 2000 per sq yd and refund the amount to him, And for that purpose also asked the bank detail,which was duly sent by the applicant vide email dated 21.08.18(C6).The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and development.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to applicant.A list of dates of approvals C7 and some important approvals as C8 &amp; C9 \r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">(i)\r\nDirecting the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 1500000/- as\r\nper Section 18 of RERA along with interest to be calculated at the rate as\r\ncontemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Rules, 2017, as the applicant has lost faith in the respondent due\r\nto misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during\r\nall these years ,did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s\r\nagreement till date, failed to develop the project and thus the applicant wish\r\nto withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of\r\nvarious provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it,\r\nas it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section\r\n44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The respondent collected the money\r\nfrom the applicant in 2013. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the\r\nground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the\r\ngeneral public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also,\r\ninspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any\r\nsale agreement and issue a plot number till date and pressurizing the applicant\r\nto pay more money for getting the allotment letter and execution of buyer\'s\r\nagreement (ii) Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs\r\nfor deficiency in services, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the\r\napplicant and for using the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long\r\nperiod. Inspite of repeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did\r\nnot issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date.\r\n(iii) Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000/-<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5000000.00,1500000.00,'2015-10-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-10-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','no allotment yet','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-10-24 13:56:05.000','Ramantakiar','2018-10-24 13:56:05.000'),(136,1063,'1063',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramesh Mittal','rameshmittal69@gmail.com',9934787251,0,0,'Mittal House, Main Road','Near Pankaj Cinema, Raxaul',5,188,'845305','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Spring','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Applicant on 21.10.2013 booked(C1)250 sq yards plot @RS. 20000 per sq yd from the respondent in Palm Spring.Respondent assured that it has all approvals except layout which will be obtained within 2-3months and possession will be delivered in 2 years.A broacher(C2)was also provided to applicant before booking. Applicant paid Rs. 1500000 i.e 30% of sale consideration vide two cheques(C3)dated 21.10.13 &amp; 19.12.13. Insipte of repeated requests,respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement.Respondent had even concealed that it was not having CLU and it was in September,2014(C4)it informed the applicant that it has received the CLU now and allotment shall be made in Dec,2014.The applicant was shocked after knowing that as he was under impression that it was having all the approvals but since the respondent assured to make allotment in Dec, 2014 the applicant chose to have the plot since substantial amount was already paid by him.But the respondent did not issue any allotment letter even by the said date.The respondent even failed to start any development.Inspite of number of visits,repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement during year 2014 to 2018.Email was also sent to respondent on 17.08.18(C5)requesting the respondent to refund the amount since the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute agreement.Then the respondent telephonically informed the applicant that it will sell the plot at premium of Rs. 2000 per sq yd and refund the amount to him, And for that purpose also asked the bank detail,which was duly sent by the applicant vide email dated 21.08.18(C6).The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and development.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to applicant.A list of dates of approvals C7 and some important approvals as C8 &amp; C9 \r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-s