rid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">(i)\r\nDirecting the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 1500000/- as\r\nper Section 18 of RERA along with interest to be calculated at the rate as\r\ncontemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Rules, 2017, as the applicant has lost faith in the respondent due\r\nto misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during\r\nall these years ,did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s\r\nagreement till date, failed to develop the project and thus the applicant wish\r\nto withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of\r\nvarious provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it,\r\nas it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section\r\n44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The respondent collected the money\r\nfrom the applicant in 2013. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the\r\nground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the\r\ngeneral public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also,\r\ninspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any\r\nsale agreement and issue a plot number till date and pressurizing the applicant\r\nto pay more money for getting the allotment letter and execution of buyer\'s\r\nagreement (ii) Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs\r\nfor deficiency in services, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the\r\napplicant and for using the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long\r\nperiod. Inspite of repeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did\r\nnot issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date.\r\n(iii) Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000/-<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5000000.00,1500000.00,'2015-10-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-10-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','no allotment & Agreement yet','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2018-10-24 18:54:08.000','rerafilingformn','2018-10-24 18:54:08.000'),(141,1063,'1063',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramesh Mittal','rameshmittal69@gmail.com',9934787251,0,0,'Mittal House, Main Road','Near Pankaj Cinema, Raxaul',5,188,'845305','1','House No.253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Spring','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Applicant, on 21.10.2013 booked a (C1) 250 sq yards plot @RS. 20000 per sq yd from the respondent in Palm Spring.Respondent assured that it has all approvals except layout which will be obtained within 2-3months and possession will be delivered in 2 years.A broacher (C2) was also provided to applicant before booking. Applicant paid Rs. 1500000 i.e 30% of sale consideration vide two cheques (C3)dated 21.10.13 &amp; 19.12.13. Insipte of repeated requests,respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement.Respondent had even concealed that it was not having CLU and it was in September,2014(C4)it informed the applicant that it has received the CLU now and allotment shall be made in Dec,2014.The applicant was shocked after knowing that as he was under impression that it was having all the approvals but since the respondent assured to make allotment in Dec, 2014 the applicant chose to have the plot since substantial amount was already paid by him.But the respondent did not issue any allotment letter even by the said date.The respondent even failed to start any developmen