 apartment, we&nbsp;have been forced to take a flat on rent at above-mentioned address and have been paying Rs. 16,500 per month along with maintenance.&nbsp;Therefore we&nbsp;are also entitled to recover compensation to the tune of&nbsp;Rs. 16,500 per month</li><li class=\"m_5142867886888198341gmail-li1\" style=\"margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">Mental agony/Legal Fee\'s: We have&nbsp;suffered severe mental agony and harassment and further had to incur the litigation expenses to pursue the present complaint. Therefore we&nbsp;are entitled to recover compensation to the tune of Rs.5,00,000/- towards mental agony and litigation expenses.</li><li class=\"m_5142867886888198341gmail-li1\" style=\"margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">Contractual Provision: As per Clause 6.3 of Buyer-seller agreement i.e&nbsp; Rs 5 per month/per square feet of the Super Built-up Area (2400sqft.)</li></ol><style type=\"text/css\"> li.li1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px \'Helvetica Neue\'; color: #454545} ol.ol1 {list-style-type: decimal} </style>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',2,0,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-10-25 14:55:46.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-10-25 14:55:46.000'),(154,1036,'1036',1092,'506ad359-88c1-4045-ba35-1eef15c3e32e','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-04 11:51:37.000','Darshan  Singh','advbswalia@gmail.com',9814685406,1722625103,497110579868,'5405, Sector 38 West ','',6,128,'160014','1','5405, Sector 38 West ','',6,128,'160014','B.S. Walia','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','Punjab Urban Planning and Development authority (LOBP Scheme)','Punjab Urban Planning and Development authority (PUDA) through Estate Officer','helpdesk@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA  Bhawan , Sector 62 , S.A.S Nagar , Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA  Bhawan , Sector 62 , S.A.S Nagar , Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>That the respondent issued allotment Letter of intent (LOI) to applicant for residential plot  no. 94 measuring 545 Sq. Yard, Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali- 160055 dated 14.1.2016  in reference to application form no. 832. That in furtherance  of letter of Intent , allotment letter&nbsp; dated 9-8-2016 was issued to applicant . The tentative price of the plot is Rs. 11445000/- at the rate of Rs. 21,000/- Rs/Sq. Yard. In pursuance to Allotment Letter, Applicant paid full and final lump sum payment of Rs.1,14,45,000/- .</p><p>Thus, till date Rs. 11445000/- has been paid by Applicant to the respondent as per statement of account. As per the Allotment Letter dated 9.8.2016, the possession of the said plot in question was to be given within 18 months from the date of issuance of allotment which is already over i.e. 8.2.2018 Thus, the respondent has failed to handover possession within the stipulated time as written in the allotment letter agreed between the parties. The respondent has yet to give reply to Applicant whether they have got the Occupancy Certificate/Completion Certificate for the said plot or not? Respondent has been avoiding this question for too long since the Allotment letter was issued. That the said project promoted by respondent lacks basic infrastructure like roads, poor connectivity, drains, electricity, water supply, green cover and parks, street lights missing, roads without berm, no provision of security nor any existence of police post. All these factors further make plot unfit for habitation and construction.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Applicant has given a letter on 30-11-2017\r\nregarding possession of plot no. 94 , Sector 118-119 , Gateway City Mohali. Even today</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">, <span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the development works at the said ‘Gateway\r\nCity’ are not complete, which means the possession of plot is no sooner\r\nexpected than 2019 from respondent. Thus, there is a clear delay on the part of\r\nrespondent.</span></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In\r\nview of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> </span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">prays\r\nfor the following compensation(s):- </span><o:p></o:p></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1 </span></span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant\r\npay 12% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> 11445000</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;letter-spacing:1.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">/-</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">from date of possession .</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> </span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2 Compensation for inability/failure to discharge obligations\r\nas per Allotment Letter and RERA Act under </span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">Section\r\n18 (3)</span></i></b></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> lacking in basic\r\nservices which was initially promised and no disclosure about status of Completion\r\nCertificate/Occupancy Certificate before handing over the possession.</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3\r\nCompensation on account of mental agony, pain and litigation expenses upto Rs.\r\n2 lakh as illustrated in the Section 72 of the RERA Act. </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4 Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may deem\r\nfit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of\r\nApplicant.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>',11445000.00,11445000.00,'2018-02-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','#94, Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'bswalia','2018-10-27 20:06:37.000','bswalia','2018-10-27 20:06:37.000'),(155,1065,'1065',1173,'dd2e0667-81c8-4893-b732-43ed1d145484','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Atul Mehan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815075066,0,0,'Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','1','Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,8699174000,'GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<p>asdc</p>','<p>ascc</p>',7381250.00,5550000.00,'2016-04-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-04-02 00:00:00','2013-04-02 00:00:00','Flat No. 103, Tower-2, First Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, MOhali','','',2,0,0,0,'atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:19:41.000','atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:19:41.000'),(156,1065,'1065',1173,'dd2e0667-81c8-4893-b732-43ed1d145484','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Atul Mehan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815075066,0,0,'Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','1','Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,8699174000,'GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<ul><li><li>That the respondent is developing Group Housing under the name and style of Acme Eden Court in the JLPL Township Sector 90 91, SAS Nagar, District Mohali.&nbsp;</li><li>That the original layout plan of the Acme Eden Court is attached at Annexure I.</li><li>That the applicant booked an apartment in the year 2010 with the respondent&nbsp; vide application for&nbsp; unit No 103, Floor 1, Tower 2 having an approximate super area of 2330 sq.ft. and paid an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- towards booking amount as per payment receipt attached as Annexure II.</li><li>The the applicant made additional payment of Rs. 18,00,000/- on 02.04.2013 vide payment receipt attached as Annexure III. The allotment letter was issued to the applicant as attached at Annexure IV.&nbsp;</li><li>That the respondent signed Builder Buyer Agreement with the applicant on 05.04.2013 attached at Annexure V. The total consideration of the allotted unit was fixed at Rs. 7381250/- and the payment plan was defined in Plan-C of Schedule I referred in clause 2 of the agreement.&nbsp;</li><li>That despite no progress on construction work at project site, the applicant made payments as requested as per payment receipts dated 5.11.2015 attached as Annexure VI for PLC charges of Rs. 728125 plus service tax and Annexure VII towards construction work of 10% of BSP amounting to Rs. 5,23,169/- plus service tax,&nbsp;</li><li>That the applicant again cooperated with the respondent and in the hope of getting early possession of the allotted unit, paid additional amount of Rs 22,50,000/- including service tax on 3rd July 2015 as per payment receipts attached at Annexure VIII.</li><li>The respondent immediately on receipt of 80% of the amount of BSP, sent a reminder on 7th July, 2015 asking for balance payment of BSP, PLC and even the amount payable at the time of possession as attached at Annexed IX which was later kept in abeyance.</li></li></ul>','<p>ascc</p>',7381250.00,5550000.00,'2016-04-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-04-02 00:00:00','2013-04-02 00:00:00','Flat No. 103, Tower-2, First Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, MOhali','','',2,0,0,0,'atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:22:12.000','atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:22:12.000'),(157,1065,'1065',1173,'dd2e0667-81c8-4893-b732-43ed1d145484','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Atul Mehan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815075066,0,0,'Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','1','Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,8699174000,'GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<ul><li>That the respondent is developing Group Housing under the name and style of Acme Eden Court in the JLPL Township Sector 90 91, SAS Nagar, District Mohali.&nbsp;</li><li>That the original layout plan of the Acme Eden Court is attached at Annexure I.</li><li>That the applicant booked an apartment in the year 2010 with the respondent&nbsp; vide application for&nbsp; unit No 103, Floor 1, Tower 2 having an approximate super area of 2330 sq.ft. and paid an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- towards booking amount as per payment receipt attached as Annexure II.</li><li>The the applicant made additional payment of Rs. 18,00,000/- on 02.04.2013 vide payment receipt attached as Annexure III. The allotment letter was issued to the applicant as attached at Annexure IV.&nbsp;</li><li>That the respondent signed Builder Buyer Agreement with the applicant on 05.04.2013 attached at Annexure V. The total consideration of the allotted unit was fixed at Rs. 7381250/- and the payment plan was defined in Plan-C of Schedule I referred in clause 2 of the agreement.&nbsp;</li><li>That despite no progress on construction work at project site, the applicant made payments as requested as per payment receipts dated 5.11.2015 attached as Annexure VI for PLC charges of Rs. 728125 plus service tax and Annexure VII towards construction work of 10% of BSP amounting to Rs. 5,23,169/- plus service tax,&nbsp;</li><li>That the applicant again cooperated with the respondent and in the hope of getting early possession of the allotted unit, paid additional amount of Rs 22,50,000/- including service tax on 3rd July 2015 as per payment receipts attached at Annexure VIII.</li><li>The respondent immediately on receipt of 80% of the amount of BSP, sent a reminder on 7th July, 2015 asking for balance payment of BSP, PLC and even the amount payable at the time of possession as attached at Annexed IX which was later kept in abeyance.</li></ul>','<ul><li><li>A total of Rs. 55,50,000/- including service tax of Rs 2,24,793/- has been paid by the applicant up to 03.07.2015 with no corresponding progress on the construction of the residential complex/allotted unit.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure X. These pics clearly indicate that the development works are still underway.</li><li>That the respondent has got the project registered with RERA, Punjab as per registration number PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124, being an ongoing project.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of abnormal delay in completing development works, changes in original layout plan without the consent of the applicant and other allottees.</li><li>As per clause 15 of the Builder Buyer Agreement, the possession of the allotted unit was to be offered within 36 months from the date of signing of the said agreement i.e. on 1.04.2016.&nbsp;</li><li>In view of the points above, it is clearly established that the respondent has violated the provisions of Section 12, 14, 18 &amp; 19 of Real Estate (Development &amp; Regulations) Act, 2016.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer may consider our submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 55,50,000/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent and a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- for the economic and mental sufferings to the applicant.</li></li></ul>',7