ion work at project site, the applicant made payments as requested as per payment receipts dated 5.11.2015 attached as Annexure VI for PLC charges of Rs. 728125 plus service tax and Annexure VII towards construction work of 10% of BSP amounting to Rs. 5,23,169/- plus service tax,&nbsp;</li><li>That the applicant again cooperated with the respondent and in the hope of getting early possession of the allotted unit, paid additional amount of Rs 22,50,000/- including service tax on 3rd July 2015 as per payment receipts attached at Annexure VIII.</li><li>The respondent immediately on receipt of 80% of the amount of BSP, sent a reminder on 7th July, 2015 asking for balance payment of BSP, PLC and even the amount payable at the time of possession as attached at Annexed IX which was later kept in abeyance.</li></ul>','<ul><li>A total of Rs. 55,50,000/- including service tax of Rs 2,24,793/- has been paid by the applicant up to 03.07.2015 with no corresponding progress on the construction of the residential complex/allotted unit.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure X. These pics clearly indicate that the development works are still underway.</li><li>That the respondent has got the project registered with RERA, Punjab as per registration number PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124, being an ongoing project.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of abnormal delay in completing development works, changes in original layout plan without the consent of the applicant and other allottees.</li><li>As per clause 15 of the Builder Buyer Agreement, the possession of the allotted unit was to be offered within 36 months from the date of signing of the said agreement i.e. on 1.04.2016.&nbsp;</li><li>In view of the points above, it is clearly established that the respondent has violated the provisions of Section 12, 14, 18 &amp; 19 of Real Estate (Development &amp; Regulations) Act, 2016.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer may consider our submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 55,50,000/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent and a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- for the economic and mental sufferings to the applicant.</li></ul>',7381250.00,5550000.00,'2016-04-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-04-02 00:00:00','2013-04-02 00:00:00','Flat No. 103, Tower-2, First Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, MOhali','','',2,0,0,0,'atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:24:57.000','atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:24:57.000'),(159,1065,'1065',1173,'dd2e0667-81c8-4893-b732-43ed1d145484','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Atul Mehan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815075066,0,0,'Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','1','Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,8699174000,'GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<ul><li>That the respondent is developing Group Housing under the name and style of Acme Eden Court in the JLPL Township Sector 90 91, SAS Nagar, District Mohali.&nbsp;</li><li>That the original layout plan of the Acme Eden Court is attached at Annexure I.</li><li>That the applicant booked an apartment in the year 2010 with the respondent&nbsp; vide application for&nbsp; unit No 103, Floor 1, Tower 2 having an approximate super area of 2330 sq.ft. and paid an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- towards booking amount as per payment receipt attached as Annexure II.</li><li>The the applicant made additional payment of Rs. 18,00,000/- on 02.04.2013 vide payment receipt attached as Annexure III. The allotment letter was issued to the applicant as attached at Annexure IV.&nbsp;</li><li>That the respondent signed Builder Buyer Agreement with the applicant on 05.04.2013 attached at Annexure V. The total consideration of the allotted unit was fixed at Rs. 7381250/- and the payment plan was defined in Plan-C of Schedule I referred in clause 2 of the agreement.&nbsp;</li><li>That despite no progress on construction work at project site, the applicant made payments as requested as per payment receipts dated 5.11.2015 attached as Annexure VI for PLC charges of Rs. 728125 plus service tax and Annexure VII towards construction work of 10% of BSP amounting to Rs. 5,23,169/- plus service tax,&nbsp;</li><li>That the applicant again cooperated with the respondent and in the hope of getting early possession of the allotted unit, paid additional amount of Rs 22,50,000/- including service tax on 3rd July 2015 as per payment receipts attached at Annexure VIII.</li><li>The respondent immediately on receipt of 80% of the amount of BSP, sent a reminder on 7th July, 2015 asking for balance payment of BSP, PLC and even the amount payable at the time of possession as attached at Annexed IX which was later kept in abeyance.</li><li>The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure X.<br></li></ul>','<ul><li>A total of Rs. 55,50,000/- including service tax of Rs 2,24,793/- has been paid by the applicant up to 03.07.2015 with no corresponding progress on the construction of the residential complex/allotted unit.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure X. These pics clearly indicate that the development works are still underway.</li><li>That the respondent has got the project registered with RERA, Punjab as per registration number PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124, being an ongoing project.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of abnormal delay in completing development works, changes in original layout plan without the consent of the applicant and other allottees.</li><li>As per clause 15 of the Builder Buyer Agreement, the possession of the allotted unit was to be offered within 36 months from the date of signing of the said agreement i.e. on 1.04.2016.&nbsp;</li><li>In view of the points above, it is clearly established that the respondent has violated the provisions of Section 12, 14, 18 &amp; 19 of Real Estate (Development &amp; Regulations) Act, 2016.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer may consider our submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 55,50,000/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent and a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- for the economic and mental sufferings to the applicant.</li></ul><p>Place: Mohali</p><p>Date: 29/10/2018</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">						</span>Applicant: Atul Mehan&nbsp;</p><p>Through&nbsp;</p><p>Authorized Representative</p><p>(Ved Parkash)</p><p>CS in Practice</p>',7381250.00,5550000.00,'2016-04-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-04-02 00:00:00','2013-04-02 00:00:00','Flat No. 103, Tower-2, First Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, MOhali','','',2,0,0,0,'atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:33:41.000','atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:33:41.000'),(160,1065,'1065',1173,'dd2e0667-81c8-4893-b732-43ed1d145484','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 19:08:45.000','Atul Mehan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815075066,0,0,'Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','1','Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,8699174000,'GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<ul><li>That the respondent is developing Group Housing under the name and style of Acme Eden Court in the JLPL Township Sector 90 91, SAS Nagar, District Mohali.&nbsp;</li><li>That the original layout plan of the Acme Eden Court is attached at Annexure I.</li><li>That the applicant booked an apartment in the year 2010 with the respondent&nbsp; vide application for&nbsp; unit No 103, Floor 1, Tower 2 having an approximate super area of 2330 sq.ft. and paid an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- towards booking amount as per payment receipt attached as Annexure II.</li><li>The the applicant made additional payment of Rs. 18,00,000/- on 02.04.2013 vide payment receipt attached as Annexure III. The allotment letter was issued to the applicant as attached at Annexure IV.&nbsp;</li><li>That the respondent signed Builder Buyer Agreement with the applicant on 05.04.2013 attached at Annexure V. The total consideration of the allotted unit was fixed at Rs. 7381250/- and the payment plan was defined in Plan-C of Schedule I referred in clause 2 of the agreement.&nbsp;</li><li>That despite no progress on construction work at project site, the applicant made payments as requested as per payment receipts dated 5.11.2015 attached as Annexure VI for PLC charges of Rs. 728125 plus service tax and Annexure VII towards construction work of 10% of BSP amounting to Rs. 5,23,169/- plus service tax,&nbsp;</li><li>That the applicant again cooperated with the respondent and in the hope of getting early possession of the allotted unit, paid additional amount of Rs 22,50,000/- including service tax on 3rd July 2015 as per payment receipts attached at Annexure VIII.</li><li>The respondent immediately on receipt of 80% of the amount of BSP, sent a reminder on 7th July, 2015 asking for balance payment of BSP, PLC and even the amount payable at the time of possession as attached at Annexed IX which was later kept in abeyance.</li><li>The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure X.<br></li></ul>','<ul><li>A total of Rs. 55,50,000/- including service tax of Rs 2,24,793/- has been paid by the applicant up to 03.07.2015 with no corresponding progress on the construction of the residential complex/allotted unit.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure X. These pics clearly indicate that the development works are still underway.</li><li>That the respondent has got the project registered with RERA, Punjab as per registration number PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124, being an ongoing project.&nbsp;</li><li>The applicant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of abnormal delay in completing development works, changes in original layout plan without the consent of the applicant and other allottees.</li><li>As per clause 15 of the Builder Buyer Agreement, the possession of the allotted unit was to be offered within 36 months from the date of signing of the said agreement i.e. on 1.04.2016.&nbsp;</li><li>In view of the points above, it is clearly established that the respondent has violated the provisions of Section 12, 14, 18 &amp; 19 of Real Estate (Development &amp; Regulations) Act, 2016.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer may consider our submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 55,50,000/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent and a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- for the economic and mental sufferings to the applicant.</li></ul><p>Place: Mohali</p><p>Date: 29/10/2018</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">						</span>Applicant: Atul Mehan&nbsp;</p><p>Through&nbsp;</p><p>Authorized Representative</p><p>(Ved Parkash)</p><p>CS in Practice</p>',7381250.00,5550000.00,'2016-04-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-04-02 00:00:00','2013-04-02 00:00:00','Flat No. 103, Tower-2, First Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, MOhali','','',1,0,0,0,'atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:34:06.000','atulmehan','2018-10-29 15:34:06.000'),(161,1066,'1066',1156,'fe9d0b35-d692-47a7-ad8a-e66a989164d1','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jai Bhushan Chandan','jb.chandan@yahoo.com',8360074813,0,703317526144,'23-B','Moti nagar',28,366,'141010','1','23-B','Moti nagar',28,366,'141010','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811555,'ATS INFRABUILD PVT LTD','711/92 Deepali Nehru Place new Delhi',10,120,'110019','1','ATS INFRABUILD PVT LTD','711/92 Deepali Nehru Place new Delhi',10,120,'110019','0','<p>Further to interest sought in Form M in separate complaint, we seek&nbsp; compensation for mental anguish&nbsp; at my old age of 61 plus of&nbsp; Rs. 10 lacs and reimbursement of rent being paid for hiring&nbsp; &nbsp;alternate accommodation @ Rs. 26000 per month at Suncity Parikarma in Sector 20 Panchkula from 01.04.18 plus cost of freight involved.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>','<p>Further to interest sought in Form M in separate complaint, we seek&nbsp; compensation for mental anguish&nbsp; at my old age of 61 plus of&nbsp; Rs. 10 lacs and reimbursement of rent being paid for hiring&nbsp; &nbsp;alternate accommodation @ Rs. 26000 per month at Suncity Parikarma in Sector 20 Panchkula from 01.04.18 plus cost of freight involved.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>',9697570.00,9249570.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','0','','2018-01-04 00:00:00','2018-01-04 00:00:00','10171, carpet area 209.59 sq meter. ','','',1,0,0,0,'JBchandan','2018-10-29 17:37:20.000','JBchandan','2018-10-29 17:37:20.000'),(162,1060,'1060',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-30 19:48:52.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','1','344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','Motia Developers, Private Limited','M/s Motia Developers, Private Limited','info@motiagroup.com',8558844525,0,'Chandigarh - Ambala Highway,','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Chandigarh - Ambala Highway,','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿</span><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">a</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">.\r\nApplicants are husband and wife and joint allottees of the unit 31B-3<sup>rd</sup>\r\nFloor as per Allotment Letter dated Feb 5,2016 (Annexure 1). They have made\r\nfull payment except for the amount due at the time of possession (for details Annexure\r\n2)</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">\r\nRespondent has committed to hand over possession of the unit on or before Feb\r\n4, 2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of allotment in the Buyers Agreement/Agreement\r\nof Sale (relevant page of agreement at Annexure 3) but has failed to deliver\r\npossession by the stipulated date which is evident from his letter dated Feb 7,\r\n2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">The project is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so\r\ncalled Completion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5)\r\nbut it certifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy (cf. ‘</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman;color:#231F20\">completion certificate’ and\r\n‘occupancy certificate’ definitions in the Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2016, <i>henceforth called\r\nthe Real Estate Act,</i> - Section 2, clause (q) and (zf) respectively).</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">The most important fact and bottom line is that Respondent\r\nhas not given possession by the stipulated date irrespective of his position on\r\ncompletion. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\"> Applicants have served a Legal\r\nNotice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent (Annexure 6) He has been requested\r\nto refund the received amount of Rs. 42, 50,362.00 with interest plus\r\ncompensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice. The notice was\r\nreceived on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> The project is an ongoing project and it is now\r\nwell settled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgements of\r\nthe Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer, Punjab.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Applicants submit that the application has a legal flaw - claim for refund of amount with interest and compensation has been submitted in one Form N. They withdraw the application and request for permission to file&nbsp; afresh one for the claim of refund of Amount with Interest in Form M and subsequently another for Compensation in Form N.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><br></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B - 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh - Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',1,1,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-10-30 19:48:25.000','kssidhu','2018-10-30 19:48:25.000'),(163,1067,'1067',1192,'fd81b4d3-2fe8-488a-b353-63b880719945','FormTypeN',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','DAYA  SAGAR','7739959887daya@gmail.com',7903312315,0,0,'Flat No A 501; Jalvayu Towers','Sector 125; sunny Enclave, Mohali',28,507,'140401','1','SCO NO 64- 65; 3rd floor, union bank of India','Sector 17; bank square, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0114','Hero homes','Sunil Kant munjal','gurjeet.singh@herorealty.in',0,0,'264, ground floor, Okhla industrial area,','Phase 3; new delhi',10,120,'110020','1','264, ground floor, Okhla industrial area,','Phase 3; new delhi',10,120,'110020','1','<div dir=\"auto\">We booked a flat in hero homes mohali flat no 503 tower 8 in the name of daya sagar by paying 2.5 lakhs of token money.&nbsp;</div><div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Within a week we came to know that company has included the credit input in discount without disclosing the fact. When we made complain regarding hiding this fact they are not giving any answer. When we told him to refund the amount , hero home is saying amount is forfeited. However there is no legal agreement made between hero homes mohali and me.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Thus company has cheated us and not refunding our money. Please do the needful so that we could get the money back.</span><br style=\"font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\"></div><div><span style=\"font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 12.8px;\"><br></span></div>','<p>Refund of booking amount of 2.5 lakhs with 18% of compound interest.</p>',6500000.00,250000.00,'2018-11-03 00:00:00.000','2018-11-03 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-11-03 00:00:00','2018-11-03 00:00:00','Flat no 503, tower 8, hero homes , mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'Joy0909','2018-11-03 23:41:34.000','Joy0909','2018-11-03 23:41:34.000'),(164,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 15:35:54.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA\r\nVillage Budmajra,\r\nKharar, Sector 121,\r\nS.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd ','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I purchased an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt.\r\nLtd. The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized\r\n2400 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.9158000/- Plus taxes.\r\nI’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the company. I paid Rs.50,000/-\r\non dated 31/1/2017, Rs.5,00,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. The\r\nCompany, executed Apartment Buyer Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of\r\nthe flat in question, on 9<sup>th</sup> February, 2017. The builder/company\r\npromised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017.\r\nHowever, the company reserved a grace period of 3 months for possession of the\r\napartment. Thus the effective date of possession was March 2018. Unfortunately,\r\ndespite having paid 95% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver\r\nthe possession of the flat. I have taken a home loan from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying\r\nhuge amount of interest, every month.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I\'ve been visiting the builder / company office and contacting\r\nthe officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and to\r\nknow the actual date of possession, to no avail though.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">That as per the allotment letter cum agreement, the\r\ncompany is charging penal interest from the buyers <b><u>@12% &nbsp;to &nbsp;&nbsp;18% per annum</u></b>, for delay in making\r\npayment, as and when demanded by the builder/company. I’ve paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- to the company.\r\nHowever, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for\r\nno rhyme or reason. The builder has neither offered possession yet, nor paid\r\nany compensation as per the provisions of RERA. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Thus I seek parity &amp; equity between the interest paid\r\nby the buyer &amp; the interest paid by the builder/company. The interest that\r\nthe builder/company ought to pay as compensation, should be at par with what\r\nthey charge from the helpless buyers. Here it also worth mentioning that during\r\nthis entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or\r\ncircumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company\r\nmight try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. <b><u>RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>\r\nI seek Compensation as per the relevant provisions of RERA, for inordinate\r\ndelay in possession, even after having paid Rs. 88,30,492/- amounting to over 95% of\r\nthe total sale consideration.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2018-11-13 14:13:08.000','rachnabhi','2018-11-13 14:13:08.000'),(165,1046,'1046',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-09-27 07:47:23.000','DAKSHA','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'H. NO. 1/3 BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','1','H. NO. 1/3 BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','RAVINDER PAL SINGH','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0076','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','info@ansalapi.com',0,0,'SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','<p>Respondents came up with commercial project as CITI CENTRE at Sector 115 Mohali. </p><p>Husband of the complainant appraoched the Respondents for booking of one showroom floated by the Respondent. </p><p>Respondents also allured the Complainant of ASSURED RETURNS on the amount invested till the date of possession. </p><p>Initially complainant booked one showroom bearing No. 6UGF measuring 1772 sq. ft. @ Rs.30,12,400/-. </p><p>Agreement executed on 09.02.2010 (A-2) </p><p>Complainant deposited Rs.28,61,780/- on 30.01.2010.</p><p>Agreement executed on 09.02.2010 promising possession within 42 months maximum.&nbsp;</p><p> </p><p>Respondent was liable to pay Rs.53,847/- per month which was paid by 31.03.2012. </p><p>Since the construction of the showroom was very slow complainant decided to shift in other showroom in same project.</p><p> Respondent offered two showrooms bearing no. 03SF and 04SF. </p><p>Present case is pertains to showroom No. 03SF. </p><p>Complainant paid Rs.20,00,000/- more on 25.05.2012. </p><p>Price of each showroom was fixed as Rs.25,00,000/-. Each unit is measuring 1588 sq. ft. </p><p>Complainant paid total Rs.48,61,780/- till date for both showrooms.</p><p>New Agreement of SF03 showroom executed on 08.06.2012&nbsp; wherein possession was to be given within 42 months maximum which expired on 08.12.2016.</p><p>Construction has been stopped in between. Possession not offered till date.</p><p>Assured Returns stopped after JULY, 2016 violating the terms of the agreement as well as provisions of RERA Act.</p><p>Respondents are in arrears of Rs.9,94,588/- (01.07.2016 to 31.10.2018) as ASSURED RETURN and they may be directed to deposit the said amount as interim measure.</p><p>Present application filed seeking possession of the Unit No.03SF alongwith assured returns till actual possession of unit.</p>','<p>SEEKING POSSESSION OF THE UNIT NO. 03SF, CITI&nbsp; CENTRE PROJECT, SECTOR 115 MOHALI </p><p>ASSURED RETURN AMOUNTING TO RS.9,94,588/- DUE W.E.F. 01.07.2016 TILL 31.08.2018 </p><p>FUTURE ASSURED RETURNS TILL ACTUAL POSSESSION OF SHOWROOM No.03SF. </p><p>COMPENSATION OF RS.15,00,000/- AND RS,1,10,000/- AS COST OF LITIGATION.&nbsp;</p>',2500000.00,2430890.00,'2015-06-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-06-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','03 SF, CITY CENTRE, SECTOR 115 MOHALI, ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT LTD','','',2,0,0,0,'advravinder','2018-11-13 22:57:59.000','advravinder','2018-11-13 22:57:59.000'),(166,1046,'1046',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 23:02:48.000','DAKSHA','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'H. NO. 1/3 BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','1','H. NO. 1/3 BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','RAVINDER PAL SINGH','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0076','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','info@ansalapi.com',0,0,'SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','<p>Respondents came up with commercial project as CITI CENTRE at Sector 115 Mohali. </p><p>Husband of the complainant appraoched the Respondents for booking of one showroom floated by the Respondent. </p><p>Respondents also allured the