\r\ndelayed period of 72 months.</span><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 54pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the respondents was issued a demand notice\r\namounting to</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;6, 64,288<b>/- (p36)</b></span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;to the claimant along with the offer of possession without\r\nadjusting the amount of compensation.</span></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 54pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">The claimant is paying an installment&nbsp;of Rs 4600/- P.M\r\nto HDFC on a/c of availed loan that includes Rs 42000/- as interest component .</li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 54pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">The claimant is middle class salaried person having no property.</li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 54pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">The family paid house rent Rs 13500/ to <span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Rs 18000/- P.M during the period of delay by the respondents. Thus the\r\nclaimant has suffered financial loss of more than 12 lacs due to delay in\r\npossession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>','The claimant should be given compensation covering financial loss and loss on a/c of mental agony due to delay in offering possession as per the provisions of the rera.',2458727.00,1978144.00,'2012-11-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2009-08-26 00:00:00','2009-11-12 00:00:00','UNIT NO.15, BLOCK B, SINGLETON FLOOR SECTOR 107 UNIWORLD CITY MOHALI','','',1,1,0,0,'lovely','2018-12-03 11:16:08.000','lovely','2018-12-03 11:16:08.000'),(187,1079,'1079',1216,'11d722ae-bbbb-479b-bed1-c40adf90f1de','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswant  Singh','sjaswants803@gmail.com',9466694194,0,0,'85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','1','85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0316','Green Valley Heights','Harbans Lal Singla','greenvalleyheights2010@yahoo.co.in',9876718666,0,'M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','<p>na</p>','<p>na</p>',2850000.00,3046384.00,'2015-01-14 00:00:00.000','2018-07-13 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-10-15 00:00:00','2013-02-08 00:00:00','512,fifth floor, tower xii, green valley heights, zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 12:25:23.000','jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 12:25:23.000'),(188,1079,'1079',1216,'11d722ae-bbbb-479b-bed1-c40adf90f1de','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-03 12:47:45.000','Jaswant  Singh','sjaswants803@gmail.com',9466694194,0,0,'85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','1','85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0316','Green Valley Heights','Harbans Lal Singla','greenvalleyheights2010@yahoo.co.in',9876718666,0,'M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:49.5pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;\">(i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">I booked a 2 BHK residential Flat of <st1:metricconverter productid=\"1285 sq. ft\" w:st=\"on\">1285 sq. ft</st1:metricconverter>. area in\r\ngreen valley heights for rupees 28,50,000/- on 11.7,2011 by paying 10% i.e. Rs.\r\n2,85,000/- and provisionally allotted with flat No. 512 vide application /\r\ninitial agreement dated 28-09-2011 and subsequently on 15-10- 2011, I was\r\nallotted with flat No. <st1:metricconverter productid=\"512 in\" w:st=\"on\">512 in</st1:metricconverter>\r\nGreen Valley Heights dated 15-10-2011. As per the allotment letter I was\r\npromised the delivery of semi-furnished flat within three years from the date\r\nof booking/allotment. On <st1:date year=\"2013\" day=\"2\" month=\"8\" ls=\"trans\" w:st=\"on\">8-2-2013</st1:date> respondent(s) handed over a printed Buyer’s\r\napartment agreement after the delay of 19 months from date of booking. The\r\ndelay in providing this agreement letter was deliberate and a tactics on the\r\npart of respondents as this document should have been executed within\r\nreasonable time along with allotment. This is unfair trade practice.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:49.5pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:49.5pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;\">(ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">On 30-4-2016 respondents issued me a\r\nletter in haste for offer of possession without completing it &amp; without\r\nobtaining CC and OC but actual physical possession was given on 13-07-2018. I\r\nhad cleared all dues on 09-05-2017 and obtained “No dues certificate”. My\r\nrequest letters and Emails dated 23-0516, 27-03-17,30-08-17 and all other\r\nefforts were neglected by the respondents for delay compensation and other\r\nreliefs along with possession. Thus on 15-4-2017 I served the respondents legal\r\nnotice through my attorney to substantiate my claims.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The\r\n</span></b><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">following</span></b><b><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> reliefs and compensations may be\r\nawarded:-<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:13.5pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(i) Cost of litigation Rs 50,000/- as the\r\ncomplaint has paid Rs.5500/- for legal notice and incurred expenditure on legal\r\nconsultation &amp; processing. (ii)Rs. 50,000/- to attend cases in RERA\r\nfrom26-09-2017 when the case was initially filled to till 13-11-2018 at least\r\n15 attendance so far.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:13.5pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">(iii)Rs 2,50,000/- for mental agony and\r\nharassment as the respondent kept on toes the complainant without any fault of\r\nhim for more than seven years from 11-07-2011 to 13-07-2018. (iv) Compensation\r\nof Rs. 50,000/-for visiting the site at least for two dozen of times.(v)\r\nCompensation for unfair trade practices of Rs 50,000/- for delay of 19 months\r\nin executing agreement and not providing cc,oc before offer of possession and\r\nall other relevant documents. (vi) Interest on the compensation due as on\r\n13-07-2018 date of physical possession to till the decision of the case.(vii) The\r\nrespondents charged 141946/-additional illegally, unreasonable and without\r\napproval of appropriate authority without my consent for 64 sq. ft. (viii) The\r\nrespondent also charged extra&nbsp; Rs.24000/-\r\nand Rs.5000/- for upvc windows &amp; gas connection fittings as a hidden\r\ncharges which the respondents are required to refund with interest. (ix) The\r\nrespondents modified/altered the project without the proper permission or authority.\r\nNo break up of flat area provided, in case it is deficient may be compensated.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:13.5pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale AMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">(v) Interim order may\r\nkindly be passed in favor of complainant for any other reliefs hon’ble\r\nauthority deem fit.</span><br></p>',2850000.00,3046384.00,'2015-01-14 00:00:00.000','2018-07-13 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-10-15 00:00:00','2013-02-08 00:00:00','512,fifth floor, tower xii, green valley heights, zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 12:28:20.000','jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 12:28:20.000'),(189,1080,'1080',1240,'a29ccb2a-7316-46f6-826d-024d9eaa180c','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Col. Jagjit Singh Randhawa','jagjit1919@gmail.com',7597383970,0,0,'House no. 818, Phase 7, Sector 61','',28,507,'160062','0','House no. 333, Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex (MDC)','',13,15,'134114','Adv. Livleen SIngh','livleen.singh@legacylawoffices.com',9914533339,1722559332,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0143','Parkwood Glade\r\nTower A,B,C,D\r\nand G','Parkwood Developers Private Limited','mail@parkwoodgroup.in',0,0,'Parkwood Developers Private Limited, 10th Floor, Hemkunt Chambers','89, Nehru Place',10,429,'110019','1','Parkwood Developers Private Limited, 10th Floor, Hemkunt Chambers','89, Nehru Place',10,429,'110019','1','<p>ABCD&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>','<p>ABCD</p>',3995500.00,3947721.00,'2014-07-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-01-07 00:00:00','2012-01-07 00:00:00','Unit No. D-202, Block ‘D’, Parkwood Glade, Sector 116, Kharar-Landran Road, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'JagjitSingh','2018-12-03 15:15:51.000','JagjitSingh','2018-12-03 15:15:51.000'),(190,1080,'1080',1240,'a29ccb2a-7316-46f6-826d-024d9eaa180c','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Col. Jagjit Singh Randhawa','jagjit1919@gmail.com',7597383970,0,0,'House no. 818, Phase 7, Sector 61','',28,507,'160062','0','House no. 333, Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex (MDC)','',13,15,'134114','Adv. Livleen SIngh','livleen.singh@legacylawoffices.com',9914533339,1722559332,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0143','Parkwood Glade\r\nTower A,B,C,D\r\nand G','Parkwood Developers Private Limited','mail@parkwoodgroup.in',0,0,'Parkwood Developers Private Limited, 10th Floor, Hemkunt Chambers','89, Nehru Place',10,429,'110019','1','Parkwood Developers Private Limited, 10th Floor, Hemkunt Chambers','89, Nehru Place',10,429,'110019','1','<p>abcd</p>','<p>ABCD</p>',3995500.00,3947721.00,'2014-07-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-01-07 00:00:00','2012-01-07 00:00:00','Unit No. D-202, Block ‘D’, Parkwood Glade, Sector 116, Kharar-Landran Road, Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'JagjitSingh','2018-12-03 15:52:43.000','JagjitSingh','2018-12-03 15:52:43.000'),(191,1050,'1050',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-10 16:54:14.000','Amarjit Kaur','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','1','House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','THE PALM','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,0,'SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n106%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That\r\nthe husband of the applicant initially booked four plots with the respondent\r\nhaving different sizes, two of them measuring 500 Square yards each @ Rs. 18,500/-\r\nin the project “Palm Garden” and two of them measuring 250 Square Yards each @ Rs.\r\n18,000 per Sq. yard in the project “Palm Spring”, Mullanpur (New Chandigarh),\r\nnear Chandigarh being developed by the respondent.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">The booking amount against the plots was directly paid to\r\nthe company by the applicant. Before purchasing these plots, the applicant\r\ncontacted the respondent who assured them that it was having all the approvals\r\nand sanctions for the said project and possession of the plot will be delivered\r\nwithin 2 years.&nbsp; It was assured to the\r\napplicant that the possession of the plots will be delivered within 2 years and\r\nthe buyer’s agreement will be executed within 3-4 months.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">That thereafter the husband of the applicant visited the\r\nproject site in the month of June, 2013 and was shocked to see that only open\r\nfields were there and the respondent had not started any development. On the\r\nsame day the applicant visited the office of respondent who assured the\r\napplicant that development will be started soon and the further payment would\r\nbe demanded when the development work would be started.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That\r\nthereafter the husband of the applicant died in September, 2016 and the Plots\r\nwere transferred in the name of applicant.&nbsp;</span><b style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Century Gothic&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">That the applicant after the death of her husband, visited\r\nthe site of the project and saw no development at the site and asked the\r\nrespondent to refund the amount but respondents showed their inability to\r\nrefund the amount and persuaded the applicant that she should get the deposited\r\namount adjusted into a single plot.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That\r\nthereafter, the amount of the applicant was adjusted against the one plot and\r\nPlot no. 418 measuring 402.32 Sq. yds. (Approx.) was allotted to the applicant\r\non 24.05.2018. That the respondent thereafter in June, 2018 offered Plot Buyer’s Agreement for execution.</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Compensation of Rs. 10 lacs relying upon the provision of Section 18 of Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016.&nbsp;</span></b><font face=\"Century Gothic, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\"><b>as the applicants have lost faith in the respondent due&nbsp;</b></span></font><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">to misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during all these years and thus&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">the applicant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of various&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">respondent collected the money from the applicants in 2012. The approvals were granted to the&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">respondent on the ground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving 100% of sale&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">consideration the respondent did not execute any sale agreement and the same was executed after a&nbsp;</b><font face=\"Century Gothic, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\"><b>delay of more than 6 years and after having received more than 100% of the sale consideration.</b></span></font><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">&nbsp;A separate complaint under Form M is being filed seeking refund of amount deposited alongwith interest with the respondent.</span></b></p>',8472457.00,9562500.00,'2014-02-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-05-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','418','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2018-12-04 18:12:57.000','BeeG','2018-12-04 18:12:57.000'),(192,1050,'1050',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-04 18:24:22.000','Amarjit Kaur','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','1','House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','THE PALM','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,0,'SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n106%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That\r\nthe husband of the applicant initially booked four plots with the respondent\r\nhaving different sizes, two of them measuring 500 Square yards each @ Rs. 18,500/-\r\nin the project “Palm Garden” and two of them measuring 250 Square Yards each @ Rs.\r\n18,000 per Sq. yard in the project “Palm Spring”, Mullanpur (New Chandigarh),\r\nnear Chandigarh being developed by the respondent.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">The booking amount against the plots was directly paid to\r\nthe company by the applicant. Before purchasing these plots, the applicant\r\ncontacted the respondent who assured them that it was having all the approvals\r\nand sanctions for the said project and possession of the plot will be delivered\r\nwithin 2 years.&nbsp; It was assured to the\r\napplicant that the possession of the plots will be delivered within 2 years and\r\nthe buyer’s agreement will be executed within 3-4 months.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">That thereafter the husband of the applicant visited the\r\nproject site in the month of June, 2013 and was shocked to see that only open\r\nfields were there and the respondent had not started any development. On the\r\nsame day the applicant visited the office of respondent who assured the\r\napplicant that development will be started soon and the further payment would\r\nbe demanded when the development work would be started.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That\r\nthereafter the husband of the applicant died in September, 2016 and the Plots\r\nwere transferred in the name of applicant.&nbsp;</span><b style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Century Gothic&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">That the applicant after the death of her husband, visited\r\nthe site of the project and saw no development at the site and asked the\r\nrespondent to refund the amount but respondents showed their inability to\r\nrefund the amount and persuaded the applicant that she should get the deposited\r\namount adjusted into a single plot.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That\r\nthereafter, the amount of the applicant was adjusted against the one plot and\r\nPlot no. 418 measuring 402.32 Sq. yds. (Approx.) was allotted to the applicant\r\non 24.05.2018. That the respondent thereafter in June, 2018 offered Plot Buyer’s Agreement for execution.</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:.9pt;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:.5in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:0in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Compensation of Rs. 10 lacs relying upon the provision of Section 18 of Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016.&nbsp;</span></b><font face=\"Century Gothic, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\"><b>as the applicants have lost faith in the respondent due&nbsp;</b></span></font><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">to misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during all these years and thus&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">the applicant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of various&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">respondent collected the money from the applicants in 2012. The approvals were granted to the&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">respondent on the ground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving 100% of sale&nbsp;</b><b style=\"font-size: 18.6667px; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">consideration the respondent did not execute any sale agreement and the same was executed after a&nbsp;</b><font face=\"Century Gothic, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\"><b>delay of more than 6 years and after having received more than 100% of the sale consideration.</b></span></font><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">&nbsp;A separate complaint under Form M is being filed seeking refund of amount deposited alongwith interest with the respondent.</span></b></p>',8472457.00,9562500.00,'2014-02-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-05-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','418','','',1,1,0,0,'BeeG','2018-12-04 18:16:47.000','BeeG','2018-12-04 18:16:47.000'),(193,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 15:35:54.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA\r\nVillage Budmajra,\r\nKharar, Sector 121,\r\nS.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd ','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I purchased an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt.\r\nLtd. The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized\r\n2400 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.9158000/- Plus taxes.\r\nI’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the company. I paid Rs.50,000/-\r\non dated 31/1/2017, Rs.49,50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. The\r\nCompany, executed Apartment Buyer Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of\r\nthe flat in question, on 9<sup>th</sup> February, 2017. The builder/company\r\npromised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017.\r\nHowever, the company reserved a grace period of 3 months for possession of the\r\napartment. Thus the effective date of possession was March 2018. Unfortunately,\r\ndespite having paid 95% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver\r\nthe possession of the flat. I have taken a home loan from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying\r\nhuge amount of interest, every month.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I\'ve been visiting the builder / company office and contacting\r\nthe officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and to\r\nknow the actual date of possession, to no avail though.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">That as per the allotment letter cum agreement, the\r\ncompany is charging penal interest from the buyers <b><u>@12% &nbsp;to &nbsp;&nbsp;18% per annum</u></b>, for delay in making\r\npayment, as and when demanded by the builder/company. I’ve paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- to the company.\r\nHowever, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for\r\nno rhyme or reason. The builder has neither offered possession yet, nor paid\r\nany COMPENSATION AS PER THE PROVISIONS OF RERA. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Here it also worth mentioning that during\r\nthis entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or\r\ncircumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company\r\nmight try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u><br></u></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u>&nbsp; &nbsp; RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">FOR INORDINATE DELAY IN POSSESSION&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp;OR&nbsp; COMPENSATION, AS PER THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF RERA. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; I HAVE PAID RS.88,30,492/- WHICH AMOUNTS TO OVER 95% OF THE TOTAL SALE CONSIDERATION, SINCE ALMOST 2 YEARS</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2018-12-05 14:01:16.000','rachnabhi','2018-12-05 14:01:16.000'),(194,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 15:35:54.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA\r\nVillage Budmajra,\r\nKharar, Sector 121,\r\nS.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd ','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I purchased an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt.\r\nLtd. The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized\r\n2400 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.9158000/- Plus taxes.\r\nI’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the company. I paid Rs.50,000/-\r\non dated 31/1/2017, Rs.49,50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. The\r\nCompany, executed Apartment Buyer Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of\r\nthe flat in question, on 9<sup>th</sup> February, 2017. The builder/company\r\npromised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017.\r\nHowever, the company reserved a grace period of 3 months for possession of the\r\napartment. Thus the effective date of possession was March 2018. Unfortunately,\r\ndespite having paid 95% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver\r\nthe possession of the flat.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;Here it is also pertinent to mention that I have taken a HOME LOAN from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying\r\nhuge amount of interest, every month. Here it is also relevant to mention that since I have taken home loan from HDFC, all the documents like allotment letter, apartment buyer agreement, payment receipts&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">pertaining to the flat unit in question</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">were handed over by the builder company directly to the bank/financier. The builder company only handed over Copy of Apartment Buyer Agreement to me and no other document whatsoever.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I\'ve been visiting the builder / company office and contacting\r\nthe officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and to\r\nknow the actual date of possession, to no avail though.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">That as per the allotment letter cum agreement, the\r\ncompany is charging penal interest from the buyers <b><u>@12% &nbsp;to &nbsp;&nbsp;18% per annum</u></b>, for delay in making\r\npayment, as and when demanded by the builder/company. I’ve paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- to the company.\r\nHowever, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for\r\nno rhyme or reason. The builder has neither offered possession yet, nor paid\r\nany COMPENSATION AS PER THE PROVISIONS OF RERA. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Here it also worth mentioning that during\r\nthis entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or\r\ncircumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company\r\nmight try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u><br></u></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u>&nbsp; &nbsp; RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">FOR INORDINATE DELAY IN POSSESSION&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp;OR&nbsp; COMPENSATION, AS PER THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF RERA. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; I HAVE PAID RS.88,30,492/- WHICH AMOUNTS TO OVER 95% OF THE TOTAL SALE CONSIDERATION, SINCE ALMOST 2 YEARS</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2018-12-05 14:18:07.000','rachnabhi','2018-12-05 14:18:07.000'),(195,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-05 14:18:45.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA\r\nVillage Budmajra,\r\nKharar, Sector 121,\r\nS.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd ','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I purchased an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt.\r\nLtd. The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized\r\n2400 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.9158000/- Plus taxes.\r\nI’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the company. I paid Rs.50,000/-\r\non dated 31/1/2017, Rs.49,50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. The\r\nCompany, executed Apartment Buyer Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of\r\nthe flat in question, on 9<sup>th</sup> February, 2017. The builder/company\r\npromised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017.\r\nHowever, the company reserved a grace period of 3 months for possession of the\r\napartment. Thus the effective date of possession was March 2018. Unfortunately,\r\ndespite having paid 95% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver\r\nthe possession of the flat.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;Here it is also pertinent to mention that I have taken a HOME LOAN from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying\r\nhuge amount of interest, every month. Here it is also relevant to mention that since I have taken home loan from HDFC, all the documents like allotment letter, apartment buyer agreement, payment receipts&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">pertaining to the flat unit in question</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">were handed over by the builder company directly to the bank/financier. The builder company only handed over Copy of Apartment Buyer Agreement to me and no other document whatsoever.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I\'ve been visiting the builder / company office and contacting\r\nthe officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and to\r\nknow the actual date of possession, to no avail though.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">That as per the allotment letter cum agreement, the\r\ncompany is charging penal interest from the buyers <b><u>@12% &nbsp;to &nbsp;&nbsp;18% per annum</u></b>, for delay in making\r\npayment, as and when demanded by the builder/company. I’ve paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- to the company.\r\nHowever, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for\r\nno rhyme or reason. The builder has neither offered possession yet, nor paid\r\nany COMPENSATION AS PER THE PROVISIONS OF RERA. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Here it also worth mentioning that during\r\nthis entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or\r\ncircumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company\r\nmight try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u><br></u></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u>&nbsp; &nbsp; RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">FOR INORDINATE DELAY IN POSSESSION&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp;OR&nbsp; COMPENSATION, AS PER THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF RERA. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; I HAVE PAID RS.88,30,492/- WHICH AMOUNTS TO OVER 95% OF THE TOTAL SALE CONSIDERATION, SINCE ALMOST 2 YEARS</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2018-12-05 14:18:42.000','rachnabhi','2018-12-05 14:18:42.000'),(196,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222427,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-06 14:21:54.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-06 14:21:54.000'),(197,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222427,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.The Respondent had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014. A statement showing the account status of the respondent reflecting the amount of plot is annexed as Annexure C/1.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondent had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”). A copy of the Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondent is being annexed to the instant complaint as Annexure C/2. As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter.</p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 but it should have been calculated from first date of payment made i.e from 05.03.2014..&nbsp;</p><p>3.The respondent had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now more than 5 lakhs. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondent as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/2 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>4.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month.</p><div><br></div>','<p>abc</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-06 14:23:55.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-06 14:23:55.000'),(198,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222427,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.The Respondent had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014. A statement showing the account status of the respondent reflecting the amount of plot is annexed as Annexure C/1.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondent had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”). A copy of the Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondent is being annexed to the instant complaint as Annexure C/2. As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter.</p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 but it should have been calculated from first date of payment made i.e from 05.03.2014..&nbsp;</p><p>3.The respondent had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now more than 5 lakhs. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondent as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/2 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>4.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month.</p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to direct the respondent to complete the Allotted Unit in all respects by providing the requisite amenities and facilities as per the terms and conditions of the Allotment Letter dated 20.06.2014 and the specifications of the Allotted Unit as appended therewith and thereafter handover its actual physical possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to restrain the respondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the Complainant.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-06 14:25:40.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-06 14:25:40.000'),(199,1078,'1078',1148,'d6b33f13-0c3f-4ab1-b43d-e6d1dcd0a882','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-25 11:33:06.000','DEEPAK GARG','cadeepakgarg@gmail.com',9855519149,1724641410,0,'HOUSE NO 3003','TRIBUNE SOCIETY SECTOR 50 D',6,128,'160047','1','HOUSE NO 3003','TRIBUNE SOCIETY SECTOR 50 D',6,128,'160047','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','EMAIL@ATSGREENS.COM',0,0,'SITE OFFICE ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED, SECTOR 121','NEAR VERKA MILK PLANT, MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','SITE OFFICE ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED, SECTOR 121','NEAR VERKA MILK PLANT, MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>FACT OF CASE:</span></u></b></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>Booking:</span></u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'> On 9<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup> April, 2017, We ( Deepak Garg &amp; Shilpa Gupta) had\r\nbooked a residential flat (3+1<span style=\"margin: 0px;\">&nbsp; </span>BHK, Type\r\nB, Flat No 7032, Floor 3<sup><font size=\"2\">rd</font></sup>, Tower 7<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup>) by giving an\r\nadvance of Rs. 5,00,000/- (receipt no. CSAMR/03150 dt. 13<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup> April,\r\n2017) FOR Rs. 98,78,000/-</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>Execution of Agreement</span></u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>: the 30 (Thirty) page apartment buyer agreement\r\nwas duly executed on dated 11<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup> May, 2017, wherein date of\r\nCompletion of Construction was described as December 2017 with a grace period\r\nof 3 Months. (Refer para 6.2 on page 12 of said agreement).</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>Payments made till date</span></u><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>: Total amount till date was paid against Basic\r\nCost is Rs. 85,71,866/- along with service tax of Rs. 385734/-</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\'>Possession not handed over:-<span style=\"margin: 0px;\">&nbsp; </span>Even after passing of Eleven (11) Months from\r\nthe date of completion mentioned in agreement the completion of property is\r\nstill under construction and possession letter is not offered. </span