 execute agreement.Then the respondent telephonically informed the applicant that it will sell the plot at premium of Rs. 2000 per sq yd and refund the amount to him, And for that purpose also asked the bank detail,which was duly sent by the applicant vide email dated 21.08.18(C6).The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and development.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to applicant.A list of dates of approvals C7 and some important approvals as C8 &amp; C9 \r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs\r\nfor deficiency in services, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the\r\napplicant and for using the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long\r\nperiod. Inspite of repeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did\r\nnot issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date. The\r\nrespondent was not having approval when the plot was sold to the applicant. As\r\nper the approvals and sanctions, the respondent was barred from collecting the\r\nmoney from public till exemption u/s 44 is received, which was infact received\r\non 25.01.2017.&nbsp;That the&nbsp; conduct of the opposite party in not\r\ndelivering the possession of the plot in a time bound manner, not doing\r\ndevelopment on the site, booking the plot in question without obtaining any\r\napproval and permissions, not issuing any allotment letter to the applicant,\r\nnot executing the buyer’s agreement&nbsp;&nbsp;even after receiving about 30%\r\nof the total cost of plot, misrepresented the applicant during all these years\r\nabout the approvals and sanctions and also about the development, demanding\r\nmore money in the shape of IDC which it cannot do, has caused and is causing\r\nmental harassment and the applicant is suffering huge financial loss due to\r\nnon-allotment and non-delivery of possession of the said plot.The respondent is\r\nliable to pay Rs. 10 lacs&nbsp;for causing financial loss, escalation in prices\r\nand on account of mental and physical harassment and agony besides litigation\r\nexpenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><br clear=\"all\">\r\n&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><br></p>',5000000.00,1500000.00,'2015-10-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-10-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','no allotment & Agreement yet','','',1,1,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2018-12-11 22:16:29.000','rerafilingformn','2018-12-11 22:16:29.000'),(225,1061,'1061',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-22 18:39:51.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134109','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/S MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE & CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','Complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked(C-1)a 350 sq yards plot @ RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC)from the respondent in the project Palm Springs, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured by respondent that it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained within 2-3 months &amp; the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2 years.The applicant paid Rs. 1890000 i.e. 30% of total sale consideration.Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yard plot instead of 350 sq yard &amp; accordingly requested(C-2) respondent to change the size of plot. The said request was accepted. Out of the amount of Rs. 1890000, respondent adjusted Rs. 1350000/- i.e. 30 % sale consideration towards 250 sq yrd plot @ Rs 18000 per sq yrd and only refunded Rs. 490000(C-3) instead of Rs. 540000.The respondent issued an acknowledgement(C-4) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it arbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed between the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened the applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid. Also in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/- instead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust remaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.Inspite of number of visits, repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-5) was also sent to it but to no avail.The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and the development . It had not even applied the permissions when the plot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals along with the dates when the same were applied and obtained is attached as C-6 and some important approvals as C-7 &amp; C-8.The respondent was not having approval or sanction for collecting money','<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:15.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing the respondent\r\nto pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade\r\npractices and harassment caused to the applicant and for using the hard earned\r\nmoney of the applicant for such a long period. Inspite of repeated requests\r\nvisits by the applicant the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and\r\nexecute the buyer\'s agreement till date. The respondent was not having approval\r\nwhen the plot was sold to the applicant. As per the approvals and sanctions,\r\nthe respondent was barred from collecting the money from public till exemption\r\nu/s 44 is received, which was infact received on 25.01.2017.&nbsp;That\r\nthe&nbsp; conduct of the respondent in not delivering the possession of the\r\nplot in a time bound manner, not doing development on the site, booking the\r\nplot in question without obtaining any approval and permissions, not issuing\r\nany allotment letter to the applicant, not executing the buyer’s agreement&nbsp;&nbsp;even\r\nafter receiving more than 30% of the total cost of plot, misrepresented the\r\napplicant during all these years about the approvals and sanctions and also\r\nabout the development, demanding more money in the shape of IDC which it cannot\r\ndo, has caused and is causing mental harassment and the applicant is suffering huge\r\nfinancial loss due to non-allotment and non-delivery of possession of the said\r\nplot.The respondent is liable to pay Rs. 10 lacs&nbsp;for causing financial\r\nloss, escalation in prices and on account of mental and physical harassment and\r\nagony besides litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:15.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p></div>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'2013-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-02-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-12-11 23:32:41.000','Ramantakiar','2018-12-11 23:32:41.000'),(226,1061,'1061',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-11 23:33:12.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134109','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/S MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE & CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','SECTOR-17C',6,128,'160017','1','Complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked(C-1)a 350 sq yards plot @ RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC)from the respondent in the project Palm Springs, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured by respondent that it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained within 2-3 months &amp; the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2 years.The applicant paid Rs. 1890000 i.e. 30% of total sale consideration.Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yard plot instead of 350 sq yard &amp; accordingly requested(C-2) respondent to change the size of plot. The said request was accepted. Out of the amount of Rs. 1890000, respondent adjusted Rs. 1350000/- i.e. 30 % sale consideration towards 250 sq yrd plot @ Rs 18000 per sq yrd and only refunded Rs. 490000(C-3) instead of Rs. 540000.The respondent issued an acknowledgement(C-4) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it arbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed between the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened the applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid. Also in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/- instead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust remaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.Inspite of number of visits, repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-5) was also sent to it but to no avail.The respondent has misrepresented the applicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals and the development . It had not even applied the permissions when the plot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals along with the dates when the same were applied and obtained is attached as C-6 and some important approvals as C-7 &amp; C-8.The respondent was not having approval or sanction for collecting money','<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:15.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing the respondent\r\nto pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade\r\npractices and harassment caused to the applicant and for using the hard earned\r\nmoney of the applicant for such a long period. Inspite of repeated requests\r\nvisits by the applicant the respondent did not issue any allotment letter and\r\nexecute the buyer\'s agreement till date. The respondent was not having approval\r\nwhen the plot was sold to the applicant. As per the approvals and sanctions,\r\nthe respondent was barred from collecting the money from public till exemption\r\nu/s 44 is received, which was infact received on 25.01.2017.&nbsp;That\r\nthe&nbsp; conduct of the respondent in not delivering the possession of the\r\nplot in a time bound manner, not doing development on the site, booking the\r\nplot in question without obtaining any approval and permissions, not issuing\r\nany allotment letter to the applicant, not executing the buyer’s agreement&nbsp;&nbsp;even\r\nafter receiving more than 30% of the total cost of plot, misrepresented the\r\napplicant during all these years about the approvals and sanctions and also\r\nabout the development, demanding more money in the shape of IDC which it cannot\r\ndo, has caused and is causing mental harassment and the applicant is suffering huge\r\nfinancial loss due to non-allotment and non-delivery of possession of the said\r\nplot.The respondent is liable to pay Rs. 10 lacs&nbsp;for causing financial\r\nloss, escalation in prices and on account of mental and physical harassment and\r\nagony besides litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:15.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p></div>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'2013-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-02-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT YET','','',1,1,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-12-11 23:33:10.000','Ramantakiar','2018-12-11 23:33:10.000'),(227,1088,'1088',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','1','Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','Ravikant Choudhary','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA Homes','Bhola Ram Goyal','casahomes2016@gmail.com',0,0,'Future City developers pvt. ltd, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','',28,507,'140307','1','Future City developers pvt. ltd, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4)	That as per clause 7 of the agreement, the possession of the flat was to be handed over to the allottee by 31st March 2018 after obtaining OC, but the OC is still to be produced to us for taking possession of the flat which is clearly an event of default by promoter.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Casa Homes has charged us the payment for\r\n<b>Club House</b> but the same is not even\r\nconstructed. There is no such clause in the agreement which entitles the\r\nbuilder to charge for the facility which is not provided to allotte. It is\r\ntherefore requested to refund us the payment pertaining to club house and\r\ncharge only when it is constructed and handed over to residents.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Casa Homes have charged us GST @12% which has\r\nincreased the cost of our flat. As per the government notification, the cost of\r\nflat should come down even after levying the GST and that extra burden should\r\nnot be passed on the buyers. As we have already paid the GST@12% on approx. 90%\r\nof the cost of Flat, please provide us the receipt of GST paid to the\r\ngovernment so that we can take up the matter separately with the department\r\nconcerned for pursuing our case of GST</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->3)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span><!--[endif]-->Casa Homes have sold this flat on the pretext of\r\ngiving Subvention benefit. The same however has been started in July 2018 but stopped\r\nwef 1<sup>st</sup> Sept 2018 whereas the possession of flat is still not given\r\nto us without assigning any reason thereof</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span><!--[endif]-->That as per the clause ( G ) of the agreement,\r\nCarpet area of the Flat is 1350 SqFt , type 2 BHK on second floor in block D.\r\nFurther Clause 1.2 states that that “the total price for the apartment based on\r\nthe carpet area is 2893340 “and having per sqft rate of INR 2143.21. Further\r\nclause 1.7 states that the promoter shall furnish the details of the carpet\r\narea to ascertain the total price of the apartment. Please furnish the required\r\ndetails so that the final price of the flat can be arrived based on the carpet\r\narea.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">1)&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><o:p><br></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><o:p><br></o:p></p>','<p>1. Compensation on account of delayed possession from 1st April 2018 till the date of producing the occupation certificate as per the Rera rules.</p><p>2. Compensation on account of subvention scheme till the time possession has not been accepted , for which payment has been made by promoter till 31st August 2018 but stopped after that.</p><p>3. Refund ( with interest ) of payment taken by builder on account of Club house as the same is not even constructed</p><p>4. Actual carpet area to be measured jointly by promoter and allotee and accordingly refund / demand balance payment. The carpet area mentioned in the agreement is 1350 Sqft and the same to be handed over to allotee.</p><p>5. Current state of flat portrays substandard quality and workmanship. All substandard material to be replaced like wooden doors/ Tiles/ etc or compensation to be paid.</p><p>6. Decision of GST demanded by promoter.</p>',2893340.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-10-08 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','DDD-3 , Second Foor ,CASA Homes, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','','',2,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2018-12-16 14:52:58.000','Ravikant','2018-12-16 14:52:58.000'),(228,1088,'1088',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-17 13:01:18.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','1','Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA Homes','Bhola Ram Goyal','casahomes2016@gmail.com',0,0,'Future City developers pvt. ltd, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','',28,507,'140307','1','Future City developers pvt. ltd, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4)	That as per clause 7 of the agreement, the possession of the flat was to be handed over to the allottee by 31st March 2018 after obtaining OC, but the OC is still to be produced to us for taking possession of the flat which is clearly an event of default by promoter.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Casa Homes has charged us the payment for\r\n<b>Club House</b> but the same is not even\r\nconstructed. There is no such clause in the agreement which entitles the\r\nbuilder to charge for the facility which is not provided to allotte. It is\r\ntherefore requested to refund us the payment pertaining to club house and\r\ncharge only when it is constructed and handed over to residents.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Casa Homes have charged us GST @12% which has\r\nincreased the cost of our flat. As per the government notification, the cost of\r\nflat should come down even after levying the GST and that extra burden should\r\nnot be passed on the buyers. As we have already paid the GST@12% on approx. 90%\r\nof the cost of Flat, please provide us the receipt of GST paid to the\r\ngovernment so that we can take up the matter separately with the department\r\nconcerned for pursuing our case of GST</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->3)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span><!--[endif]-->Casa Homes have sold this flat on the pretext of\r\ngiving Subvention benefit. The same however has been started in July 2018 but stopped\r\nwef 1<sup>st</sup> Sept 2018 whereas the possession of flat is still not given\r\nto us without assigning any reason thereof</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span><!--[endif]-->That as per the clause ( G ) of the agreement,\r\nCarpet area of the Flat is 1350 SqFt , type 2 BHK on second floor in block D.\r\nFurther Clause 1.2 states that that “the total price for the apartment based on\r\nthe carpet area is 2893340 “and having per sqft rate of INR 2143.21. Further\r\nclause 1.7 states that the promoter shall furnish the details of the carpet\r\narea to ascertain the total price of the apartment. Please furnish the required\r\ndetails so that the final price of the flat can be arrived based on the carpet\r\narea.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">1)&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><o:p><br></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><o:p><br></o:p></p>','<p>1. Compensation on account of delayed possession from 1st April 2018 till the date of producing the occupation certificate as per the Rera rules.</p><p>2. Compensation on account of subvention scheme till the time possession has not been accepted , for which payment has been made by promoter till 31st August 2018 but stopped after that.</p><p>3. Refund ( with interest ) of payment taken by builder on account of Club house as the same is not even constructed</p><p>4. Actual carpet area to be measured jointly by promoter and allotee and accordingly refund / demand balance payment. The carpet area mentioned in the agreement is 1350 Sqft and the same to be handed over to allotee.</p><p>5. Current state of flat portrays substandard quality and workmanship. All substandard material to be replaced like wooden doors/ Tiles/ etc or compensation to be paid.</p><p>6. Decision of GST demanded by promoter.</p>',2893340.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-10-08 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','DDD-3 , Second Foor ,CASA Homes, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','','',2,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2018-12-16 15:20:44.000','Ravikant','2018-12-16 15:20:44.000'),(229,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.The Respondent had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014. A statement showing the account status of the respondent reflecting the amount of plot is annexed as Annexure C/1.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondent had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”). A copy of the Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondent is being annexed to the instant complaint as Annexure C/2. As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter.</p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 but it should have been calculated from first date of payment made i.e from 05.03.2014..&nbsp;</p><p>3.The respondent had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now more than 5 lakhs. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondent as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/2 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>4.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month.</p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to direct the respondent to complete the Allotted Unit in all respects by providing the requisite amenities and facilities as per the terms and conditions of the Allotment Letter dated 20.06.2014 and the specifications of the Allotted Unit as appended therewith and thereafter handover its actual physical possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to restrain the respondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the Complainant.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 17:14:26.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 17:14:26.000'),(230,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.The Respondent had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014. A statement showing the account status of the respondent reflecting the amount of plot is annexed as Annexure C/1.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondent had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”). A copy of the Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondent is being annexed to the instant complaint as Annexure C/2. As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter.</p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 but it should have been calculated from first date of payment made i.e from 05.03.2014..&nbsp;</p><p>3.The respondent had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now more than 5 lakhs. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondent as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/2 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>4.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month.</p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to direct the respondent to complete the Allotted Unit in all respects by providing the requisite amenities and facilities as per the terms and conditions of the Allotment Letter dated 20.06.2014 and the specifications of the Allotted Unit as appended therewith and thereafter handover its actual physical possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to restrain the respondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the Complainant.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 18:50:48.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 18:50:48.000'),(231,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.  The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.  In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”). As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. A statement showing the account status of the respondents reflecting the amount of plot is annexed as Annexure C/1 and Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents as ANNEXURE C/2.</p><p>2.As per Clause 6.