 possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to compensate the Complainant for deficiency in service rendered to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 19:33:29.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 19:33:29.000'),(236,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as Annexure C/2.<br></p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 .This clause is one sided as the period of 42 plus 3 months should be counted from the very first payment towards the purchased plot i.e from 05.03.2014 and the delay in signing of the allotment letter is done intentionally to use the huge amount of booking paid by the buyer for personal purposes of the builders.</p><p>3.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month which has not been paid till date adopting unfairand restrictive trade practices and missusing the hard earned money of the Complainant.</p><p>4.That the Complainant, on account of the delay were forced to retain possession of the tenanted premises on a rent of Rs. 80,000/- per month.<br></p><p><br></p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to direct the respondent to complete the Allotted Unit in all respects by providing the requisite amenities and facilities as per the terms and conditions of the Allotment Letter dated 20.06.2014 and the specifications of the Allotted Unit as appended therewith and thereafter handover its actual physical possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to compensate the Complainant for deficiency in service rendered to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 20:12:46.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 20:12:46.000'),(237,1086,'1086',1256,'d72e4c4b-b5ec-4480-ad45-a996edad35da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 07:23:03.000','SANJAY NEGI','sanket.dhall@gmail.com',9876252581,0,822537351691,'HOUSE NO 630,PANCHKULA HEIGHTS','PEER MUCHALLA ROAD DHAKAULI ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','HOUSE NO 630,PANCHKULA HEIGHTS','PEER MUCHALLA ROAD DHAKAULI ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','SANKET DHALL','sanketdhall@gmail.com',9888159159,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS','BHOLA RAM GOYAL','casahomes2016@gmail.com',8128881288,0,'FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD,AMARI HEIGHTS','SECTOR-115,KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD,MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD,AMARI HEIGHTS','SECTOR-115,KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD,MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿THAT THE COMPLAINANT BOOKED AN APARTMENT AT CASA HOMES A&nbsp; PROJECT WITH FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS AT SECTOR 115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI, VIDE AGREEMENT TO SELL DATED 23-12-2017 AND ALLOTMENT LETTER DATED 5-4-2018 IN WHICH THE RESPONDENT HAS PROMISED THE COMPLAINANT THAT HE WILL DELIVER THE POSSESSION OF THE FLAT IN JUNE 2018 AND IF NOT POSSIBLE IN JUNE DUE TO NATURAL CALAMINITY THEN THE POSSESSION WILL BE GIVEN ON OCTOBER 2018,BUT TILL DATE RESPONDENT HAS NOT HANDED OVER THE POSSESSION TO THE COMPLAINANT BECAUSE THE WORK IN THE CASA HOMES PROJECT HAS&nbsp; NOT BEEN COMPLETED AS YET,THEREFORE THE SAID POSSESSION HAS NOT BEEN HANDED OVER AS YET,TO SEE THE DEVELOPMENT WORK AT THE SITE, PHOTOGRAPHS OF THE PROJECT AND MY APARTMENT HAS BEEN ANNEXED WITH THE COMPLAINT.THE TOTAL COST OF THE APARTMENT IS 31,80,800/- AND THE COMPLAINANT HAS PAID RUPEES 190,8480/- LAKH TILL DATE TO THE RESPONDENT VIDE RECEIPT NOS 232 AND 257 DATED 21-4-18 AND 14-5-18.THAT THE COMPLAINANT IS READY TO PAY THE PENDING AMOUNT ALSO BUT THE PROJECT IS NOT READY AND THE MONEY THE COMPLAINANT HAS ALREADY PAID TO THE RESPONDENT IS ALL WASTED BECAUSE THE SAID PROJECT IS NOT READY AND RTESPONDENT IS MAKING FOOL OF THE RESPONDENT A DAY AND THE OTHER. AS IT IS THE HARD EARNED MONEY OF THE COMPLAINANT BECAUSE HE IS DOING A PRIVATE JOB AND HAS TAKEN LOAN FROM THE FINANCE COMPANY AMOUNTING TO RS 31,00,000/-,AND PAYING MONTHLY INSTALLEMENTS TO THE LOAN AGENCY FROM HIS HARD EARNED MONEY BUT THE RESPONDENT IS PLAYING WITH THE HARD EARNED MONEY OF THE COMPLAINANT AND DID NOT DELIVER THE POSSESSION&nbsp; TO THE COMPLAINANT TILL DATE. IT IS THEREFORE PRAYED TAHT KINDLY LOOK INTO THE MATTER IN THE INTEREST OF JUSTICE.</span><br></p>','<p>I- THAT FOR GRANT OF COMPENSATION ON ACCOUNT OF DEFICIENCY IN SERVICES BY THE RESPONDENT AND NOT DELIVERING THE POSSESSION ON TIME AMOUNTING TO RUPEES 10 LAKHS.<br></p><p>III- THAT TO PAY THE MENTAL HARRASSEMENT ,MENTAL AGONY TO THE COMPLAINANT TO THE TUNE OF RS 2 LAKHS.</p><p>IIII- THAT TO PAY THE LITIGATION EXPENSES TO THE TUNE OF RS 1,00,000/-</p><p>ANY OTHER RELIEF WHICH THIS COURT SEEKS FIT TO GRANT TO THE COMPLAINANT.</p>',3180800.00,1908480.00,'2018-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-04-05 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','CASA HOMES,F-4,TOWER-F,SECTOR-115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD KHARAR','','',1,1,0,0,'sanket.dhall','2018-12-17 13:22:24.000','sanket.dhall','2018-12-17 13:22:24.000'),(238,1064,'1064',1175,'fdc30a3a-7552-4e5c-8f07-8c6e1d95cb8c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-13 22:28:17.000','Manjit Singh Chimni','amangr@gmail.com',9855999111,8873092885,409690247527,'Flat No 201, HEWO Apartments','MDC, Sector 6',13,15,'134114','1','Flat No 201, HEWO Apartments','MDC, Sector 6',13,15,'134114','Vaneesh Khanna','vaneeshkhanna@yahoo.co.in',9814301225,7973088659,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE, BY SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD','SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD','info@sushmabuildtech.com',7307980092,1724610092,'Unit No B 107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase 1',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No B 107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase 1',6,128,'160002','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The complaints are senior citizens Husband &amp;\r\nWife resident of Chirkunda, Jharkhand wanting to shift to chandigarh booked a\r\nflat with SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD in their project SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE,\r\nZirakpur, Distt: SAS Nagar, Mohali – Flat No: H-101 (Measuring 2085 sq ft), Ist\r\nFloor, Tower-H.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The Flat was booked via Allotment Letter Dated:\r\n06.08.2012 and subsequently executed Apartment Buyers Agreement on 06.08.2012.\r\nAs per agreement total consideration price was Rs.&nbsp;&nbsp;68,50,000/- and\r\nthe complainants have paid Rs. 61,65,000/- + Service tax Rs. 1,95,329/-. Balance\r\nRemaining to be paid Rs. 6,85,000/- + Taxes.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">As per Agreement Dated: 06.08.2012, Clause 14 the\r\npossession date was 38 months from the date of execution of Agreement i.e.\r\n05.10.2015.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The respondents have failed to deliver the\r\npossession till date. The Complaints on assurance of respondents had sold their\r\nhouse property in home town – Chirkunda, Jharkhand on 24.05.2018 and have\r\nshifted permanently in a rental accomodation at Flat No: 201, HEWO Apartments,\r\nSector 6, Mansa Devi Complex, Panchkula.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The complaints are aggrieved party. The respondents\r\nhave failed to address their grievances for delay in possession for more than 3\r\nyears. A Legal notice was also served to them in his context on 15.07.2018. The\r\nrespondents had shown no interest to our complaint and have adopted a very\r\nindifferent attitude.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">That due to the deficiency in service\r\non the part of the&nbsp;respondents&nbsp;resulting into a\r\nbig&nbsp;harassment,&nbsp;tension&nbsp;and&nbsp;apprehension&nbsp;as well as monetary\r\nloss, the complainants are entitled to the&nbsp;following&nbsp;reliefs from\r\nthe&nbsp;respondents:</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1. Immediate&nbsp;possession\r\nof the fully developed&nbsp;apartment&nbsp;as promised by the&nbsp;respondents</span><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 8pt;\">2. A\r\nsum of Rs. 5 lacs as compensation on account of harassment, tension and\r\napprehension caused to the complainant due to delay in possession of the\r\napartment</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">3. Legal\r\nExpense to the tune of Rs. 75,000/- for forcing the complainant to enter into\r\nthis uncalled for litigation</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 8pt;\">4. Amount of rent\r\nand&nbsp;maintenance&nbsp;charges paid / to be paid by the complaint in respect\r\nof the rented flat where they are presently residing from 01.05.2018, till the\r\ndate of handing over the possession of the&nbsp;apartment.</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 8pt; text-align: justify;\">It is therefore prayed that\r\nthe&nbsp;respondents&nbsp;be directed to give the above mention reliefs to the\r\ncomplainants as the&nbsp;complaints&nbsp;are entitled to the above said relief\r\nin&nbsp;lieu&nbsp;of the facts and circumstances explained.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 8pt; text-align: justify;\">NOTE: WE HAVE ALSO APPLIED FOR RELIEFS UNDER FORM - M - AS PER NEW RERA RULES<br></span><br></p>',6850000.00,6360329.00,'2015-10-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-08-06 00:00:00','2012-08-06 00:00:00','Flat No H101, Tower H\r\n1st Floor, Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'manjit305','2018-12-17 13:57:05.000','manjit305','2018-12-17 13:57:05.000'),