tial completion certificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">That respondent issued offer of possession\r\nletter and No Due Certificate on 15.05.2016. Thereafter, applicant requested\r\nnumber of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed\r\nresolve the issues raised by applicants and to provide occupation/completion\r\ncertificate even after receiving legal notice.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">4.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">That the applicants requested number to times\r\nto respondent through letter &amp; emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and\r\nother issues but the respondent failed to revert the any of letter/email sent\r\nby applicants.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span>i.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To pay\r\na compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing\r\nmental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering\r\nservice and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of\r\njustice.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>ii.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To\r\nremove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc\r\nand to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>iii.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To\r\nrefund the amount received as service tax from the applicant alongwith interest\r\n@ 18% since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned\r\ndepartment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">To\r\nrefund the amount for giving less carpet area.</span><br></p>',6300000.00,6300000.00,'2016-04-29 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-04-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Building H1, Flat - 103, Maya Garden City, Nagla Road, Zirakpur 140603','','',1,0,0,0,'vishalanand','2019-01-03 18:23:07.000','vishalanand','2019-01-03 18:23:07.000'),(257,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as ANNEXURE C/2.<br></p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 .This clause is one sided as the period of 42 plus 3 months should be counted from the very first payment towards the purchased plot i.e from 05.03.2014 and the delay in signing of the allotment letter is done intentionally to use the huge amount of booking paid by the buyer for personal purposes of the builders.</p><p>3.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month which has not been paid till date adopting unfairand restrictive trade practices and missusing the hard earned money of the Complainant.</p><p>4.That the Complainant, on account of the delay were forced to retain possession of the tenanted premises on a rent of Rs. 80,000/- per month.<br></p><p><br></p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to direct the respondent to complete the Allotted Unit in all respects by providing the requisite amenities and facilities as per the terms and conditions of the Allotment Letter dated 20.06.2014 and the specifications of the Allotted Unit as appended therewith and thereafter handover its actual physical possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to compensate the Complainant for deficiency in service rendered to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:55:58.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:55:58.000'),(258,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-04 19:10:32.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as ANNEXURE C/2.<br></p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 .This clause is one sided as the period of 42 plus 3 months should be counted from the very first payment towards the purchased plot i.e from 05.03.2014 and the delay in signing of the allotment letter is done intentionally to use the huge amount of booking paid by the buyer for personal purposes of the builders.</p><p>3.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month which has not been paid till date adopting unfairand restrictive trade practices and missusing the hard earned money of the Complainant.</p><p>4.That the Complainant, on account of the delay were forced to retain possession of the tenanted premises on a rent of Rs. 80,000/- per month.<br></p><p><br></p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to direct the respondent to complete the Allotted Unit in all respects by providing the requisite amenities and facilities as per the terms and conditions of the Allotment Letter dated 20.06.2014 and the specifications of the Allotted Unit as appended therewith and thereafter handover its actual physical possession to the Complainant;&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation to the Complainant for the inordinate delay in offering the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018 in the form of interest @ 24% per annum payable on the amount of Rs. 99,50,000/- till such time the actual physical possession of the Allotted Unit, complete in all respects, is handed over to the Complainant;</p><p>iii) to pay the promised amount for delay in possession to be paid by the respondent i.e. Rs.1,32,000/- including interest @ 18% on the said amount.</p><p>iv) to compensate the Complainant for deficiency in service rendered to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>vi) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8 lacs on account of mental agony and harassment caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vii) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:56:40.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:56:40.000'),(259,1095,'1095',1318,'4b6e8884-5d03-401d-a0d6-887e7b4d02be','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Aman Sunda','kulwindersinghadvocate@gmail.com',9988776655,0,0,'Building H1, Flat - 102','Maya Garden City, Nagla Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Building H1, Flat - 102','Maya Garden City, Nagla Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Kulwinder Singh','kulwindersinghadvocate@gmail.com',9977554433,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0192','Maya Garden City','Barnala Builders','dummymail@gmail.com',9216910335,0,'opposite McDonalds','Chandigarh Ambala Highway',28,507,'140603','1','opposite McDonalds','Chandigarh Ambala Highway',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">That applicants booked 5BHK flat for their own\r\nresidence in the project of respondent no. 1 vide application dated 30.12.2011\r\nand the respondent issued allotment of flat no. 102 measuring 2850 Sq. Ft. in\r\nH1 block at first floor vide letter dated 24.07.2012. The applicants entered\r\ninto agreement to sell with respondent, as per which total consideration of\r\nflat was Rs. 57,00,000/-. As per clause 5 of agreement the date of sale deed\r\nwas fixed on or before 30th November, 2015. The applicants paid Rs. 66,87,479/-\r\nwith the respondent against total consideration of Rs. 57,00,000/- which\r\nincludes maintenance, late payment charges and service tax etc.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">That as per brochure, respondents are liable to\r\nprovide club facility and swimming pool etc which were also not provided by\r\nrespondents till date. The possession was handed over to applicants but the\r\nsale deed was not made in favor of applicants as respondents failed to get\r\ncompletion certificate from competent authority and the partial completion\r\ncertificate issued to respondent was conditional &amp; due to non fulfilment of\r\nconditions the pollution control board has already written letter to competent\r\nauthority to cancel the partial completion certificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">That respondent issued offer of possession\r\nletter and No Due Certificate on 15.05.2016. Thereafter, applicant requested\r\nnumber of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed\r\nresolve the issues raised by applicants and to provide occupation/completion\r\ncertificate even after receiving legal notice.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">4.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">That the applicants requested number to times\r\nto respondent through letter &amp; emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and\r\nother issues but the respondent failed to revert the any of letter/email sent\r\nby applicants.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span>i.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To pay\r\na compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing\r\nmental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering\r\nservice and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of\r\njustice.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>ii.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To\r\nremove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc\r\nand to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>iii.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To\r\nrefund the amount received as service tax from the applicant alongwith interest\r\n@ 18% since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned\r\ndepartment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:2.0cm;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-2.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-1.0cm;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:list 2.0cm\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Century;mso-bidi-font-family:Century\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>iv.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Century&quot;,serif\">To\r\nrefund the amount for giving less carpet area.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',5700000.00,5700000.00,'2014-11-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-11-30 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Building H1, Flat - 102, Maya Garden City, Nagla Road, Zirakpur - 140603 ','','',1,0,0,0,'vishalanand','2019-01-05 17:35:10.000','vishalanand','2019-01-05 17:35:10.000'),(260,1081,'1081',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 19:32:59.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as ANNEXURE C/2.<br></p><p>2.As per Clause 6.2 of the Allotment letter dated 20.06.2014, the Respondent were contractually bound to give possession within a period of 45 months from the date of signing the allotment letter i.e. on or before 20.06.2014 .This clause is one sided as the period of 42 plus 3 months should be counted from the very first payment towards the purchased plot i.e from 05.03.2014 and the delay in signing of the allotment letter is done intentionally to use the huge amount of booking paid by the buyer for personal purposes of the builders.</p><p>3.The respondent had promised to pay an amount of Rs. 5/- per Sq.ft per month for delay in possession on Super Built up Area i.e. 2400 Sq.ft totalling Rs.12,000/- per month which has not been paid till date adopting unfairand restrictive trade practices and missusing the hard earned money of the Complainant.</p><p>4.That the Complainant, on account of the delay were forced to retain possession of the tenanted premises on a rent of Rs. 80,000/- per month.<br></p><p><br></p><div><br></div>','<p>1.That in view of the facts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account of being deficient in rendering services to the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices in fleecing the Complainant of their hard earned money are thus liable to compensate the Complainant and as such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned complaint as under:-&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>i) to compensate the Complainant for keeping the complainant on his toes and wasting his precious time to visit the site repeatedly, to the tune of&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Rs.2,00,000/-&nbsp;</p><p>ii) to pay compensation of Rs.10,00,000/- on account of harassment due to delay in Possession to the Complainant beyond the stipulated time period which expired on 20.03.2018.</p><p>iii) to compensate the Complainant for deficiency in service rendered to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.<br></p><p>iv) to direct the Respondent to compensate the Complainant for the rental money of Rs. 80,000/- per month paid by them for occupying the rented accommodation from the proposed date of possession till its actual realization;&nbsp;</p><p>v) to direct the Respondent to pay compensation to the Complainant to the tune of Rs. 8,00,000/- on account of mental agony&nbsp; caused to the Complainant;</p><p>vi) to pay Rs. 1,50,000/- as litigation costs.&nbsp;</p>',9950000.00,9950000.00,'2018-03-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no 09062 tower no 9 ','','',1,1,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-07 19:32:53.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-07 19:32:53.000'),(261,1047,'1047',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-10 07:27:09.000','DAKSHA','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'H. NO. 1/3, BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','1','H. NO. 1/3, BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','Ravinderpal Singh','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0076','CITY CENTRE ','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','info@ansalapi.com',0,0,'SCO 183-184, SECTOR 9-C CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','SCO 183-184, SECTOR 9-C CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Respondents\r\ncame up with commercial project as CITI CENTRE at Sector 115 Mohali. Husband of\r\nthe complainant approached the Respondents for booking of one showroom floated\r\nby the Respondent. Respondents also allured the Complainant of ASSURED RETURNS\r\non the amount invested till the date of possession. Initially complainant\r\nbooked one showroom bearing No. 6UGF measuring 1772 sq. ft. @ Rs.30,12,400/-.\r\nAgreement executed on 09.02.2010 (A-2) Complainant deposited Rs.28,61,780/- on\r\n30.01.2010. Agreement executed on 09.02.2010 promising possession within 42\r\nmonths maximum.&nbsp;Respondent was liable to pay Rs.53,847/- per month which\r\nwas paid by 31.03.2012. Since the construction of the showroom was very slow\r\ncomplainant decided to shift in other showroom in same project. Respondent\r\noffered two showrooms bearing no. 03SF and 04SF. Complainant paid\r\nRs.20,00,000/- more on 25.05.2012 jointly against both showrooms. Price of each\r\nshowroom was fixed as Rs.25,00,000/-. Each unit is measuring 1588 sq. ft.\r\nComplainant paid total Rs.48,61,780/- till date for both showrooms.\r\nRs.24,30,890/- against each unit. balance Rs.69,110/- to be paid on offer of\r\npossession which never offered till date. New Agreement of SF04 showroom\r\nexecuted on 08.06.2012&nbsp; wherein possession was to be given within 42\r\nmonths maximum which expired on 08.12.2016. As per new agreement Rs.1,06,563/-\r\nwas to be paid as assured return per quarter per showroom (i.e. Rs.35,521/- per\r\nmonth).&nbsp;Assured Returns stopped after JULY, 2016 violating the terms of\r\nthe agreement as well as provisions of RERA. Construction has been stopped in\r\nbetween. Possession not offered till date. Neither obtained completion and\r\noccupation certificates. Respondents are in arrears of Rs.1065630/- (01.07.2016\r\nto 31.12.2018) as ASSURED RETURN. </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\">Separate complaint seeking possession and assured return has been filed under Form - M&nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\">Present application filed seeking compensation for </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\">Non payment of Assured Return, </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\">Not offering timely possession within the period of 42 months,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\">Not completing the construction of the project,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\">Violation of provisions of RERA,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><font face=\"roboto, serif\">Causing mental and Physical Harassment to the complainant.</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><font face=\"roboto, serif\">Cost of litigation Rs.1,10,000/-</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><br></p>',2500000.00,2430890.00,'2015-06-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-06-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','SF-04, CITY CENTRE SECTOR 115 MOHALI','','',1,1,0,0,'advravinder','2019-01-10 07:27:03.000','advravinder','2019-01-10 07:27:03.000'),(262,1064,'1064',1175,'fdc30a3a-7552-4e5c-8f07-8c6e1d95cb8c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-02 11:27:46.000','Manjit Singh Chimni','amangr@gmail.com',9855999111,8873092885,409690247527,'Flat No 201, HEWO Apartments','MDC, Sector 6',13,15,'134114','1','Flat No 201, HEWO Apartments','MDC, Sector 6',13,15,'134114','Vaneesh Khanna','vaneeshkhanna@yahoo.co.in',9814301225,7973088659,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE, BY SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD','SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD','info@sushmabuildtech.com',7307980092,1724610092,'Unit No B 107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase 1',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No B 107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase 1',6,128,'160002','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The\r\ncomplaints are senior citizens resident of Chirkunda, Jharkhand wanting to\r\nshift to chandigarh booked a flat with SUSHMA in their project SUSHMA\r\nCHANDIGARH GRANDE, Zirakpur - Flat No: H-101, Ist Floor. The Flat was booked\r\nvia Allotment Letter Dated: 06.08.2012 and Apartment Buyers Agreement on\r\n06.08.2012. As per agrmt total consideration price was\r\nRs.&nbsp;&nbsp;68,50,000/- and the complainants have paid Rs.\r\n61,65,000/-+Service tax Rs. 1,95,329/ .Balance Remaining to be paid Rs.\r\n6,85,000/-+ Taxes. As per Agreement Dated: 06.08.2012, Clause 14 the possession\r\ndate was 38 months from the date of execution of Agreement i.e. 05.10.2015. The\r\nrespondents having failed to offer possession by March 2018, the Complainants\r\nhad to get the sale deeds executed on 24.05.2018 and handed over the possession\r\nof his Chirkunda residential house to the seller as per their sale agreement.\r\nAfter&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">selling</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;his house at Chirkunda, they shifted with\r\ntheir baggage to Panchkula on 01.06.2018 on rented &nbsp;flat no 201, HEWO&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Apartments</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">,\r\nSector 6, MDC Pkl with effective 01.05.2018 on a rented flat with Rent of\r\n33000+2200 as maintenance Charges.&nbsp;&nbsp;It is&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">pertinent</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;to\r\nmention here that due to anxiety and&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">uncertainty</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;created by&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">respondents</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">,\r\nthe applicant suffered heart attach and had to undergo angioplasty at Colombia\r\nAsia Hospital Kolkata on 15.08.2017. The Complainants had taken&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Housing</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;loan\r\nfrom India Bulls and were entitled for rebate under IT Act @30% on the interest\r\npaid on Rs. 1370000/- but since the possession has not been given the\r\ncomplainant could not claim&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;set rebate.&nbsp;&nbsp;Since GST has been\r\nenacted the builders are insisting on GST@12% on balance pymt whereas the&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">complaints</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;would\r\nhave paid Service&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt\"><a href=\"mailto:Tax@4.5%25\"><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 14px;\">Tax@4.5%</span></a><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;had they given the possession on time. A Legal notice\r\nwas also served to them in his context on 15.07.2018. The respondents had shown\r\nno interest to our complaint and have adopted a very indifferent attitude. The\r\ncomplaints have been regularly visiting the site and the head office since 2015.</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: roboto, serif;\">That due to the deficiency in service\r\non the part of the&nbsp;respondents&nbsp;resulting into a\r\nbig&nbsp;harassment,&nbsp;tension&nbsp;and&nbsp;apprehension&nbsp;as well as monetary\r\nloss, the complainants are entitled to the&nbsp;following&nbsp;reliefs from\r\nthe&nbsp;respondents:</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Sum of Rs. 500000 as\r\ncompensation on account of harassment tension &amp; apprehension Course to the\r\napplicants. The Complainants have visited their site &amp; head office numerous\r\ntimes but the builder have failed to address to their griviences. </span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Legal Expenses to the tune of Rs. 75000 for forcing the complainants to enter\r\ninto this uncalled-for litigation as complainant has paid Rs. 21000/- vide\r\ncheque for legal notice and incurred expenditure on legal consultation and\r\nprocessing.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Amount of Rent &amp; Maintenance Charges Paid/ to be paid by the applicants I\r\nrespect of the rented flat where the applicants are presently residing from\r\n01.05.2018 till the date of handing over the possession of the apartment.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Interim order may kindly be passed in favour of complainant and for any other\r\nrelief or reliefs Honorable RERA Authority deems fit.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span><!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span><!--[endif]--></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 8pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">NOTE: WE HAVE ALSO APPLIED FOR RELIEFS UNDER FORM - M - AS PER NEW RERA RULES</span><br></span><br></p>',6850000.00,6360329.00,'2015-10-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-08-06 00:00:00','2012-08-06 00:00:00','Flat No H101, Tower H\r\n1st Floor, Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'manjit305','2019-01-10 13:42:05.000','manjit305','2019-01-10 13:42:05.000'),(263,1064,'1064',1175,'fdc30a3a-7552-4e5c-8f07-8c6e1d95cb8c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-10 13:54:37.000','Manjit Singh Chimni','amangr@gmail.com',9855999111,8873092885,409690247527,'Flat No 201, HEWO Apartments','MDC, Sector 6',13,15,'134114','1','Flat No 201, HEWO Apartments','MDC, Sector 6',13,15,'134114','Vaneesh Khanna','vaneeshkhanna@yahoo.co.in',9814301225,7973088659,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE, BY SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD','SUSHMA BUILDTECH LTD','info@sushmabuildtech.com',7307980092,1724610092,'Unit No B 107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase 1',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No B 107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase 1',6,128,'160002','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.8pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The\r\ncomplaints are senior citizens resident of Chirkunda, Jharkhand wanting to\r\nshift to chandigarh booked a flat with SUSHMA in their project SUSHMA\r\nCHANDIGARH GRANDE, Zirakpur - Flat No: H-101, Ist Floor. The Flat was booked\r\nvia Allotment Letter Dated: 06.08.2012 and Apartment Buyers Agreement on\r\n06.08.2012. As per agrmt total consideration price was\r\nRs.&nbsp;&nbsp;68,50,000/- and the complainants have paid Rs.\r\n61,65,000/-+Service tax Rs. 1,95,329/ .Balance Remaining to be paid Rs.\r\n6,85,000/-+ Taxes. As per Agreement Dated: 06.08.2012, Clause 14 the possession\r\ndate was 38 months from the date of execution of Agreement i.e. 05.10.2015. The\r\nrespondents having failed to offer possession by March 2018, the Complainants\r\nhad to get the sale deeds executed on 24.05.2018 and handed over the possession\r\nof his Chirkunda residential house to the seller as per their sale agreement.\r\nAfter&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">selling</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;his house at Chirkunda, they shifted with\r\ntheir baggage to Panchkula on 01.06.2018 on rented &nbsp;flat no 201, HEWO&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Apartments</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">,\r\nSector 6, MDC Pkl with effective 01.05.2018 on a rented flat with Rent of\r\n33000+2200 as maintenance Charges.&nbsp;&nbsp;It is&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">pertinent</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;to\r\nmention here that due to anxiety and&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">uncertainty</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;created by&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">respondents</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">,\r\nthe applicant suffered heart attach and had to undergo angioplasty at Colombia\r\nAsia Hospital Kolkata on 15.08.2017. The Complainants had taken&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Housing</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;loan\r\nfrom India Bulls and were entitled for rebate under IT Act @30% on the interest\r\npaid on Rs. 1370000/- but since the possession has not been given the\r\ncomplainant could not claim&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;set rebate.&nbsp;&nbsp;Since GST has been\r\nenacted the builders are insisting on GST@12% on balance pymt whereas the&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">complaints</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;would\r\nhave paid Service&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt\"><a href=\"mailto:Tax@4.5%25\"><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 14px;\">Tax@4.5%</span></a><span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;had they given the possession on time. A Legal notice\r\nwas also served to them in his context on 15.07.2018. The respondents had shown\r\nno interest to our complaint and have adopted a very indifferent attitude. The\r\ncomplaints have been regularly visiting the site and the head office since 2015.</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: roboto, serif;\">That due to the deficiency in service\r\non the part of the&nbsp;respondents&nbsp;resulting into a\r\nbig&nbsp;harassment,&nbsp;tension&nbsp;and&nbsp;apprehension&nbsp;as well as monetary\r\nloss, the complainants are entitled to the&nbsp;following&nbsp;reliefs from\r\nthe&nbsp;respondents:</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Sum of Rs. 500000 as\r\ncompensation on account of harassment tension &amp; apprehension Course to the\r\napplicants. The Complainants have visited their site &amp; head office numerous\r\ntimes but the builder have failed to address to their grievances. </span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Legal Expenses to the tune of Rs. 75000 for forcing the complainants to enter\r\ninto this uncalled-for litigation as complainant has paid Rs. 21000/- vide\r\ncheque for legal notice and incurred expenditure on legal consultation and\r\nprocessing.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Amount of Rent &amp; Maintenance Charges Paid/ to be paid by the applicants I\r\nrespect of the rented flat where the applicants are presently residing from\r\n01.05.2018 till the date of handing over the possession of the apartment.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Interim order may kindly be passed in favour of complainant and for any other\r\nrelief or reliefs Honorable RERA Authority deems fit.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span><!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span><!--[endif]--></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;\r\nline-height:normal;tab-stops:14.2pt\"><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 8pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">NOTE: WE HAVE ALSO APPLIED FOR RELIEFS UNDER FORM - M - AS PER NEW RERA RULES</span><br></span><br></p>',6850000.00,6360329.00,'2015-10-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-08-06 00:00:00','2012-08-06 00:00:00','Flat No H101, Tower H\r\n1st Floor, Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Zirakpur','','',1,1,0,0,'manjit305','2019-01-10 13:42:23.000','manjit305','2019-01-10 13:42:23.000'),(264,1096,'1096',1336,'8a3f1fab-d113-44e2-80ff-3b7cfc2e5188','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Anjana  Anand','KULWINDERSINGHADVOCATE@GMAIL.COM',9872903100,0,0,'H1-103, Maya Garden City','Zirakpur, District Mohali',28,507,'140603','1','H1-103, Maya Garden City','Zirakpur, District Mohali',28,507,'140603','Kulwinder Singh','ksvarun513@gmail.com',9915772513,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0192','Maya Garden City','Maya Garden City','barnalabuilders@ymail.com',9216910335,0,'Opposite McDonald\'s, Chandigarh-Ambala Highway','Zirakpur, Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','Opposite McDonald\'s, Chandigarh-Ambala Highway','Zirakpur, Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','<p>That applicant booked 5BHK flat for her own residence in the project of respondent no. 1 vide application dated 08.12.2012 and the respondent issued allotment of flat no. 103 measuring 2850 Sq. Ft. in H1 block at first floor vide letter dated 14.12.2012. The applicant entered into agreement to sell with respondent, as per which total consideration of flat was Rs. 63,00,000/-. As per clause 5 of agreement the date of sale deed was fixed on or before 30th November, 2014. The applicants paid Rs. 68,41,850/- with the respondent against total consideration of Rs. 63,00,000/- which includes maintenance, late payment charges and service tax etc.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per brochure, respondents are liable to provide club house facility and swimming pool etc which were also not provided by respondents till date. The possession was to be handed over on or before 30.11.2014 but the same was offered on 15.04.2016 and the sale deed was also to be done on 30.11.2014 which was done on 22.03.2018 in favor of applicant. It is relevant to mention here that the respondents failed to get completion certificate from competent authority and the partial completion certificate issued to respondent was conditional &amp; due to non fulfillment of conditions the pollution control board has already written letter to competent authority to cancel the partial completion certificate.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That applicant requested number of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed resolve the issues raised by applicant and to provide occupation/completion certificate even after receiving legal notice.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the applicant requested number to times to respondent through letter and emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and other issues but the respondent failed to revert&nbsp; any of letter/email sent by applicant.</p>','<p>To pay Rs. 8,02,000 as per valuation report to make the flat in the position as promised by the respondent.&nbsp;</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000 (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing mental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering service and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To remove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc and to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount received as service tax from the applicant since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned department.</p><p>e.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount for giving less carpet area.</p><p>f.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give NEC and get the sale deed done as per RERA with clear carpet area in favour of the applicant.</p><p>g.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay interest @ 18% on the amount of Rs. 63,00,000 from the due date of possession i.e. 30 Nov 2014 till the date of sale deed/issuance of completion certificate.</p><p>h.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide club/swimming pool etc alongwith all facilities as per promise made in brochure.</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide all other facilities which are promised by not provided like provision of DTH, Broadband, Intercom Facility, approach from Highway.</p><p>j.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- as litigation expenses.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Or Any other order as the Hon’ble&nbsp; Adjudicating Officer may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances in favor of the Applicant be passed, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6300000.00,6841850.00,'2014-11-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-12-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','H1-103, Maya Garden City, Zirakpur, District Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'ANJANAANAND','2019-01-11 12:20:03.000','ANJANAANAND','2019-01-11 12:20:03.000'),(265,1097,'1097',1331,'8b292055-1541-4c28-810a-ccc6e9a24878','FormTypeN',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sameer Madan','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 2123,','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','1','Sector 15 C,','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Bishangarh & Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur.','Sushma Buildtech Ltd. through Sh. Bharat Mittal, MD','sushmagrande@gmail.com',0,0,'Plot No. 381','Industrial Area Ph. I',6,128,'160002','1','Plot No. 381','Industrial Area Ph. I',6,128,'160002','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the applicant had applied for an Apartment/Flat/Residential unit . The applicant got an allotment letter issued by the respondent on 14th of Feb, 2012, in which the applicant was finally allotted the unit Number F-1403, 14th Floor in Tower F ( measuring 1885 sq. ft. ,super area) , in Sushma Chandigarh Grande at Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Teh. Derabassi, Mohali, in the year 2012. That as per the allotment the total consideration of the unit was Rs 5990530 (Rs. Fifty Nine Lac Ninety Thousand Five Hundred Thirty only), out of which the applicant paid Rs. 600,000 (Rs. Six lacs) as earnest money along with the application form. That the applicant had opted for construction linked plan and paid Rs. 5655261 (Rs. Fifty Six Lacs Fifty Five Thousand Two hundred and Sixty One only). That an agreement dated 03-April-2012 was reduced into writing and as per clause number 14(d) of the agreement the applicant was to get the possession within a period of 42 months from the date of agreement and six months grace period was available with the developer for completing and handing over the unit to the applicant. That the applicant was to get the possession latest by 02-April-2016. But the respondent failed to comply with his own terms and conditions. That a demand letter dated 19-Nov.-2018, for balance consideration amount of Rs. 335473 (Rs. Three Lac Thirty Five Thousand Four Hundred and Seventy Three only), was issued to the applicant. That the applicant seeing the track record of the developer regarding the upkeep of promises, has decided to withdraw from the said project as per Section 18(1)(a) of the RERA and seeks refund of the amount paid to the developer with interest as applicable as per the Act and any other relief which this Honorable Court deems fit in the interest of justice for the applicant.</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the applicant seeks for compensation of Rs. 500000 (Rs. Five Lacs only) from the respondent on account of causing monetary losses in terms of money withheld without any sufficient reason and cause as well as without any explanation. That the applicant further prays for Rs. 35000 (Rs. Thirty Five Thousand only) as litigation costs and Rs. 50,000 (Rs.Fifty Thousand only) for mental agony. That the compensation as prayed, is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a foul play by using the money of the applicant and by not delivering the unit within the agreed time period as mentioned in the agreement.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',5990530.00,5655261.00,'2016-04-02 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-02-14 00:00:00','2012-04-03 00:00:00','F-1403, 14th Flr., Tower \"F\", Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Bishangarh & Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur.','','',2,0,0,0,'madaansameer08012019','2019-01-11 12:57:54.000','madaansameer08012019','2019-01-11 12:57:54.000'),(266,1098,'1098',1325,'ba7e9568-25c6-4f4e-80be-eab9afc56f7a','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SANDEEP BANSAL','bansalz@gmail.com',9212014142,1143592524,560059477000,'B-3/9','JANAK PURI',10,562,'110058','1','B-3/9','JANAK PURI',10,562,'110058','SHYAM LAL BANSAL','slbansal4242@gmail.com',9899171794,1143592524,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','feedback@emaarmgf.com',0,1723314800,'SCO 120 to 122','Sector 17C 2nd Floor Cabin No 203',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 120 to 122','Sector 17C 2nd Floor Cabin No 203',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Vide order 28th NOVEMBER 2018 in case No AO 07 2017 passed by the Adjudicating officer to return the complaint with liberty to file a fresh complaint before the Authority hence fresh complaint is submitted on N Form for payment of compensation Confined to adjudicating compensation under section 12 and 14 and 16 and 19 of the Act So filed fresh complaint as order dated 28th November 2018 vide Memo No RERA 2018 Legal 8556 dated 03rd December 2018 Annexure P1</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Apartment booked on 12th August 2006 Annexure P2</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Apartment allotment dated 06th April 2007 of Premium Residential Complex No F 3 502 on 5th Floor situated Project in The Views at Mohali Hills in Sector 105 SAS Nagar District Punjab Annexure P3 Unit Code TVM F3 F05 502</p><p>d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Builder Buyers Agreement executed between the parties on 14th March 2008 Annexure P4</p><p>e)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As per Clause no 21 1 of Builder Buyers Agreement possession for apartment to be handed over up to 06th October 2010 maximum 36 months add 6 months grace period total 42 months from the allotment letter dated 06th April 2007 Annexure P3 but till date 99 months has passed no possession is ready</p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above the applicant prays for the following compensation</p><p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Compensation under Section of the Act Promoter given incorrect and false statement to handover the possession within 36 months from the date of allotment hence I am entitled for compensation in the manner provided under RERA act</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The promoter fails to complete or unable to give possession of the apartment plot or building fails to discharge any other obligations imposed on him under this act or the rules or regulations made thereunder or in accordance with the terms and conditions of the agreement for sale He shall be liable to pay such compensation to the allottee in the manner as provided under RERA Act</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The builder failed to discharge their obligation as provided in the act and failed to handover the physical possession of the apartment</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant shall be entitled to claim compensation in the manner as provided under this act from the promoter</p><p>e.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The respondent fails to offer possession of the apartment within 36 months add 6 months grace period maximum up to 42 months The promoter shall be liable to pay delay compensation as per Builder Buyers Agreement clause no 23 1 Annexure P4 at the rate of&nbsp; Rs 5 per square feet per month of the super area of the said apartment for the period of delayed possession for 98 months as demanded by the complainant in so many letters Annexure P5 Letter page 47 to 50</p><p>The calculation is as under</p><p>Flat Area x delay months x Rate of compensation per month</p><p>&nbsp;1550&nbsp; &nbsp;x&nbsp; &nbsp;98 months x Rs 5 Rs 759500</p><p>f.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the respondent to pay Rs 100000 as compensation to the complainant for causing mentally agony</p><p>g.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the respondent to pay Rs 100000 cost of litigation expenses</p>',4727150.00,4132278.00,'2010-04-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2007-04-06 00:00:00','2008-03-14 00:00:00','F3 502 THE VIEWS MOHALI HILLS DISTRICT MOHALI PUNJAB','','',1,0,0,0,'SANDEEPBANSAL','2019-01-12 13:30:07.000','SANDEEPBANSAL','2019-01-12 13:30:07.000'),(267,1099,'1099',1325,'ba7e9568-25c6-4f4e-80be-eab9afc56f7a','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-21 13:22:04.000','SANDEEP BANSAL','bansalz@gmail.com',9212014142,1143592524,560059476997,'B-3/9','JANAK PURI',10,562,'110058','1','B-3/9','JANAK PURI',10,562,'110058','SHYAM LAL BANSAL','slbansal4242@gmail.com',9899171794,1143292524,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','feedback@emaarmgf.com',0,1723314800,'SCO 120 to 122','Sector 17C 2nd Floor Cabin No 203',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 120 to 122','Sector 17C 2nd Floor Cabin No 203',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Vide order 28th NOVEMBER 2018 in case No AO 07 2017 passed by the Adjudicating officer to return the complaint with liberty to file a fresh complaint before the Authority hence fresh complaint is submitted on N Form for payment of compensation Confined to adjudicating compensation under section 12 and 14 and 16 and 19 of the Act So filed fresh complaint as order dated 28th November 2018 vide Memo No RERA 2018 Legal 8556 dated 03rd December 2018 Annexure P1</p><p>Apartment booked on 12th August 2006 Annexure P2</p><p>Apartment allotment dated 06th April 2007 of Premium Residential Complex No F 3 502 on 5th Floor situated Project in The Views at Mohali Hills in Sector 105 SAS Nagar District Punjab Annexure P3 Unit Code TVM F3 F05 502</p><p>Builder Buyers Agreement executed between the parties on 14th March 2008 Annexure P4</p><p>As per Clause no 21 1 of Builder Buyers Agreement possession for apartment to be handed over up to 06th October 2010 maximum 36 months add 6 months grace period total 42 months from the allotment letter dated 06th April 2007 Annexure P3 but till date 99 months has passed no possession is ready</p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above the applicant prays for the following compensation</p><p>Compensation under Section of the Act Promoter given incorrect and false statement to handover the possession within 36 months from the date of allotment hence I am entitled for compensation in the manner provided under RERA act</p><p>The promoter fails to complete or unable to give possession of the apartment plot or building fails to discharge any other obligations imposed on him under this act or the rules or regulations made thereunder or in accordance with the terms and conditions of the agreement for sale He shall be liable to pay such compensation to the allottee in the manner as provided under RERA Act</p><p>The builder failed to discharge their obligation as provided in the act and failed to handover the physical possession of the apartment</p><p>The complainant shall be entitled to claim compensation in the manner as provided under this act from the promoter</p><p>The respondent fails to offer possession of the apartment within 36 months add 6 months grace period maximum up to 42 months The promoter shall be liable to pay delay compensation as per Builder Buyers Agreement clause no 23 1 Annexure P4 at the rate of&nbsp; Rs 5 per square feet per month of the super area of the said apartment for the period of delayed possession for 98 months as demanded by the complainant in so many letters Annexure P5 Letter page 47 to 50</p><p>The calculation is as under</p><p>Flat Area x delay months x Rate of compensation per month</p><p>&nbsp;1550 x 98 months x Rs 5 Rs 759500</p><p>Direct the respondent to pay Rs 100000 as compensation to the complainant for causing mentally agony</p><p>Direct the respondent to pay Rs 100000 cost of litigation expenses</p>',4727150.00,4132278.00,'2010-04-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2007-04-06 00:00:00','2008-03-14 00:00:00','UNIT NO F3 502 THE VIEWS MOHALI HILL DISTRICT MOHALI PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'SANDEEPBANSAL','2019-01-12 17:49:53.000','SANDEEPBANSAL','2019-01-12 17:49:53.000'),(268,1097,'1097',1331,'8b292055-1541-4c28-810a-ccc6e9a24878','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-14 12:21:39.000','Sameer Madan','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 2123,','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','1','H.No. 2123,','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Bishangarh & Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur.','Sushma Buildtech Ltd. through Sh. Bharat Mittal, MD','sushmagrande@gmail.com',0,0,'Plot No. 381','Industrial Area Ph. I',6,128,'160002','1','Plot No. 381','Industrial Area Ph. I',6,128,'160002','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the applicant had applied for an Apartment/Flat/Residential unit . The applicant got an allotment letter issued by the respondent on 14th of Feb, 2012, in which the applicant was finally allotted the unit Number F-1403, 14th Floor in Tower F ( measuring 1885 sq. ft. ,super area) , in Sushma Chandigarh Grande at Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Teh. Derabassi, Mohali, in the year 2012. That as per the allotment the total consideration of the unit was Rs 5990530 (Rs. Fifty Nine Lac Ninety Thousand Five Hundred Thirty only), out of which the applicant paid Rs. 600,000 (Rs. Six lacs) as earnest money along with the application form. That the applicant had opted for construction linked plan and paid Rs. 5655261 (Rs. Fifty Six Lacs Fifty Five Thousand Two hundred and Sixty One only). That an agreement dated 03-April-2012 was reduced into writing and as per clause number 14(d) of the agreement the applicant was to get the possession within a period of 42 months from the date of agreement and six months grace period was available with the developer for completing and handing over the unit to the applicant. That the applicant was to get the possession latest by 02-April-2016. But the respondent failed to comply with his own terms and conditions. That a demand letter dated 19-Nov.-2018, for balance consideration amount of Rs. 335473 (Rs. Three Lac Thirty Five Thousand Four Hundred and Seventy Three only), was issued to the applicant. That the applicant seeing the track record of the developer regarding the upkeep of promises, has decided to withdraw from the said project as per Section 18(1)(a) of the RERA and seeks refund of the amount paid to the developer with interest as applicable as per the Act and any other relief which this Honorable Court deems fit in the interest of justice for the applicant.</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the applicant seeks for compensation of Rs. 500000 (Rs. Five Lacs only) from the respondent on account of causing monetary losses in terms of money withheld without any sufficient reason and cause as well as without any explanation. That the applicant further prays for Rs. 35000 (Rs. Thirty Five Thousand only) as litigation costs and Rs. 50,000 (Rs.Fifty Thousand only) for mental agony. That the compensation as prayed, is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a foul play by using the money of the applicant and by not delivering the unit within the agreed time period as mentioned in the agreement.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0pt; font-size: 10.5pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',5990530.00,5655261.00,'2016-04-02 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-02-14 00:00:00','2012-04-03 00:00:00','F-1403, 14th Flr., Tower \"F\", Sushma Chandigarh Grande, Bishangarh & Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur.','','',1,1,0,0,'madaansameer08012019','2019-01-14 12:10:03.000','madaansameer08012019','2019-01-14 12:10:03.000'),(269,1100,'1100',1334,'d2ee06f3-c476-4a55-a3b3-19a64b5572f1','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-19 13:32:08.000','Rishi Malhotra','fortunateme2@gmail.com',9971705420,0,0,'B105 SAINIK NAGAR','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','T1D403, OMAXE PALM GREEN','Sector MU',33,216,'201310','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0106','MTPL FTP90 , fashion technology park','Sumesh chawala ','roc@monatownships.com',8088098809,0,'MCH, SEC-115, KHARAR, LANDRAN ROAD, KHARAR','',28,507,'140603','1','MCH, SEC-115, KHARAR, LANDRAN ROAD, KHARAR','',28,507,'140603','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">I have booked\r\n100 sqft. commercial space in year 2006 in a project called fashion technology\r\npark greater mohali sector 90 with a builder called chandigarh overseas private\r\nlimited. We have booked and made payments in their New Delhi connaught place office\r\nat that time.&nbsp; Builder has promised to deliver the project in 3 years but\r\ntill now the project is not complete and builder has refused to return our hard\r\nearned money. we have tried to recover our money on multiple occasions that\r\nincludes visiting project site office several times, visiting booking office\r\nold and changed ones, written multiple mails, and tried to put pressure on\r\nbuilder through several several telephone calls at that time.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Builder has\r\nalso promised to pay fine if the project is not complete on time which is also\r\ndenied by the builder on several occasions.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">During this\r\ntenure from 2006 to 2019 builder has collaborated with different investors to\r\ncomplete the project without informing or intimating us. Also i have not\r\nreceived any relevant communication about the project status except their false\r\nassurances over phone. I have not received any written committed communication\r\nabout delivery of project as it was very uncertain from the builder\'s side,\r\nhence the builder did not commit.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Me and my\r\nfamily members have been mentally tortured throughout this long journey of\r\nrecovery of our hard earned money but till now there is no result.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">I need money\r\nback with interest and fine.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','made several phone calls, written mails, made site visits but given all the false assurances nothing else.',500000.00,475000.00,'2009-06-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2006-01-18 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Studio no.16, floor 5th, blockA2','','',1,0,0,0,'fortunateme2','2019-01-14 22:37:51.000','fortunateme2','2019-01-14 22:37:51.000'),(270,1101,'1101',1345,'b5b2009e-2c8e-49a3-97e7-2b6fec72df19','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','VINAY SOOD','vinay.sood@yahoo.co.in',9881732530,0,0,'A-402 AAKASHGANGA, RAHATANI','NEAR KONKANE CHOWK',21,470,'411017','1','A-402 AAKASHGANGA, RAHATANI','NEAR KONKANE CHOWK',21,470,'411017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','Getamber Anand','email@atsgreens.com',0,0,'711/92, Deepali','NEHRU PLACE NEW DELHI',10,120,'110019','1','711/92, Deepali','NEHRU PLACE NEW DELHI',10,120,'110019','1','<p>Facts and grounds of Complaint.\r\n</p><p>It is a case of delayed possession, hence claim for compensation in the form of Interest for delayed possession.\r\n</p><p>Developer entered into an Apartment buyer agreement, dated 27th March 2017. \r\n</p><p>Clause 6.2 states the Developer endeavour to complete the construction of the Apartment by December 2017, along with grace period of three months. The company will send the possession Notice and offer possession of the Apartment to the Applicant, as and when the company receives the occupation certificate from the competent authority.\r\n</p><p>Applicant after December asked the status of possession by personal visit to the e site, and through various phone calls but did not get any answer for the possession status.\r\n</p><p>On 18th March Applicant visited the site and was told that the construction going in full swing but without any commitment for the possession date, Applicant followed this visit with a mail dated 22/03, copy attached.\r\n</p><p>Applicant remained in constant contact with Developer over phone and then again followed with a mail on 6h June and reply received from Developer on 11th June, clearly saying that they do not have any clarity on the possession of the flat, hence  possession indefinitely\r\n</p><p>On 18th August again representative of Applicant visited the site and applicant followed with mail, copy attached wherein Developer was inform do of delay penalty claim at 18% interest on the money paid.\r\n</p><p>Since no satisfactory reply was coming for possession on 27th October applicant sent a speed post letter and also copied on a mail copy enclosed, wherein giving notice for delayed possession penalty at 12% interest.\r\n</p><p>Continuous follow up was made after this letter and mail and as late as at 17th December, the developed informed through e mail informed that they ae trying to complete the construction, on war footing basis, but no commitment was given for possession date.\r\n</p><p>On 10th January Developer sends the  Possession letter, and in that also it was mentione</p>','<p>In view of the facts given in para 4 above, we claim a relief of interest to be paid to us, for the period 01.01.2108 to 10.01.2019, without any demur.\r\n</p><p>The possession was promised on 31/12/2018, and possession letter issued on 10.01.2109, that too without copy of PCC.\r\n</p><p>We claim a delay interest on our deposit balance of Rs 78, 03,703.00 (as on 30.04.2017, @ 12% interest per annum), therefore our  claim stands at Rs 9.62,548.00.\r\n</p><p>Why 12% interest should be paid by the builder?\r\n</p><p>Refer to the clause 4.3 of the Apartment Buyer agreement, which states….Buyer shall be liable to make the payment of the balance instalments on receipt of the demand notice from the Developer, which shall inter alia state the completion of the corresponding construction stage. If the buyer fails to pay any instalment as and when demanded by the Developer, the Developer may grant the grace period of 30 days from the due date to the buyer to make the payment. However the buyer shall be liable to pay interest at 12% per annum on the unpaid amount computed from the commencement of grace period-balance money till the date of actual payment.\r\n</p><p>Therefore our demand for delayed possession claim @ 12% is justified.\r\n</p><p>Further  we state the Developer has not given any reasons for delay whatsoever, and repeatedly stated that construction is going in full swing, and the possession will be handed over as soon as possible, the last communication was of, as late as mail dated 17th December, copy exhibited.\r\n</p><p>According to Sec 18 (i) of the RERA Act, if the promoter fails to complete a project or unable to give possession of an apartment, plot or building, the allottee shall be paid interest for the period of delay in handing over the possession at a rate as may be prescribed. In this reference we refer to the judgement of MahaRERA under section 18 of the RERA Act, in his judgement, wherein eight complainants have been sold flats in Soham Builders project Tropical Lagoon on Ghod bunder Road, where Member Dr Vija</p>',9628400.00,9979132.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','2019-01-10 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-03-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','7191/Tower Number 7, VILLAGE BAD MAJRA MOHALI, DISTRICT SAS NAGAR','','',1,0,0,0,'SOODVINAY','2019-01-16 13:24:24.000','SOODVINAY','2019-01-16 13:24:24.000'),(271,1090,'1090',1191,'16dedd0c-2e6f-4eb1-85bb-f16106f43c42','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-16 16:02:12.000','NITIN Jindal','Nitin.email2me@gmail.com',8800669083,0,0,'D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','1','D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','Sushma Buildtech Limited','Bharat Mittal','Bharat@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'B 107, First Floor, Business Complex','Elante Mall, Industrial Area 1',6,128,'160002','1','B 107, First Floor, Business Complex','Elante Mall, Industrial Area 1',6,128,'160002','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><b>1. Delay in Possession\r\n(Section 18)</b>: My possession date as per agreement is 31-Mar, 2015\r\nand had paid about 85% of amount till Jul, 2014 (Rs 42,32,843).\r\nThis year builder had further demand – one in September (for flooring work) and\r\nfinal demand on offer the possession on 11 Dec, 2018 (that too without sharing occupancy certificate).&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">&nbsp;.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><b>2. Multiple\r\nchanges in Specification without information (</b>Under section 19): Rights and\r\nDuties of Allottees, Builder had changes the layout and specification without\r\nany notification and also not ready to share the details (moreover provided\r\nincorrect information that they have not made any changes). One example is the\r\nchange in location of the swimming pool, now constructed in front of my tower\r\n(instead originally not proposed at that location). This is unacceptable.</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><b>3. Not\r\nsharing information&nbsp;</b><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">(</span>Under section 19)<span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">:&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px;\">Builder is not ready to share the specification details and also partial occupancy certificate. But forcing me to pay the final demand for offer of possession (applies 24% interest penalty).</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><b>4.&nbsp;</b><b style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Not delivered as promised at the time of sale (Section 12 &amp; 14):&nbsp;</b><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">As the time of sale builder promised to provide covered car parking, but now providing open parking.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: small;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">1. As per Section 19, Builder must provide the details of any changes and penalty should be applied considering wrong information was shared. Also as promoter is not ready to share the partial occupancy certificate and not&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">responding</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">&nbsp;to queries, so request to compensate for the same.</span></font></p><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">2. As per section 12, 14, 18, promoter need to compensate for not delivering as promised at the time of sale and also compensation for the delay in&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">possession</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">. I shall submit a separate application (Form M) for interest penalty due to delay in&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">possession.</span></font></div><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\"><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\">3. Harassment, mental agony compensation and other expenses to be paid by promoter.</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;</div>',5053900.00,5006075.00,'2015-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-11-05 00:00:00','2012-03-21 00:00:00','704, Tower F, Sushma Crescent, Sushma Tower','','',2,0,0,0,'Nitinjindal0505','2019-01-16 18:14:57.000','Nitinjindal0505','2019-01-16 18:14:57.000'),(272,1090,'1090',1191,'16dedd0c-2e6f-4eb1-85bb-f16106f43c42','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-18 11:25:05.000','NITIN Jindal','Nitin.email2me@gmail.com',8800669083,0,0,'D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','1','D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','Sushma Buildtech Limited','Bharat Mittal','Bharat@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'B 107, First Floor, Business Complex','Elante Mall, Industrial Area 1',6,128,'160002','1','B 107, First Floor, Business Complex','Elante Mall, Industrial Area 1',6,128,'160002','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><b>1. Delay in Possession\r\n(Section 18)</b>: My possession date as per agreement is 31-Mar, 2015\r\nand had paid about 85% of amount till Jul, 2014 (Rs 42,32,843).\r\nThis year builder had further demand – one in September (for flooring work) and\r\nfinal demand on offer the possession on 11 Dec, 2018 (that too without sharing occupancy certificate).&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">&nbsp;.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><b>2. Multiple\r\nchanges in Specification without information (</b>Under section 19): Rights and\r\nDuties of Allottees, Builder had changes the layout and specification without\r\nany notification and also not ready to share the details (moreover provided\r\nincorrect information that they have not made any changes). One example is the\r\nchange in location of the swimming pool, now constructed in front of my tower\r\n(instead originally not proposed at that location). This is unacceptable.</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><b>3. Not\r\nsharing information&nbsp;</b><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">(</span>Under section 19)<span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">:&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 14.6667px;\">Builder is not ready to share the specification details and also partial occupancy certificate. But forcing me to pay the final demand for offer of possession (applies 24% interest penalty).</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><b>4.&nbsp;</b><b style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Not delivered as promised at the time of sale (Section 12 &amp; 14):&nbsp;</b><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">As the time of sale builder promised to provide covered car parking, but now providing open parking.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-size: small;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">1. As per Section 19, Builder must provide the details of any changes and penalty should be applied considering wrong information was shared. Also as promoter is not ready to share the partial occupancy certificate and not&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">responding</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">&nbsp;to queries, so request to compensate for the same.</span></font></p><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">2. As per section 12, 14, 18, promoter need to compensate for not delivering as promised at the time of sale and also compensation for the delay in&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">possession</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">. I shall submit a separate application (Form M) for interest penalty due to delay in&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">possession.</span></font></div><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\"><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\">3. Harassment, mental agony compensation and other expenses to be paid by promoter.</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;</div>',5053900.00,5006075.00,'2015-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-11-05 00:00:00','2012-03-21 00:00:00','704, Tower F, Sushma Crescent, Sushma Tower','','',1,1,0,0,'Nitinjindal0505','2019-01-16 18:15:34.000','Nitinjindal0505','2019-01-16 18:15:34.000'),(273,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-17 16:55:41.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA\r\nVillage Budmajra,\r\nKharar, Sector 121,\r\nS.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd ','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I purchased an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt.\r\nLtd. The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized\r\n2400 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.9158000/- Plus taxes.\r\nI’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the company. I paid Rs.50,000/-\r\non dated 31/1/2017, Rs.49,50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. The\r\nCompany, executed Apartment Buyer Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of\r\nthe flat in question, on 9<sup>th</sup> February, 2017. The builder/company\r\npromised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017.\r\nHowever, the company reserved a grace period of 3 months for possession of the\r\napartment. Thus the effective date of possession was March 2018. Unfortunately,\r\ndespite having paid 95% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver\r\nthe possession of the flat.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;Here it is also pertinent to mention that I have taken a HOME LOAN from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying\r\nhuge amount of interest, every month. Here it is also relevant to mention that since I have taken home loan from HDFC, all the documents like allotment letter, apartment buyer agreement, payment receipts&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">pertaining to the flat unit in question</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">were handed over by the builder company directly to the bank/financier. The builder company only handed over Copy of Apartment Buyer Agreement to me and no other document whatsoever.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I\'ve been visiting the builder / company office and contacting\r\nthe officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and to\r\nknow the actual date of possession, to no avail though.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">That as per the allotment letter cum agreement, the\r\ncompany is charging penal interest from the buyers <b><u>@12% &nbsp;to &nbsp;&nbsp;18% per annum</u></b>, for delay in making\r\npayment, as and when demanded by the builder/company. I’ve paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- to the company.\r\nHowever, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for\r\nno rhyme or reason. The builder has neither offered possession yet, nor paid\r\nany COMPENSATION AS PER THE PROVISIONS OF RERA. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Here it also worth mentioning that during\r\nthis entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or\r\ncircumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company\r\nmight try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u><br></u></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u>&nbsp; &nbsp; RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">FOR INORDINATE DELAY IN POSSESSION&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp;OR&nbsp; COMPENSATION, AS PER THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF RERA. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; I HAVE PAID RS.88,30,492/- WHICH AMOUNTS TO OVER 95% OF THE TOTAL SALE CONSIDERATION, SINCE ALMOST 2 YEARS</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2019-01-17 16:55:36.000','rachnabhi','2019-01-17 16:55:36.000'),(274,1102,'1102',1314,'04fa3bcf-efed-4da9-83be-a5a0ee84d0da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-21 07:27:41.000','Rajiv Chhabra','deepam.adv@outlook.com',9953315000,0,0,'Villa no. 238, Vipul Tatvan Villa','Sector-48',13,5,'122001','1','Civil Lines','Sector-48',13,5,'122001','Deepam Raghava','deepam.adv@gmail.com',9953315000,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','Mohali Hills','EMAAR MGF','feedback@emaar-india.com',0,0,'SCO no. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO no. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C',6,128,'160017','0','<p>1.	The complainant applied for a plot at Augusta Park, Sector – 109, Mohali Hills, Mohali (Punjab) super area admeasuring 300 yd.2 for a total cost of Rs. 34,50,000 at the rate of 11,500 per square yards as basic sale price. The total cost was Rs. 36,19,104/– including external development charges of Rs. 1,69,104. On the same day the complainant paid the 1st instalment of Rs. 10,25,000/– i.e. 30 percent of the basic Sale Price (BSP) on dated 19/06/2007. A plot buyers agreement vide application no. 1447 dated 19/06/2007 was also executed between the parties to the complaint at Chandigarh.\r\n</p><p>2.	A plot bearing no. 499 in Augusta Park, sector – 109, Augusta Park, Sector – 109, Mohali Hills, Mohali (Punjab) was allotted in the name of the complainant and the agreement was duly executed on the same day under the signature of the complainant.\r\n</p><p>3.	The complainant had paid an amount of Rs. 10,35,000 on dated 19/06/2007, Rs. 1,72,450 on dated 11/09/2007, Rs. 1,72,500 on dated 10/03/2008, Rs. 3,45,000 on dated 15/05/2008 and an amount of Rs. 3,45,000 on dated 01/08/2008.\r\n</p><p>4.	The possession was to be delivered within a period of 2 years of the execution of the aforesaid agreement, but not later than 3 years.\r\n</p><p>5.	The respondent was unable to fulfil the conditions of the agreement dated 19/06/2007 and requested the complainant to amend the agreement dated 19/06/2007. A new amended agreement dated 12/04/2012 was executed between the complainant and respondent vide which the complainant was again allotted a plot bearing no. 26 situated in Block no. MLU admeasuring 300 yd.2 in Sector – 108, Mohali (Punjab).\r\n</p><p>6.	The complainant requested the respondents to fulfil the conditions of the amended agreement dated 12/04/2012 and requested the respondent to hand over the possession of the plot but all in vain. Finally on dated 20/02/2018 the complainant sent a legal notice to the respondent but no reply was send by the respondent.\r\n Hence this complaint.</p>','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to hand over the physical possession of the plot/apartment to the complainant or to direct the respondent to refund the entire amount paid by the complainant i.e. Rs. 20,69,950 along with 18 percent interest from the date of respective payment till the actual realization of the entire amount.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to hand over the physical possession of the plot/apartment.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to refund illegally unexplained and this excessively charged amount from the complaint, along with interest these in &amp; 18 percent premium w.e.f the dater of Said charging till the refund in made.&nbsp;</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay complaint for the torture, sufferings, harassment and embarrassment etc. caused to the complaint the reports their neglectful attitude in dealing with the complainant.&nbsp;</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To award compensation to the complaint and penalty upon the respondent for the said unfair trade practice and deficiency in service.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay interest &amp; 18 percent per annum on the amounts charged illegally and so advance as registration charges and stamp duty etc, being not required at that time.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay Rs. 50 per square yards per month as penalty for delaying in delivering the possession of the said plot/apartment to the complainant as agreed by both the parties in the agreement.</p><p>8.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief (s) which this Hon\'ble Authority may deem fit and proper may also be granted in favour of the complainant and against the respondent.</p><div><br></div>',3450000.00,2069950.00,'2010-06-19 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2007-06-19 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','499, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills,  Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'deepam1983','2019-01-18 12:46:16.000','deepam1983','2019-01-18 12:46:16.000'),(275,1103,'1103',1336,'8a3f1fab-d113-44e2-80ff-3b7cfc2e5188','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Anjana  Anand','KULWINDERSINGHADVOCATE@GMAIL.COM',9872903100,0,0,'H1-103, Maya Garden City','Zirakpur, District Mohali',28,507,'140603','1','H1-103, Maya Garden City','Zirakpur, District Mohali',28,507,'140603','Kulwinder Singh','ksvarun513@gmail.com',9915772513,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0192','Maya Garden City','Maya Garden City','barnalabuilders@ymail.com',9216910335,0,'Opposite McDonald\'s, Chandigarh-Ambala Highway','Zirakpur, Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','Opposite McDonald\'s, Chandigarh-Ambala Highway','Zirakpur, Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','<p><br></p><p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That applicant booked 5BHK flat for her own residence in the project of respondent no. 1 vide application dated 08.12.2012 and the respondent issued allotment of flat no. 103 measuring 2850 Sq. Ft. in H1 block at first floor vide letter dated 14.12.2012. The applicant entered into agreement to sell with respondent, as per which total consideration of flat was Rs. 63,00,000/-. As per clause 5 of agreement the date of sale deed was fixed on or before 30th November, 2014. The applicants paid Rs. 68,41,850/- with the respondent against total consideration of Rs. 63,00,000/- which includes maintenance, late payment charges and service tax etc.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per brochure, respondents are liable to provide club house facility and swimming pool etc which were also not provided by respondents till date. The possession was to be handed over on or before 30.11.2014 but the same was offered on 15.04.2016 and the sale deed was also to be done 0n 30.11.2014 which was done on 22.03.2018 in favor of applicant. It is relevant to mention here that the respondents failed to get completion certificate from competent authority and the partial completion certificate issued to respondent was conditional &amp; due to non fulfillment of conditions the pollution control board has already written letter to competent authority to cancel the partial completion certificate.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That applicant requested number of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed resolve the issues raised by applicant and to provide occupation/completion certificate even after receiving legal notice.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the applicant requested number to times to respondent through letter and emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and other issues but the respondent failed to revert&nbsp; any of letter/email sent by applicant.</p><div><br></div>','<p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay Rs. 8,02,000 as per valuation report to make the flat in the position as promised by the respondent.&nbsp;</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000 (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing mental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering service and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To remove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc and to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount received as service tax from the applicant since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned department.</p><p>e.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount for giving less carpet area.</p><p>f.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give NEC and get the sale deed done as per RERA with clear carpet area in favour of the applicant.</p><p>g.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay interest @ 18% on the amount of Rs. 63,00,000 from the due date of possession i.e. 30 Nov 2014 till the date of sale deed/issuance of completion certificate.</p><p>h.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide club/swimming pool etc alongwith all facilities as per promise made in brochure.</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide all other facilities which are promised by not provided like provision of DTH, Broadband, Intercom Facility, approach from Highway.</p><p>j.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- as litigation expenses.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Or Any other order as the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances in favour of the Applicant be passed, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6300000.00,6841850.00,'2014-11-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-12-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','H1-103, Maya Garden City, Zirakpur, District Mohali\r\n','','',1,0,0,0,'ANJANAANAND','2019-01-18 15:48:29.000','ANJANAANAND','2019-01-18 15:48:29.000'),(276,1104,'1104',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-18 19:03:02.000','RAJ KUMAR AND KULJEET KAUR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,999057822446,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0005','JOSAN HEIGHTS','JSJ Builders Pvt Ltd','jsjbuilders.in@gmail.com',8699885568,0,'Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','<p>The complainants had booked a unit with super area measuring 1423 Sq. Ft. at OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS on 04.10.2016.&nbsp; That on 04.10.2016, the OP furnished an Allotment letter against the unit and allotted UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK C, MEASURING 1423 SQ. FT in OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS. It was stated in the Allotment letter that the possession will be handed over by 25.10.2016.</p><p>That on 04.10.2016, the OP executed a BUILDER BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and assured promised to hand over the possession of the unit&nbsp; including all the amenities as per the brochure That on 25.10.2016, OP offered the possession of the unit to the complainant but neither did OP did had the completion certificate for the project nor had the occupation certificate before offering possession to the complainants in 2016.</p><p>That the OP directed the complainants to execute the sale deed against the said unit and the same was executed. That it is pertinent to mention here that the OP received the PARTIAL COMPLETION CERTIFICATE on 14.12.2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of possession and OP has yet to receive Occupation certificate from the concerned authority and has offered possession of the unit without possessing OCCUPATION CERTIFICATE.</p><p>That OP has failed to completely develop the project as per the brochure and has taken complete consideration against the unit from the complainants and has offered possession of the unit without possessing occupancy certificate, till date and has even allowed 4 Mobile towers to be installed it its project without approval violation of Section 12 as well as causing mental physical harassment. Therefore, the complainants craves the indulgence of the HONBLE ADJUDICATING OFFICER, RERA PUNJAB to direct the OP to hand over the compensation along with damages, as the OP failed to comply with its legal obligation according to the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016 and Punjab Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017.</p>','<p>i<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for not completing the project as per brochure and commitments made to the RERA AUTHORITY, especially Gym, Swimming Pool, Club House etc. , till date under Section 12 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016</p><p><br></p><p>ii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to remove the MOBILE Towers Installed above the residential Towers and pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000 FIVE LAKS for causing serious health hazard by installing the same.</p><p><br></p><p>iii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>iv<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>v<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to complete all the infractions committed by the OP as per the brochure as soon as possible</p><p><br></p><p>vi<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants was constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite party.</p><p><br></p><p>vii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Adjudicating Officer deems appropriate.</p>',3000000.00,3000000.00,'2016-10-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-10-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK-C, JOSAN HEIGHTS, SECTOR-126, CHHAJUMAJRA, SAS NAGAR (MOHALI), PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-01-18 18:04:00.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-01-18 18:04:00.000'),(277,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-17 16:55:41.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA\r\nVillage Budmajra,\r\nKharar, Sector 121,\r\nS.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd ','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I purchased an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt.\r\nLtd. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized\r\n2400 sq ft. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.9158000/- Plus taxes.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the builder/company. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I paid Rs.50,000/-\r\non dated 31/1/2017, Rs.49,50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The\r\nCompany, executed Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of\r\nthe flat in question, on 9<sup>th</sup> February, 2017. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The builder/company\r\npromised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017. Unfortunately,\r\ndespite having paid 95% of the total amount, and January of 2019 underway, the company has failed to deliver\r\nthe possession of the flat.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;Here it is also pertinent to mention that I have taken a HOME LOAN from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying\r\nhuge amount to the bank, every month. Here it is also relevant to mention that since I have taken home loan from HDFC, all the documents like allotment letter, apartment buyer agreement, payment receipts&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">pertaining to the flat unit in question</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">were handed over by the builder company directly to the bank/financier. The builder company only handed over very limited documents to me, which i am enclosing herewith this complaint.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I\'ve been visiting the builder / company office and contacting\r\nthe officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and seeking information regarding the actual date of possession,&nbsp; but to no avail though.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">That I’ve paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- out of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">9158000&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">to the company since last almost two years.\r\nHowever, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for\r\nno rhyme or reason. The builder has not paid\r\nany COMPENSATION AS PER THE PROVISIONS OF RERA.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Here it also worth mentioning that during\r\nthis entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or\r\ncircumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company\r\nmight try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u><br></u></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u>RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">FOR INORDINATE DELAY IN POSSESSION&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp;OR&nbsp; COMPENSATION, AS PER THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF RERA.</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2019-01-20 00:12:16.000','rachnabhi','2019-01-20 00:12:16.000'),(278,1068,'1068',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-17 16:55:41.000','Rachna Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vi