de &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u><br></u></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:15.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><b><u>RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18.6667px;\">FOR : *(1) Physical Harassment, *(2) Mental Harassment and Agony, *(3) Emotional Distress, *(4) Site Visit Expenses, *(5) Financial and Professional Loss suffered due to loss of precious time *(6) Legal Expenses&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&amp; / OR any other amount that this Hon\'ble Authority deems appropriate, proper and just.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'rachnabhi','2019-01-24 14:22:39.000','rachnabhi','2019-01-24 14:22:39.000'),(284,1105,'1105',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,832756086566,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD\r\nProject :  Falcon View','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD','janta@jantahousing.com',8427100082,0,'Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','<p>I filed an application AdCNo10222018 under Form N which was returned by the Hon’ble AO on 1-11-18, since I had sought Compensation in form of Interest. Therefore I hereby file this application under Form N once again, seeking compensation, other than interest.</p><p>\r\nIn my capacity as KARTA of Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak HUF, I, purchased an apartment from M/s. Janta Land Promoters Pvt Ltd. The apartment Unit No. is 101, Tower D, Falcon View, sized 3122 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.96,17,477/- Plus taxes. I paid Rs.96,43,228/- to the company vide the following : I paid Rs.84,35,750/- vide Receipt No. 6518 dated 13/8/2016, Rs.11,12,000/- vide Receipt No.3104 dated 13/8/2016 &amp; Rs.95,478/- vide Receipt No. 6826 dated 28/9/2016. Thus altogether I\'ve paid 96% of the Total consideration amount. The Company, vide Allotment Letter dated 13/08/2016, promised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment in 12 months. Thus the effective date of possession was 13/08/2017. Unfortunately, despite having paid 96% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver the possession of the flat. Thus our joint family is compelled to live separately. My parents live in Yamunanagar whereas I live in Mohali in a small accommodation. We have been compelled to compromise with our comfort &amp; our future plannings. </p><p>I\'ve been running from pillar to post to get the true status of construction &amp; the date of actual possession, but to no avail. The office bearers of the company refuse to entertain my requests &amp; divulge any relevant information. I\'ve sent  dozens of e-mails to the company &amp; its top officials, for confirming the date of possession &amp; for seeking compensation.&nbsp; </p><p>I keep visiting the site regularly, to be disappointed at the progress of  my flat, whereas, in contrast,  I witness very good speed of work at newly launched towers in the same project. The company keeps on launching and selling newer towers while failing to handover possession to the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">earlier buyers.</span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">That the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for no rhyme or reason. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Here it also worth mentioning that during this entire period of inordinate delay, the company kept on launching newer &amp; newer towersin the same project,“Falcon View” &amp; kept selling them. It is also pertinent to mention that the work at these newly launched towers is going on uninterrupted &amp; at war footing. Thus there has not been any force majure or circumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company might try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This uncertainty &amp; anxiety is multi folds for me because of two other reasons ( For which the cause of action has not yet arisen but may arise, if the company continues to delay the possession of my apartment &amp; I may end up suffering huge amounts for no faults of mine, for which, I reserve my right to approach appropriate legal forums to recover these losses, if &amp; when they occur.) :  Firstly  That I sold my industrial unit on 12 August 2016 &amp; purchased this apartment on 13 August 2016. Thus I saved Long Term Capitals Gain Tax . As per I.T. Act, if I do not get possession of new residential property in 36 months from date of sale of industrial unit, I shall have to return, entire LTCG Tax Rebate availed, with interest, which in my case may be about Rs.15 Lac Loss. Secondly That the Punjab Government has given a rebate of 3% on stamp duty for registrations till 31-3-2019. If the company delays in possession furthermore, I may suffer another loss of about Rs.3 Lac. \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :       I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS FOR : *(1) Physical Harassment, *(2) Mental Harassment and Agony, *(3) Emotional Distress and Anxiety, *(4) Site Visit Expenses, *(5) Financial and Professional Loss suffered due to loss of precious time *(6) Legal Expenses     &amp; / OR  any other amount that this Hon\'ble&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Adjudicating Officer deems appropriate, proper and just.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p>',9617477.00,9643228.00,'2017-08-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-13 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.101, Tower-D, JLPL Falcon View, Sector 66-A, Mohali-Punjab.','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2019-01-24 15:56:54.000','rachnabhi','2019-01-24 15:56:54.000'),(285,1105,'1105',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,832756086566,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD\r\nProject :  Falcon View','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD','janta@jantahousing.com',8427100082,0,'Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','<p>I filed an application AdCNo10222018 under Form N which was returned by the Hon’ble AO on 1-11-18, since I had sought Compensation in form of Interest. Therefore I hereby file this application under Form N once again, seeking compensation, other than interest.</p><p>\r\nIn my capacity as KARTA of Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak HUF, I, purchased an apartment from M/s. Janta Land Promoters Pvt Ltd. The apartment Unit No