 witness very good speed of work at newly launched towers in the same project. The company keeps on launching and selling newer towers while failing to handover possession to the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">earlier buyers.</span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">That the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for no rhyme or reason. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Here it also worth mentioning that during this entire period of inordinate delay, the company kept on launching newer &amp; newer towersin the same project,“Falcon View” &amp; kept selling them. It is also pertinent to mention that the work at these newly launched towers is going on uninterrupted &amp; at war footing. Thus there has not been any force majure or circumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company might try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This uncertainty &amp; anxiety is multi folds for me because of two other reasons ( For which the cause of action has not yet arisen but may arise, if the company continues to delay the possession of my apartment &amp; I may end up suffering huge amounts for no faults of mine, for which, I reserve my right to approach appropriate legal forums to recover these losses, if &amp; when they occur.) :  Firstly  That I sold my industrial unit on 12 August 2016 &amp; purchased this apartment on 13 August 2016. Thus I saved Long Term Capitals Gain Tax . As per I.T. Act, if I do not get possession of new residential property in 36 months from date of sale of industrial unit, I shall have to return, entire LTCG Tax Rebate availed, with interest, which in my case may be about Rs.15 Lac Loss. Secondly That the Punjab Government has given a rebate of 3% on stamp duty for registrations till 31-3-2019. If the company delays in possession furthermore, I may suffer another loss of about Rs.3 Lac. \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :       I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS FOR : *(1) Physical Harassment, *(2) Mental Harassment and Agony, *(3) Emotional Distress and Anxiety, *(4) Site Visit Expenses, *(5) Financial and Professional Loss suffered due to loss of precious time *(6) Legal Expenses     &amp; / OR  any other amount that this Hon\'ble&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Adjudicating Officer deems appropriate, proper and just.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p>',9617477.00,9643228.00,'2017-08-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-13 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.101, Tower-D, JLPL Falcon View, Sector 66-A, Mohali-Punjab.','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2019-01-25 14:29:25.000','rachnabhi','2019-01-25 14:29:25.000'),(289,1105,'1105',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,832756086566,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD\r\nProject :  Falcon View','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD','janta@jantahousing.com',8427100082,0,'Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','<p>I filed an application AdCNo10222018 under Form N which was returned by the Hon’ble AO on 1-11-18, since I had sought Compensation in form of Interest. Therefore I hereby file this application under Form N once again, seeking compensation, other than interest.</p><p>\r\nIn my capacity as KARTA of Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak HUF, I, purchased an