0,'Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','<p>I filed an application AdCNo10222018 under Form N which was returned by the Hon’ble AO on 1-11-18, since I had sought Compensation in form of Interest. Therefore I hereby file this application under Form N once again, seeking compensation, other than interest.</p><p>\r\nIn my capacity as KARTA of Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak HUF, I, purchased an apartment from M/s. Janta Land Promoters Pvt Ltd. The apartment Unit No. is 101, Tower D, Falcon View, sized 3122 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at Rs.96,17,477/- Plus taxes. I paid Rs.96,43,228/- to the company vide the following : I paid Rs.84,35,750/- vide Receipt No. 6518 dated 13/8/2016, Rs.11,12,000/- vide Receipt No.3104 dated 13/8/2016 &amp; Rs.95,478/- vide Receipt No. 6826 dated 28/9/2016. Thus altogether I\'ve paid 96% of the Total consideration amount. The Company, vide Allotment Letter dated 13/08/2016, promised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment in 12 months. Thus the effective date of possession was 13/08/2017. Unfortunately, despite having paid 96% of the total amount, the company has failed to deliver the possession of the flat. Thus our joint family is compelled to live separately. My parents live in Yamunanagar whereas I live in Mohali in a small accommodation. We have been compelled to compromise with our comfort &amp; our future plannings. </p><p>I\'ve been running from pillar to post to get the true status of construction &amp; the date of actual possession, but to no avail. The office bearers of the company refuse to entertain my requests &amp; divulge any relevant information. I\'ve sent  dozens of e-mails to the company &amp; its top officials, for confirming the date of possession &amp; for seeking compensation.&nbsp; </p><p>I keep visiting the site regularly, to be disappointed seeing the progress of  my flat, whereas, in contrast,  I witness very good speed of work at newly launched towers in the same project. The company keeps on launching and selling newer towers while failing to handover possession to the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">earlier buyers.</span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">That the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for no rhyme or reason. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Here it also worth mentioning that during this entire period of inordinate delay, the company kept on launching newer &amp; newer towers in the same project,“Falcon View” &amp; kept selling them. It is also pertinent to mention that the work at these newly launched towers is going on uninterrupted &amp; at war footing. Thus there has not been any force majure or circumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company might try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This uncertainty &amp; anxiety is multi folds for me because of two other reasons ( For which the cause of action has not yet arisen but may arise, if the company continues to delay the possession of my apartment &amp; I may end up suffering huge amounts for no faults of mine, for which, I reserve my right to approach appropriate legal forums to recover these losses, if &amp; when they occur.) :  Firstly  That I sold my industrial unit on 12 August 2016 &amp; purchased this apartment on 13 August 2016. Thus I saved Long Term Capitals Gain Tax . As per I.T. Act, if I do not get possession of new residential property in 36 months from date of sale of industrial unit, I shall have to return, entire LTCG Tax Rebate availed, with interest, which in my case may be about Rs.15 Lac Loss. Secondly That the Punjab Government has given a rebate of 3% on stamp duty for registrations till 31-3-2019. If the company delays in possession furthermore, I may suffer another loss of about Rs.3 Lac. \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :       I SEEK COMPENSATION OF RS.10 LACS FOR : *(1) Physical Harassment, *(2) Mental Harassment and Agony, *(3) Emotional Distress and Anxiety, *(4) Site Visit Expenses, *(5) Financial and Professional Loss suffered due to loss of precious time *(6) Legal Expenses     &amp; / OR  any other amount that this Hon\'ble&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Adjudicating Officer deems appropriate, proper and just.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p>',9617477.00,9643228.00,'2017-08-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-08-13 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.101, Tower-D, JLPL Falcon View, Sector 66-A, Mohali-Punjab.','','',1,1,0,0,'rachnabhi','2019-01-29 10:52:19.000','rachnabhi','2019-01-29 10:52:19.000'),(293,1104,'1104',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-30 19:37:01.000','RAJ KUMAR AND KULJEET KAUR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,999057822446,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0005','JOSAN HEIGHTS','JSJ Builders Pvt Ltd','jsjbuilders.in@gmail.com',8699885568,0,'Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','<p>The complainants had booked a unit with super area measuring 1423 Sq. Ft. at OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS on 04.10.2016.&nbsp; That on 04.10.2016, the OP furnished an Allotment letter against the unit and allotted UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK C, MEASURING 1423 SQ. FT in OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS. It was stated in the Allotment letter that the possession will be handed over by 25.10.2016.</p><p>That on 04.10.2016, the OP executed a BUILDER BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and assured promised to hand over the possession of the unit&nbsp; including all the amenities as per the brochure That on 25.10.2016, OP offered the possession of the unit to the complainant but neither did OP did had the completion certificate for the project nor had the occupation certificate before offering possession to the complainants in 2016.</p><p>That the OP directed the complainants to execute the sale deed against the said unit and the same was executed. That it is pertinent to mention here that the OP received the PARTIAL COMPLETION CERTIFICATE on 14.12.2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of possession and OP has yet to receive Occupation certificate from the concerned authority and has offered possession of the unit without possessing OCCUPATION CERTIFICATE.</p><p>That OP has failed to completely develop the project as per the brochure and has taken complete consideration against the unit from the complainants and has offered possession of the unit without possessing occupancy certificate, till date. Therefore, the complainants craves the indulgence of the HONBLE ADJUDICATING OFFICER, RERA PUNJAB to direct the OP to hand over the compensation along with damages, as the OP failed to comply with its legal obligation according to the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016 and Punjab Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017.</p>','<p>i<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for not completing the project as per brochure and commitments made to the RERA AUTHORITY, especially Gym, Swimming Pool, Club House etc. , till date under Section 12 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016</p><p><br></p><p>ii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>iii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>iv<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to complete all the infractions committed by the OP as per the brochure as soon as possible</p><p><br></p><p>v<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants was constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite party.</p><p><br></p><p>vi<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Adjudicating Officer deems appropriate.</p>',3000000.00,3000000.00,'2016-10-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-10-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK-C, JOSAN HEIGHTS, SECTOR-126, CHHAJUMAJRA, SAS NAGAR (MOHALI), PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-01-30 19:36:48.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-01-30 19:36:48.000'),(294,1106,'1106',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','yash paul Kathpal','ykathpal@yahoo.com',9814466639,0,0,'Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','Saksham Arora','saacounselors@gmail.com',9872628189,9041300773,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','M/S Ansals Housing and construction Pvt ltd','ahcl@ansals.com',0,1123350847,'606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt