text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Assuming the work is now over &amp;\r\nthe flat is ready for possession in Jan 19, there is &nbsp;&nbsp;a gap of approximately 48 months (Dec 2014 to\r\nJan 19) and current rate of interest offered by SBI is approximately 7.00%.\r\nTotal amount paid till date is 24.22 Lakhs. After taking all the factors into\r\nconsideration the interest amount for 48 months comes down to Rs. 6.78 Lakhs. The\r\nagreement also suggests that possession can only be taken after &nbsp;&nbsp;clearance of account. Balance amount now payable\r\nis Rs. -5.51 Lakhs (1.27 lakhs - 6.78 lakhs). <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">In view of the facts mentioned in\r\npara 4,I, Suman Dhaundiyal, prays for the compensation of Rs.<b>6.78 Lakhs<o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',2550000.00,2422000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NO-950,FLOOR NO-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI,DISTT. MOHALI,PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-02-05 09:49:38.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-02-05 09:49:38.000'),(302,1111,'1111',1364,'35ea0d15-93a6-49f4-afc6-fcb51741f763','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-06 16:17:32.000','Harvinder Singh','narinder2273@gmail.com',9914952929,0,0,'J 403, Imperial Heights, Sector 115','Kharar - Landran road',28,507,'140307','1','#2273, Sector 44C','Chandigarh',6,128,'160043','Narinder Pal Sharma','narinder2273@gmail.com',9876609052,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0046','Imperial Heights','WWICS ESTATES PVT. LTD','info@wwicsestates.com',9888909978,0,'A-12, Industrial Area, Phase-VI, Mohali','',28,507,'160055','1','A-12, Industrial Area, Phase-VI, Mohali','',28,507,'160055','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1. Apartment\r\nNo.J-403 was allotted to the complainant on fourth floor at the basic price of\r\nRs. 26,66,850/- which was subsequently converted to Subvention Scheme and\r\naccordingly basic price was enhanced to Rs. 28,40,775/- and according to this\r\nscheme, the allottee was not required to make the EMI till the date of\r\npossession of the Flat. However, after 2 years of Subvention Scheme the respondent\r\nasked to complainant to start paying pre-EMI (PEMI) on the total bank loan\r\namount (that was Rs.22,28,930/- )which was not as per the letter addressed to\r\nthe complainant which was received from the respondent about explaining the\r\nsubvention scheme. The respondent withdraws full payment from the bank loan\r\naccount within 2 years&nbsp; which caused heavy pre EMI on the complainant\r\nwithout possession. The Pre-EMI was started on July 2014 and the complainant\r\ngot the possession on November 2017, As such, the complainant is entitled to\r\npay interest on the loan amount which was paid before the possession. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 6pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2. The\r\nrespondent imposed the possession on 15.11.2017 and demanded maintenance\r\ncharges without completing the construction work and agreed amenities of the\r\nproject. There were almost remaining 30 percent work which was not done till\r\nthe possession that is Club House, Central Park, Paints, Ducts not covered,\r\nRoads, Adequate Lighting, stone rubbing/Finishing, Intercom etc. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 6pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">3.\r\nFurther, the Company/respondent is not getting the sale deed executed despite\r\nreceiving the demanded sale deed/stamp duty amount of Rs 2,21,392 on 06-03-2018\r\nfor which the complainant has filed complaint separately in Form ‘M’ (Complaint\r\nDiary No: GCNo12012019) before this Hon’ble Regulatory Authority. Still\r\nfurther, it is submitted that the Respondent/Company is demanding maintenance\r\ncharges without extending any required facilities. Therefore, due to the act\r\nand conduct of the respondent/Company, the Complainant has suffered great\r\nmental as well as physical stress &amp; strain.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:1.3pt;margin-right:24.55pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:90.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:\r\n16.8pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">a)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7pt;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Respondent/Company be directed to pay Rs.50000/- as\r\ncompensation for harassment and mental agony along with the interest on the\r\ndeposited sale deed amount to Respondent.</span><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:90.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:16.8pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">b)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7pt;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The respondent/ Company may be directed to pay to\r\nthe Complainant the cost of litigation amounting to Rs. 15,000/-.</span><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:90.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:16.8pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">c)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7pt;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The respondent/ Company may also be directed to pay\r\nto the Complainant the total interest paid as pre-EMI till the possession of\r\nthe apartment.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:90.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:16.8pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">d)&nbsp;</span><font face=\"roboto, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">The respondent/ Company may be directed to complete the amenities before demanded for full maintenance&nbsp;changes.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:90.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:16.8pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">e)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 7pt;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Any other relief that this Hon’ble Authority deems\r\nfit and proper in view of the facts and circumstances of the complaint, may\r\nalso be awarded to the Complainants in the interest of justice.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:90.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:16.8pt\"><br></p>',3166519.00,3166519.00,'2015-06-30 00:00:00.000','2017-11-15 00:00:00.000','','1','','2011-12-26 00:00:00','2012-06-20 00:00:00','J403, Imperial Heights Sector 115, Kharar- Landran road, SAS Nagar, Mohali 140307','','',1,1,0,0,'narinder2273','2019-02-06 15:33:12.000','narinder2273','2019-02-06 15:33:12.000'),(303,1106,'1106',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-07 14:54:31.000','yash paul Kathpal','ykathpal@yahoo.com',9814466639,0,0,'Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','Saksham Arora','saacounselors@gmail.com',9872628189,9041300773,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','M/S Ansals Housing and construction Pvt ltd','ahcl@ansals.com',0,1123350847,'606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">The Owner of the flat in dispute had got the possession of the flat 31-Oct-2013 (annexure a2). At the time of purchasing the flat the owner was promised several features but they turned out to be a Sham. Not only did all the salient features (annexure a2) be bypassed along with all local rules, but also in the name of cover car parking (annexure a5) stilt parking has been provided. The complainant was thereafter charged for auto change panel but hasn\'t been provided with it till date(annexure a4). The society doesn\'t stand a completion certificate even after 10 years, even when their newspaper advertisement reads possession in 2009 (annexure a2). The Municipal Council has also in its letter stated that the possession of the flats should be stopped because of several discrepancies(annexure a3) which also puts a light at the intent and nature of the op to surpass rules for the purpose of its own gains. The Op has also crossed the terms of the tripartite agreement(annexure a7), by charging a huge amount than promised(annexure a6).&nbsp; The op for the purpose of creating a club, had charged a good amount(annexure a5) from the complainant and all members respectively but in the name of a club, there is only a small room built in the stilt parking area causing parking issues for the residents at the time of parking (annexure a8). The layout of the society has been provided for reference(Annexure 9).</span></font>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">1)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of money charged for stilt parking along with interest @ 21% quarterly till final order is pronounced.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">2)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The Op be barred from any sort of recovery of charges in the name of maintenance from the complainant till the builder gets a completion/occupancy certificate from the appropriate authorities.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">3)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Interest @5% p.a on the amount of Sale Deed(Rs. 44,09,262), to be paid from the date of possession till the final disposal as cost towards delay in providing completion certificate.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">4)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of excess amount charged towards installation of generator sets.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">5)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of proportionate Amount charged towards installation of firefighting equipment’s.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">6)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of the excess amount charged towards making of the club.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">7)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of Rs. 4500/- charged towards Auto Change Over Panel.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">8)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other amount the court may feel at its wisdom is required in the interest of justice.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">9)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>An additional amount of Rs. 3,00,000 towards the excess payment charged for the missing facilities (as referred in point 6 of the complaint), mental agony, harassment and legal charges in the interest of Justice.</span></font></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div>',4409262.00,4409262.00,'2013-09-25 00:00:00.000','2013-10-31 00:00:00.000','','1','','2015-05-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID , Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-02-07 14:52:52.000','AdvSaksham','2019-02-07 14:52:52.000'),(304,1104,'1104',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-08 12:54:35.000','RAJ KUMAR AND KULJEET KAUR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,999057822446,'UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK-C','JOSAN HEIGHTS, SECTOR-126, CHHAJUMAJRA, SAS NAGAR',28,507,'140301','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0005','JOSAN HEIGHTS','JSJ Builders Pvt Ltd','jsjbuilders.in@gmail.com',8699885568,0,'Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','<p>The complainants had booked a unit with super area measuring 1423 Sq. Ft. at OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS on 04.10.2016.&nbsp; That on 04.10.2016, the OP furnished an Allotment letter against the unit and allotted UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK C, MEASURING 1423 SQ. FT in OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS. It was stated in the Allotment letter that the possession will be handed over by 25.10.2016.</p><p>That on 04.10.2016, the OP executed a BUILDER BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and assured promised to hand over the possession of the unit&nbsp; including all the amenities as per the brochure That on 25.10.2016, OP offered the possession of the unit to the complainant but neither did OP did had the completion certificate for the project nor had the occupation certificate before offering possession to the complainants in 2016.</p><p>That the OP directed the complainants to execute the sale deed against the said unit and the same was executed. That it is pertinent to mention here that the OP received the PARTIAL COMPLETION CERTIFICATE on 14.12.2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of possession and OP has yet to receive Occupation certificate from the concerned authority and has offered possession of the unit without possessing OCCUPATION CERTIFICATE.</p><p>That OP has failed to completely develop the project as per the brochure and has taken complete consideration against the unit from the complainants and has offered possession of the unit without possessing occupancy certificate, till date. Therefore, the complainants craves the indulgence of the HONBLE ADJUDICATING OFFICER, RERA PUNJAB to direct the OP to hand over the compensation along with damages, as the OP failed to comply with its legal obligation according to the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016 and Punjab Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017.</p>','<p>i<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for not completing the project as per &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;brochure and commitments made to the RERA AUTHORITY, especially Gym, Swimming Pool, Club House etc. , till date under &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Section 12 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016</p><p>ii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000 (FIVE LAKS) for Installation of MOBILE Towers above the residential building&nbsp; and causing serious health hazard by installing the same.</p><p>iii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>iv<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>v<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to complete all the infractions committed by the OP as per the brochure as soon as possible</p><p><br></p><p>vi<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants was constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite party.</p><p><br></p><p>vii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Adjudicating Officer deems appropriate.</p>',3000000.00,3000000.00,'2016-10-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-10-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK-C, JOSAN HEIGHTS, SECTOR-126, CHHAJUMAJRA, SAS NAGAR (MOHALI), PUNJAB','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-08 12:54:30.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-08 12:54:30.000'),(305,1106,'1106',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-07 14:54:31.000','yash paul Kathpal','ykathpal@yahoo.com',9814466639,0,0,'Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','Saksham Arora','saacounselors@gmail.com',9872628189,9041300773,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','M/S Ansals Housing and construction Pvt ltd','ahcl@ansals.com',0,1123350847,'606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">The Owner of the flat in dispute had got the possession of the flat 31-Oct-2013 (annexure a2). At the time of purchasing the flat the owner was promised several features but they turned out to be a Sham. Not only did all the salient features (annexure a2) be bypassed along with all local rules, but also in the name of cover car parking (annexure a5) stilt parking has been provided. The complainant was thereafter charged for auto change panel but hasn\'t been provided with it till date(annexure a4). The society doesn\'t stand a completion certificate even after 10 years, even when their newspaper advertisement reads possession in 2009 (annexure a2). The Municipal Council has also in its letter stated that the possession of the flats should be stopped because of several discrepancies(annexure a3) which also puts a light at the intent and nature of the op to surpass rules for the purpose of its own gains. The Op has also crossed the terms of the tripartite agreement(annexure a7), by charging a huge amount than promised(annexure a6).&nbsp; The op for the purpose of creating a club, had charged a good amount(annexure a5) from the complainant and all members respectively but in the name of a club, there is only a small room built in the stilt parking area causing parking issues for the residents at the time of parking (annexure a8). The layout of the society has been provided for reference(Annexure 9).</span></font>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">1)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Compensation of Rs. 60,000 towards unpromised and failed future promises as have been stated by the OP.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">2)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span></span></font><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Compensation of</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Rs. 1,00,000 towards failure of its promised and duties as stated u/s 19 of the act done by the OP.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><br></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">3) Any other amount the court may feel at its wisdom is required in the interest of justice.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">4)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>An additional amount of Rs. 80,000 towards the excess payment charged for the missing facilities (as referred in point 6 of the complaint), mental agony, harassment and legal charges in the interest of Justice.</span></font></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div>',4409262.00,4409262.00,'2013-09-25 00:00:00.000','2013-10-31 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-05-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID , Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-02-12 12:10:09.000','AdvSaksham','2019-02-12 12:10:09.000'),(306,1106,'1106',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-07 14:54:31.000','yash paul Kathpal','ykathpal@yahoo.com',9814466639,0,0,'Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','Saksham Arora','saacounselors@gmail.com',9872628189,9041300773,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID, Nabha Road, Zirakpur','M/S Ansals Housing and construction Pvt ltd','ahcl@ansals.com',0,1123350847,'606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','606,6th Floor, IndraPrakash, 21, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi - 110001','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">The Owner of the flat in dispute had got the possession of the flat 31-Oct-2013 (annexure a2). At the time of purchasing the flat the owner was promised several features but they turned out to be a Sham. Not only did all the salient features (annexure a2) be bypassed along with all local rules, but also in the name of cover car parking (annexure a5) stilt parking has been provided. The complainant was thereafter charged for auto change panel but hasn\'t been provided with it till date(annexure a4). The society doesn\'t stand a completion certificate even after 10 years, even when their newspaper advertisement reads possession in 2009 (annexure a2). The Municipal Council has also in its letter stated that the possession of the flats should be stopped because of several discrepancies(annexure a3) which also puts a light at the intent and nature of the op to surpass rules for the purpose of its own gains. The Op has also crossed the terms of the tripartite agreement(annexure a7), by charging a huge amount than promised(annexure a6).&nbsp; The op for the purpose of creating a club, had charged a good amount(annexure a5) from the complainant and all members respectively but in the name of a club, there is only a small room built in the stilt parking area causing parking issues for the residents at the time of parking (annexure a8). The layout of the society has been provided for reference(Annexure 9).</span></font>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">1)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Compensation of Rs. 60,000 towards unpromised and failed future promises as have been stated by the OP.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">2)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span></span></font><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Compensation of</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Rs. 1,00,000 towards failure of its promised and duties as stated u/s 19 of the act done by the OP, e.g : failure to provide completion certificate, failure to provide documents and sanctioned plan for the society, failure in formation of the society etc.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><br></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">3) Any other amount the court may feel at its wisdom is required in the interest of justice.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">4)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>An additional amount of Rs. 80,000 towards the excess payment charged for the missing facilities (as referred in point 6 of the complaint), mental agony, harassment and legal charges in the interest of Justice.</span></font></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div>',4409262.00,4409262.00,'2013-09-25 00:00:00.000','2013-10-31 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-05-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID , Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-02-12 12:13:48.000','AdvSaksham','2019-02-12 12:13:48.000'),(307,1106,'1106',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-12 12:23:47.000','yash paul Kathpal','