e name of a club, there is only a small room built in the stilt parking area causing parking issues for the residents at the time of parking (annexure a8). The layout of the society has been provided for reference(Annexure 9).</span></font>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">1)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Compensation of Rs. 60,000 towards unpromised and failed future promises as have been stated by the OP.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">2)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span></span></font><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Compensation of</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Rs. 1,00,000 towards failure of its promised and duties as stated u/s 19 of the act done by the OP, e.g : failure to provide completion certificate, failure to provide documents and sanctioned plan for the society, failure in formation of the society etc.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><br></span></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">3) Any other amount the court may feel at its wisdom is required in the interest of justice.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;mso-line-height-alt:\r\n0pt;tab-stops:90.0pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">4)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>An additional amount of Rs. 80,000 towards the excess payment charged for the missing facilities (as referred in point 6 of the complaint), mental agony, harassment and legal charges in the interest of Justice.</span></font></p><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div>',4409262.00,4409262.00,'2013-09-25 00:00:00.000','2013-10-31 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-05-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Pine 201, Ansal Woodburry Apartment, Near PSEB GRID , Zirakpur','','',1,1,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-02-12 12:15:10.000','AdvSaksham','2019-02-12 12:15:10.000'),(308,1112,'1112',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,0,'#2147, Sector 69','SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','2147, Sector 69, Mohali','SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,0,'Promoter','PBRETA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Delayed Possession</p>','<p>Delayed Possession&nbsp;</p>',750000.00,750000.00,'2016-02-01 00:00:00.000','2019-02-04 00:00:00.000','','1','','2019-02-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2147, Sector 69. Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'harish635','2019-02-12 22:24:19.000','harish635','2019-02-12 22:24:19.000'),(309,1113,'1113',1404,'248ffdd0-76be-409f-9384-3187c1aaa82d','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramashish Byaut','ramashishbyahut@gmail.com',9855744754,0,0,'H.N 128','Village- Barmajra',28,507,'160055','1','SCO-35 FF','phase-2',28,507,'160055','Ramashish Byahut','ramashishbyahut@gmail.com',7973512823,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0192','Maya Garden City','1.Maya Garden City 2. Barnala Builder and Property Consultant','barnalabuilders@ymail.com',0,0,'Opposite McDonald\'s,','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway , Zirakhpur',28,507,'160055','1','Opposite McDonald\'s,','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway , Zirakhpur',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That applicant booked 5BHK flat for her own residence in the project of respondent no. 1 vide application dated 08.12.2012 and the respondent issued allotment of flat no. 103 measuring 2850 Sq. Ft. in H1 block at first floor vide letter dated 14.12.2012. The applicant entered into agreement to sell with respondent, as per which total consideration of flat was Rs. 63,00,000/-. As per clause 5 of agreement the date of sale deed was fixed on or before 30th November, 2014. The applicants paid Rs. 68,41,850/- with the respondent against total consideration of Rs. 63,00,000/- which includes maintenance, late payment charges and service tax etc.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per brochure, respondents are liable to provide club house facility and swimming pool etc which were also not provided by respondents till date. The possession was to be handed over on or before 30.11.2014 but the same was offered on 15.04.2016 and the sale deed was also to be done 0n 30.11.2014 which was done on 22.03.2018 in favor of applicant. It is relevant to mention here that the respondents failed to get completion certificate from competent authority and the partial completion certificate issued to respondent was conditional &amp; due to non fulfilment of conditions the pollution control board has already written letter to competent authority to cancel the partial completion certificate.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That applicant requested number of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed resolve the issues raised by applicant and to provide occupation/completion certificate even after receiving legal notice.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the applicant requested number to times to respondent through letter and emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and other issues but the respondent failed to revert&nbsp; any of letter/email sent by applicant.</p><div><br></div>','<p>To pay Rs. 8,02,000 as per valuation report to make the flat in the position as promised by the respondent.&nbsp;</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000 (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing mental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering service and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To remove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc and to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount received as service tax from the applicant since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned department.</p><p>e.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount for giving less carpet area.</p><p>f.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give NEC and get the sale deed done as per RERA with clear carpet area in favour of the applicant.</p><p>g.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay interest @ 18% on the amount of Rs. 63,00,000 from the due date of possession i.e. 30 Nov 2014 till the date of sale deed/issuance of completion certificate.</p><p>h.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide club/swimming pool etc alongwith all facilities as per promise made in brochure.</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide all other facilities which are promised by not provided like provision of DTH, Broadband, Intercom Facility, approach from Highway.</p><p>j.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- as litigation expenses.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Or Any other order as the Hon’ble Adalat may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances in favour of the Applicant be passed, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6300000.00,6841850.00,'2014-11-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-12-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','H1-103, Maya Garden City, Zirakpur, District Mohali\r\n','','',1,0,0,0,'govindkumar','2019-02-15 14:57:34.000','govindkumar','2019-02-15 14:57:34.000'),(310,1114,'1114',1230,'b1032b73-264e-4295-a2ff-d289cd0b5713','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-21 13:05:05.000','Haridev Haridev','Kaushik.378@gmail.com',7529810988,0,0,'Hno 434A','Sector 47A',6,128,'160047','1','Hno 434A','Sector 47A',6,128,'160047','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0022','MAYA GARDEN MAGNESIA','M/S BARNALA BUILDERS','INFO@MAYAGARDENMAGNESIA.COM',0,0,'MAYA GARDEN MAGNESIA,  BARNALA BUILDERS, OPPOSITE MC DONALD\'S, CHANDIGARH-AMBALA HIGHWAY, ZIRAKPUR','',28,507,'140603','1','MAYA GARDEN MAGNESIA,  BARNALA BUILDERS, OPPOSITE MC DONALD\'S, CHANDIGARH-AMBALA HIGHWAY, ZIRAKPUR','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>1.&nbsp; The promoter had offered to sale a commercial shop in real estate project “Maya Garden Magnesia” to the applicant on 27 Sep 2017 in presence of the Real estate agent Arun Pratap Singh (PBRERA-SA79-REA0485) and received an advance payment of 74 percent of total cost of shop from the applicant in contravention of the section 3(1) and 13(1) of The Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016 respectively.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>2.&nbsp; False date of Memorandum of Understanding for sale of commercial shop was shown by the promoter by using the undue influence under the pretence of forfeiture of booking amount to escape from violation of The Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>3.&nbsp; The promoter has never made available sanctioned plans, layout plans including layout of shop approved by the competent authority. Which contravenes section 11(3)(a) and section 19(1) of The Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>4.&nbsp; The promoter has shown covered area as 160 sq ft in the memorandum of understanding for sale of the commercial shop. In the “agreement for sale” as offered by the promoter on 18 Nov 2018 the carpet area of the unit has been mentioned as 139.156 sq feet whereas the clear break up of covered area and carpet area has neither been provided by the promoter. However duly approved lay out plan of the shop was not found available with the RERA (PUNJAB) which is in contravention section 4 of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>5. The promoter has not attached the schedule B to offered Agreement for sale which contravenes the section 13(2) of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>6.&nbsp; Under Para 11of the said agreement, a unfair/illegal clause has been inserted for payment of maintenance charges.</p><p><br></p><p>7.&nbsp; Illegal clause of parking charges has been inserted contrary to representations made by the promoter assuring free paid sticker for parking of vehicle to be provided at the time of offer of possession.</p>','<p>1.&nbsp; The promoter may be directed to cancel the booking of above mentioned commercial shop and return the entire amount paid till date against purchase of the above mentioned commercial shop along with interest as applicable under section 18 of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016 or as the court deem appropriate.</p><p>2.&nbsp; The promoter may be directed to pay compensation on account mental loss, pain and harassment caused to applicant for an amount of Rupees 5,00,000/- or as the court deem appropriate under section 18 of The Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016 or any other provisions made there under.</p><p>3.&nbsp; The promoter may be ordered to pay penalty under section 59, 60, 61, 63 of The Real Estate (Regulation and Development) act, 2016 or any other legal action may be taken against the promoter as the court deem appropriate.</p>',2283240.00,1698650.00,'2022-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-09-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','SHOP NO 446A(GBS93), MAYA GARDEN MAGNESIA, \r\nBARNALA BUILDERS, OPPOSITE MC DONALD\'S,\r\nCHANDIGARH-AMBALA HIGHWAY, ZIRAKPUR,DIST MOHALI\r\nPUNJAB-140603','','',1,1,0,0,'Haridev','2019-02-17 18:20:51.000','Haridev','2019-02-17 18:20:51.000'),(311,1115,'1115',1404,'248ffdd0-76be-409f-9384-3187c1aaa82d','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramashish Byaut','ramashishbyahut@gmail.com',9855744754,0,0,'H.N 128','Village- Barmajra',28,507,'160055','1','SCO-35 FF','phase-2',28,507,'160055','Kulwinder Singh','kulwindersinghadvocate@gmail.com',9915772513,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0192','Maya Garden City\r\n','Maya Garden City','barnalabuilders@ymail.com',0,0,'Opposite McDonald\'s','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'160055','1','Opposite McDonald\'s','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That applicant booked 5BHK flat for her own residence in the project of respondent no. 1 vide application dated 08.12.2012 and the respondent issued allotment of flat no. 103 measuring 2850 Sq. Ft. in H1 block at first floor vide letter dated 14.12.2012. The applicant entered into agreement to sell with respondent, as per which total consideration of flat was Rs. 63,00,000/-. As per clause 5 of agreement the date of sale deed was fixed on or before 30th November, 2014. The applicants paid Rs. 68,41,850/- with the respondent against total consideration of Rs. 63,00,000/- which includes maintenance, late payment charges and service tax etc.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per brochure, respondents are liable to provide club house facility and swimming pool etc which were also not provided by respondents till date. The possession was to be handed over on or before 30.11.2014 but the same was offered on 15.04.2016 and the sale deed was also to be done 0n 30.11.2014 which was done on 22.03.2018 in favor of applicant. It is relevant to mention here that the respondents failed to get completion certificate from competent authority and the partial completion certificate issued to respondent was conditional &amp; due to non fulfilment of conditions the pollution control board has already written letter to competent authority to cancel the partial completion certificate.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That applicant requested number of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed resolve the issues raised by applicant and to provide occupation/completion certificate even after receiving legal notice.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the applicant requested number to times to respondent through letter and emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and other issues but the respondent failed to revert&nbsp; any of letter/email sent by applicant.</p><p><br></p>','<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To pay Rs. 8,02,000 as per valuation report to make the flat in the position as promised by the &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;respondent.&nbsp;</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000 (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing mental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering service and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To remove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc and to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount received as service tax from the applicant since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned department.</p><p>e.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount for giving less carpet area.</p><p>f.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give NEC and get the sale deed done as per RERA with clear carpet area in favour of the applicant.</p><p>g.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay interest @ 18% on the amount of Rs. 63,00,000 from the due date of possession i.e. 30 Nov 2014 till the date of sale deed/issuance of completion certificate.</p><p>h.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide club/swimming pool etc alongwith all facilities as per promise made in brochure.</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide all other facilities which are promised by not provided like provision of DTH, Broadband, Intercom Facility, approach from Highway.</p><p>j.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- as litigation expenses.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Or Any other order as the Hon’ble Adalat may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances in favour of the Applicant be passed, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6300000.00,6841850.00,'2014-11-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-12-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','H1-103, Maya Garden City, Zirakpur, District Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'govindkumar','2019-02-18 10:08:44.000','govindkumar','2019-02-18 10:08:44.000'),(312,1116,'1116',1404,'248ffdd0-76be-409f-9384-3187c1aaa82d','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramashish Byaut','ramashishbyahut@gmail.com',9855744754,0,0,'H.N 128','Village- Barmajra',28,507,'160055','1','SCO-35 FF','phase-2',28,507,'160055','kulwinder Singh','kulwindersinghadvocate@gmail.com',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0192','Maya Garden City','Maya Garden City','barnalabuilders@ymail.com',0,0,'Opposite McDonald\'s','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway',28,507,'160055','1','Opposite McDonald\'s','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That applicant booked 5BHK flat for her own residence in the project of respondent no. 1 vide application dated 08.12.2012 and the respondent issued allotment of flat no. 103 measuring 2850 Sq. Ft. in H1 block at first floor vide letter dated 14.12.2012. The applicant entered into agreement to sell with respondent, as per which total consideration of flat was Rs. 63,00,000/-. As per clause 5 of agreement the date of sale deed was fixed on or before 30th November, 2014. The applicants paid Rs. 68,41,850/- with the respondent against total consideration of Rs. 63,00,000/- which includes maintenance, late payment charges and service tax etc.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per brochure, respondents are liable to provide club house facility and swimming pool etc which were also not provided by respondents till date. The possession was to be handed over on or before 30.11.2014 but the same was offered on 15.04.2016 and the sale deed was also to be done 0n 30.11.2014 which was done on 22.03.2018 in favor of applicant. It is relevant to mention here that the respondents failed to get completion certificate from competent authority and the partial completion certificate issued to respondent was conditional &amp; due to non fulfilment of conditions the pollution control board has already written letter to competent authority to cancel the partial completion certificate.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That applicant requested number of times to respondent to provide facilities as per brochure but failed resolve the issues raised by applicant and to provide occupation/completion certificate even after receiving legal notice.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the applicant requested number to times to respondent through letter and emails regarding deficiencies/anomalies and other issues but the respondent failed to revert&nbsp; any of letter/email sent by applicant.</p><div><br></div>','<p>o pay Rs. 8,02,000 as per valuation report to make the flat in the position as promised by the respondent.&nbsp;</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000 (Rupees Ten Lac) to the Applicant for causing mental agony, harassment and humiliation as the OP were deficient in rendering service and are indulged in unfair trade practices, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To remove all the encroachments made by the respondents for making parkings etc and to put the same as per plan i.e. greenery/park.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount received as service tax from the applicant since the same were not deposited by the respondents with the concerned department.</p><p>e.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To refund the amount for giving less carpet area.</p><p>f.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give NEC and get the sale deed done as per RERA with clear carpet area in favour of the applicant.</p><p>g.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay interest @ 18% on the amount of Rs. 63,00,000 from the due date of possession i.e. 30 Nov 2014 till the date of sale deed/issuance of completion certificate.</p><p>h.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide club/swimming pool etc alongwith all facilities as per promise made in brochure.</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To provide all other facilities which are promised by not provided like provision of DTH, Broadband, Intercom Facility, approach from Highway.</p><p>j.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To pay an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- as litigation expenses.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Or Any other order as the Hon’ble Adalat may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances in favour of the Applicant be passed, in the interest of justice.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',6300000.00,6841850.00,'2014-11-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-12-14 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','H1-103, Maya Garden City, Zirakpur, District Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'govindkumar','2019-02-18 10:16:45.000','govindkumar','2019-02-18 10:16:45.000'),(313,1117,'1117',1404,'248ffdd0-76be-409f-9384-3187c1aaa82d','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramashish Byaut','ramashishbyahut@gmail.com',9855744754,0,0,'H.N 128','Village- Barmajra',28,507,'160055','1','SCO-35 FF','phase-2',28,507,'16005