RE THAN ONE YEAR</p><p>AS PER AGREEMENT POSSESSION HAS TO BE HANDOVER BY 31 DECEMBER 2017 BUT EVEN AFTER PASSING OF MORE THAN ONE YEAR NO PHYSICAL POSSESSION WAS HANDOVER TILL DATE</p><p><br></p><p>GROUNDS OF APPEAL</p><p>1 EVEN AFTER&nbsp; PASSING OF MORE THAN ONE YEAR&nbsp; FROM THE DATE OF POSSESSION AS MENTIONED IN AGREEMENT TO SELL, THE RESPONDENT FAILED TO HANDOVER THE ACTUAL PHYSICAL POSSESSION.</p><p>2 COMPLAINANT HAD PAID RS. 10491073 AGAINST BASIC COST ALONG WITH 1258928 AGAINST GST.</p><p>3 COMPLAINANT HAD TAKEN A HOUSING LOAN OF RS. 4145090 AND PAYING MONTHLY INSTALLMENT&nbsp; OF RS. 40819</p><p>4 COMPLAINANT AND HIS FAMILY IS FACING A HUGE MENTAL AND FINANCIAL AGONY DUE TO FAILURE OF RESPONDENT.&nbsp;</p>','<p>RELIEF SOUGHT</p><p>1. COMPENSATION OF RS. 1000000 IN LIEU OF MENTAL AND FINANCIAL AGONY U/S 18(1) OF THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) ACT 2016</p><p><br></p><p>2. ANY OTHER RELIEF AS FEELS THINKS FIT BY HONBLE AUTHORITY</p>',11560710.00,10491073.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-10-28 00:00:00','2017-10-28 00:00:00','Apartment No. 4PH2, 26th Floor, 4th Tower, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Near Verka Milk Plant, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'damanjit','2019-02-22 14:22:41.000','damanjit','2019-02-22 14:22:41.000'),(330,1126,'1126',1388,'9f925b8d-3343-4247-ac11-f438350e37ab','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vijesh Jaiswal','vijesh44@gmail.com',9416001990,0,0,'D-44, Bawa Vihar','Sector-9',13,1,'134003','1','F-112, Orbit Apartments','VIP Road, Adjacent Metro Wholesale',28,507,'140603','Ashutosh Vig','sarassociates1211@gmail.com',9915882345,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE','Sh. Binder Pal Mittal, Chairman M/s Sushma Buildtech','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex, Ist Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex, Ist Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160002','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as the son of the applicants was suffering from celiac disease and for easy access to the good hospitals in Tricity, the applicants purchased Apartment No. G-1203 in Tower-G for a sale consideration of Rs. 45,77,100/- (Annexure A-2). Later on, the applicants requested the respondents to change the Apartment and the respondent allotted Apartment No. G-403 on 4th Floor in “G” Tower vide allotment letter dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-1) in exchange of G-1203 and adjusted the above-payment in G-403. The applicants paid full payment of the apartment i.e. G-1203 on 04.07.2016.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per the terms and condition of the lopsided agreement dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-3), the respondents were bound to deliver the possession within 12 months from the date of execution of Annexure A-3 but the respondents failed to deliver the actual physical possession of the Apartment by the due date. The relevant clause regarding the possession is reproduced hereunder:-&nbsp;</p><p>“14.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>POSSESSION :</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The Developer shall endeavor to give possession of the said unit to the buyer within a period of Twelve (12) months from the date of execution of this Agreement unless and until restrained by circumstances beyond its contemplation and control and subject to timely payment by the allottee. Besides, the Developer can take six months grace period for completing and handing over the said unit to the buyer.”</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That being aggrieved from the act and conduct of the respondents, the applicants made numerous representations (Annexure A-4) for delivering the possession of the apartment but to no effect.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That till today, the applicants are running from pillar to post to get the actual physical possession of the Apartment but the respondent did not paid any heed to the request of the applicants.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Detailed Petition is attached herewith as (Annexure A-5)</p><div><br></div>','<p>(i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to pay compensationas per Section 12, 18 and 19 of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act amounting Rs. 2,50,000/- for mental &amp; physical harassment committed upon the applicants by the respondents on account of delay in handing over the possession of the Apartment, deficiency in the services and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents and on account of losses suffered by the applicants as the applicants have taken some other premises on rent because the respondent failed to deliver the possession of the Apartment on stipulated time.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>(ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Further directions may please be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on account of litigation charges to the applicant.</p><p><br></p><p>(iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>It is further prayed that this Hon\'bleCourt may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of justice, equity and fair play.</p>',4577100.00,4577100.00,'2017-09-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-09-15 00:00:00','2016-09-15 00:00:00','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE\r\nApartment No. G-403, 4th Floor\r\nBishangarh&Bishanpura,\r\nZirakpur, District S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali)','','',2,0,0,0,'VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-22 17:18:31.000','VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-22 17:18:31.000'),(331,1126,'1126',1388,'9f925b8d-3343-4247-ac11-f438350e37ab','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vijesh Jaiswal','vijesh44@gmail.com',9416001990,0,0,'D-44, Bawa Vihar','Sector-9',13,1,'134003','1','F-112, Orbit Apartments','VIP Road, Adjacent Metro Wholesale',28,507,'140603','Ashut