n>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The Developer shall endeavor to give possession of the said unit to the buyer within a period of Twelve (12) months from the date of execution of this Agreement unless and until restrained by circumstances beyond its contemplation and control and subject to timely payment by the allottee. Besides, the Developer can take six months grace period for completing and handing over the said unit to the buyer.”</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That being aggrieved from the act and conduct of the respondents, the applicants made numerous representations (Annexure A-4) for delivering the possession of the apartment but to no effect.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That till today, the applicants are running from pillar to post to get the actual physical possession of the Apartment but the respondent did not paid any heed to the request of the applicants.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Detailed Petition is attached herewith as (Annexure A-5)</p><div><br></div>','<p>(i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to pay compensationas per Section 12, 18 and 19 of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act amounting Rs. 2,50,000/- for mental &amp; physical harassment committed upon the applicants by the respondents on account of delay in handing over the possession of the Apartment, deficiency in the services and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents and on account of losses suffered by the applicants as the applicants have taken some other premises on rent because the respondent failed to deliver the possession of the Apartment on stipulated time.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>(ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Further directions may please be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on account of litigation charges to the applicant.</p><p><br></p><p>(iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>It is further prayed that this Hon\'bleCourt may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of justice, equity and fair play.</p>',4577100.00,4577100.00,'2017-09-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-09-15 00:00:00','2016-09-15 00:00:00','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE\r\nApartment No. G-403, 4th Floor\r\nBishangarh&Bishanpura,\r\nZirakpur, District S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali)','','',2,0,0,0,'VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-22 18:03:10.000','VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-22 18:03:10.000'),(333,1128,'1128',1337,'159bd8f9-e36f-45ef-ad7d-e76a7b30b438','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Opinder Kour','paul2707@gmail.com',9906692895,0,0,'Green View Colony','Alloucha bagh',15,564,'190008','1','Green View Colony','Alloucha bagh',15,564,'190008','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0163','SAVITRY GREENS-2, NK SHARMA ENTERPRISES PVT LTD,','PARMINDER KUMAR SHARMA','NKSHARMAGROUP@YAHOO.COM',9316137947,0,'N.K SHARMA GROUP, SCO-1 & 2 CHANRANJI ENCLAVE , LOHGARH, ZIRAKPUR ','',28,507,'140603','1','N.K SHARMA GROUP, SCO-1 & 2 CHANRANJI ENCLAVE , LOHGARH, ZIRAKPUR ','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>We booked a 3BHK  flat measuring 1442 sqft in Savitry Greens 2, Ghazipur by N.K.SHARMA Builders,\r\n</p><p>\r\nInitial down-payment of Rs.100000/- paid on 18/02/2013  and then Rs.515000/-paid (date 14/03/2013) to the builder within one month of booking flat,we were assigned flat #301,3rd floor, Tower 9 measuring 1442 sqft.&nbsp;</p><p>\r\nAfter more than year after initial booking on Feb,2013 they kept us waiting to sign the agreement and  changed the above  flat to a new one in Tower 7 measuring almost 100 sqft  more (i.e 1540 sqft) and asked to pay money for the extra area added in the new one.We came to an agreement and this time they assigned the flat no 206,tower 7 measuring 1540 sqft saying they are not going to build tower 9 at all.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;\r\nAn agreement was signed  on 4/8/2014 and we were supposed to get the possession in 36 months from the date of signing the agreement  i.e is around August,2017.&nbsp;</p><p>There were two cheques paid to builder by the ICICI bank amounting close to 16.5 lakhs.&nbsp;</p><p>\r\nWe kept visiting the site many times but there was no construction happening for the flat/tower since September,2015.We were very nervous about what is going to happen with the flat, as we had invested our hard earned money being a private employee. I was paying the home loan EMI of Rs 16000 thousand per month to the bank with no possession date in sight at all and builder never told us when will we get the possession as the construction was completely halted. </p><p>We kept asking about construction completion to the builder and when the agreement date passed and we knew he was never going to complete the project,we requested them that we want to withdraw from your project and return our&nbsp; money back ,the builder was not agreeing on it at all initially.</p><p>They asked me to exchange this flat with the ones in Savitry Greens on VIP road but Savitry Greens flats had more area and they asked me it&nbsp; would cost me additional 8 Lakhs which was way beyond my budget.I said if you will give me on the same price i will take it.</p><p><br></p>','<p>In total they took around 23 lakhs including the initial payment of 615000 and bank loan cheques from ICICI bank.</p><p>So in this process which started since Feb 2013, when i booked the flat till now i have paid close to Rs 600000/- as interest to ICICI bank on the home loan and also lost interest money on the initial deposit of 615000/- which i could have earned if i would have kept it with me for more than 5 years.</p><p>My parents had to sit in builder office for so many days from morning till evening to request them to pay the money back to us and to the bank so that i can close the loan account.<br></p><p>So after so many deliberation with builder over more than a year , i got them to close the loan&nbsp; and they returned down payment money of 615000/- lacs to me.<br></p><p>Still builder owe me around more than 1.5 lacs as the principal amount paid by me on the home loan to the bank, i also want them to be liable to pay&nbsp; as per RERA rules and regulations the interest amount which is close to 6 lacs that i had to pay to the bank during the loan tenure which is a loss to me without any fault of mine .<br></p><p><br></p><p>Also as per the agreement they were supposed to pay me every month based on flat sqft area if they didn\'t complete&nbsp; the possession by&nbsp; 36 months which they never did at all.</p><p>I was told by the builder do whatever you want to do ,we will not give you money back, we don\'t owe you anything and we have closed the case at our end.If you want to approach RERA,you can go we are not scared of RERA at all.<br></p><p>I still have the TPA with me which was signed between buyer,builder and bank.<br></p><p>In nutshell i want builder to be held responsible/accountable for the loss that i have incurred monetarily, harassing us mentally, not&nbsp; being fair with customer, fooling the buyers and not abiding by the agreement rules. and RERA regulations.</p><p>I want RERA to provide me relief by asking the builder to pay me the loan principal plus the interest that i have paid to the bank which comes around to 7.5 lakhs.<br></p>',4329620.00,2300000.00,'2017-08-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-08-04 00:00:00','2014-08-04 00:00:00','206,Tower 7, Savitry Greens 2, Ghazipur,  Zirakpur, Mohali(PB)','','',1,0,0,0,'AmitPaul','2019-02-24 11:11:08.000','AmitPaul','2019-02-24 11:11:08.000'),(334,1129,'1129',1337,'159bd8f9-e36f-45ef-ad7d-e76a7b30b438','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-26 11:20:57.000','Opinder Kour','paul2707@gmail.com',9906692895,0,0,'Green View Colony','Alloucha bagh',15,564,'190008','1','Green View Colony','Alloucha bagh',15,564,'190008','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0163','SAVITRY GREENS-2 ,N K SHARMA ENTERPRISES PVT LTD ','PARM