ince there was dispute about charging\r\nof GST &amp; also vide letter dt 9.10.17 &amp; 30.10.17(C-5),it was duly\r\nconveyed to respondents but respondent did not reply satisfactorily vide letter\r\ndt 30.10.17(C-5).A sum of Rs. 6001038.30(receipts &amp; documents C-5 colly)has\r\nalready been paid by the complainants.The next installment was due on the\r\ncasting of GF roof slab which has not been done &amp; consequently there has\r\nbeen no demand raised by the respondent.Respondent has also stopped the\r\ndevelopment work at the site.A letter was also sent to respondent in this\r\nregard on 14.12.18 &amp;16.12.18(C-6) but no reply has been received.Since there\r\nhas been delay in construction &amp; the respondent was bound to deliver the\r\npossession by 22.11.17,the complainants wishes to withdraw &amp; thus are\r\nseeking refund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; Compensation</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.05.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development. The complainants does not wish to remain in the project since there has been a huge delay on the part of the respondent.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To direct the respondent to pay compensation to the tune of Rs. 500000 lacs <span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">f<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">or causing mental and physical harassment\r\nand agony to the complainants on account of delay in possession, for not doing any development on the project site, keeping the hard earned money of the complainants for so many years. The complainant has also availed the loan for paying the installments to the respondent.</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -48px; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 46.6667px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">To pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</span><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><u><o:p></o:p></u></span></span><br></span><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:250%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:250%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></p></span></li></ol>',17000222.00,6001038.30,'2017-05-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2015-10-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 104, Type B-2, Built Up Villa','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-08 18:28:46.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-08 18:28:46.000'),(363,1137,'1137',1391,'65320f7e-b851-40b3-aeda-8622083d6c16','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Parampal Singh Dhillon','rajeshbhathejaadv@yahoo.com',9814226530,0,0,'Dhillon Farm, H.No. 1010, Kotakpura Road, ','Moga',28,393,'142001','1','Flat No. 1302, Tower A-3, Purab Premium Apartments II, Sector 88, SAS Nagar, Mohali','Mohali',28,507,'160062','Rajesh Bhatheja, Advocate','rajeshbhathejaadv@yahoo.com',9814226530,1724626530,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Purab Premium Apartments II, Sector 88, SAS Nagar, Mohali','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','eoh@gmada.gov.in',0,0,'Geater Mohali Area Development Authority, ','PUDA Bhawan, Sector 62,',28,507,'160062','0','Geater Mohali Area Development Authority,','PUDA Bhawan, Sector 62,',28,507,'160062','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Complainant applied\r\nfor a flat in the project namely Purab Premium Apartment-II, Sector 88, SAS\r\nNagar, Mohali vide application number PPA000454 and paid earnest money of\r\nRs.435200/-.&nbsp; The complainant was allotted&nbsp;&nbsp;a residential\r\napartment type 3 and letter of allotment of residential apartment Type 3 in the\r\nPurab Premium Apartment II in General Category at Sector 88, SAS Nagar was\r\nissued vide letter No.GMADA-EO/2014/13973 dated 5.6.2014. Tentative price of\r\nthe Apartment Type 3 was Rs.8700000. As per clause 3 of the Letter of intent,\r\nthe possession of the allotted apartment shall be handed over in the month of\r\nDecember 2015. The Complainant made balance payment as per Plan-B and till date\r\nthe complainant has deposited a sum of Rs.9863825/-. Vide letter Memo\r\nNo.GMADA-EO/2016-33950 dated 25.7.2016&nbsp; the complainant was informed that\r\nin a draw held on 06 Jan 2016 and apartment 1302, Tower 8, Block-C, Floor-12,\r\nType 3 covered area 1904.67 has been allotted to the complainant.&nbsp;after\r\nreceiving letter dated 25.7.2016&nbsp; complainant came to know that as per\r\nallotment letter dated 25.7.2016, apartment no.1303 has been wrongly allotted\r\nbut in fact as per draw apartment no.1302, Block-3, Tower No. A, Floor no.12\r\nwas allotted to the complainant. So vide letter dated 30.8.2106, the\r\ncomplainant requested to the respondents to cancel the allotment letter and\r\noffer of possession dated 25.7.2016 and requested to issue new allotment letter\r\nand offer of possession by making necessary corrections. Thereafter the\r\ncomplainant received letter no.44719 dated 23.9.2016 from the respondents\r\nwhereby they assured that new allotment letter of possession with regard to\r\nflat No. 1302, Tower-A-3 will be issued to the complainant but nothing was\r\ndone. So the complainant sent letter dated 02.11.2017 and also sent legal\r\nnotice dated&nbsp; 08.08.2018 but till date possession of allotted apartment\r\nhas not been given. So the complainant is filing the present complaint\r\nalongwith the documents annexed herewith.</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:45.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">i)</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To direct the respondents to pay a sum\r\nof Rs.10.00 Lacs towards the compensation for harassment, mental agony and\r\nphysical agony.</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:45.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">ii)</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To direct the respondents to pay a sum\r\nof Rs.5.00 Lacs for loss of opportunity to buy the flat with other builder and\r\nescalation of the cost of fitments and furnishings during the period of delay\r\nin handing over the possession.</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:45.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">iii)</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">To direct the respondents to pay a sum\r\nof Rs.1,10,000/- towards the cost of litigation.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>',8700000.00,9863825.00,'2015-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2014-06-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No. 1302, Tower A-3, Purab Premium Apartments II, Sector 88, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'rajeshbhatheja','2019-03-09 11:05:09.000','rajeshbhatheja','2019-03-09 11:05:09.000'),(364,1138,'1138',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-11 13:48:43.000','MONIKA TAKKAR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',8622000001,1724181010,457308216625,'RZ 63, GALI NO.-2','MAIN ROAD, PALAM PURAN NAGAR, PALAM COLONY, PALAM VILLAGE',10,562,'110045','0','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0029','ANSAL GOLF LINKS','ANSAL PROPERTIES AND INFRASTRUCTURE LIMITED ','customercare@ansalapi.com',1725035035,0,'115 ANSAL BHAWAN','16 K G MARG NEW DELHI ',10,429,'110001','1','115 ANSAL BHAWAN','16 K G MARG NEW DELHI ',10,429,'110001','1','<p>That the original allottee had booked a plot on 11.12.2010 for shop cum office SCO in OPs project ANSAL GOLF LINKS situated at Mohali, Punjab. That on 12.10.2010, the Op allotted Plot No. 47 E measuring 33.33 Sq. Yard in the said Project and it was assured that the possession of the plot will be delivered by 31.12.2011. Allotment letter is annexed as ANNEXURE C-1\r\n</p><p>That on 10.02.2011, the complainant, aadhar card annexed as ANNEXURE C-2, had purchased the said plot from the original allottee vide transfer application annexed as ANENXURE C-3 COLLY. That the OP continuously demanded amount from the complainant without even having necessary approvals from the competent authority. Demand notices is annexed as ANNEXURE C-4. That the complainant had paid the complete amount along with delayed interest 18 per cent to the OP but OP failed to hand over the possession of the unit by 31.12.2011. Total amount paid by complainant is annexed as ANNEXURE C-5 COLLY.\r\n</p><p>That due to the deficiency in services and non delivery of possession of the unit, the complainant has suffered a lot of mental harassment. The complainant visited the office of OP numerous times regarding the status of the plot but OP gave no answers to the complainant which had caused a lot of physical harassment.\r\n</p><p>That due to the cost escalation of construction, the complainant has to pay 10 times the amount as on today, what he had to pay in the year 2011-2012, for which the OP need to compensate the complainant. That failure to hand over the possession of the unit within the stipulated time is not only loss of money but also loss of opportunity.\r\n</p><p>That as per the Brochure, annexed as ANNEXURE C-6, the OP had promised many facilities and amenities to be provided in the project which will draw a lot of public towards the project which will help him to exponentially grow his business as well but till date non of the facilities have been materialized by the OP which is violation of Section 12 of RERA, 2016.\r\n</p><p>That it is</p>','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand over Rs.10,000 per month from the date of possession i.e. 31.12.2011 for causing Mental harassment</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand over Rs. 10,000 per month from the date of possession i.e. 31.12.2011 for causing Physical harassment.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand over Rs. 10,000 per month from the date of possession i.e. 31.12.2011 for deficiency in services and unfair trade practice.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand over Rs. 10,000 per month from the date of possession i.e. 31.12.2011 for escalation of cost of construction.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand over Rs. 10,000 per month from the date of possession i.e. 31.12.2011 for violation of Section 12 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016.</p>',1589708.00,1589708.00,'2011-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2010-11-12 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Earlier Unit No. 47 E and Before Unit No. 54 E','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-03-10 12:35:14.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-03-10 12:35:14.000'),(365,1139,'1139',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-13 18:11:38.000','ANURADHA DUA','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'F-128, SPANGLE CONDOS','P.O. DHAKOLI, VILLAGE GAZIPUR, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'160104','1','D-711, Ravindra Apartments, Ravindra Enclave, Baltana','ZIrakpur',28,507,'140604','Ravinderpal Singh','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS GOLD MEADOWS LIFESTYLE','ATS ESTATES PRIVATE LIMITED','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'711/92, DEEPALI, NEHRU PLACE','',10,429,'110019','1','711/92, DEEPALI, NEHRU PLACE','',10,429,'110019','1','<p>Complainant had booked a residential apartment bearing no. 4051 on 5th Floor, Tower No.4, Golf Meadows, Dera Bassi, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab on 26.07.2013 for an agreed sum of Rs.81,67,500/-. Out of the total price of Rs.81,67,500/-, Complainant had already paid a sum of Rs.78,17,500/-. An agreement was executed on 12.11.2013 wherein they were required to handover possession of the flat within a period of 36 + 6 months from the date of start of construction which started in June, 2012, therefore, stipulated time period has already been over on 31.12.2015. No Force Majeure Circumstances has ever been communicated to the complainant. Complainant had brought this flat for the residential purposes of her parents (now died) Late Sh. Jaidev Bajaj (Died on 30.01.2019) and Late Smt. Satya Bajaj (Died on 03.07.2018), but, builder has failed to handover the possession of the flat in their lifetime. Earlier I have booked flat at 9th floor (sun facing flat) and thereafter complainant had requested them to shift the flat at some lower floor and accordingly it was shifted to 5th floor (Flat No. 4051) for the reason that her parents did not wanted to reside at higher floor. Despite all this, Complainant had to suffer a lot of mental tension, physical harassments, anger, anguish and pain.&nbsp; Since, the very purpose of buying the flat is now over with the death of the parents due to their death, complainant do not wish to remain with the property. Accordingly, complainant served a detailed representation to the Opposite Party seeking refund of deposited amount along with stipulated interest in view of Section 18 of the RERA Act but no reply/ refund has been given to the complainant till date. Opposite Party has violated the provisions of RERA, 2016 by firstly not handing over the possession of the flat within stipulated time and then again violated section 18 of the RERA, 2016 for not refunding the deposited amount of the complainant along with stipulated interest and compensation.</p><p><br></p>','<p>Complainant seeking refund of her deposited amount of Rs.81,07,373/- along with stipulated interest as provided under the RERA, 2016 (78,17,500/- deposited qua price of flat and Rs.2,89,873/- deposited qua taxes.) along with compensation for harrassment Rs.10,00,000/- and Rs.1,00,000/- as cost of litigation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',8167500.00,8107373.00,'2015-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-11-12 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','4051, TOWER 4, GOLF MEADOWS LIFESTYLE, VILLAGE MADHOPUR TEHSIL DERABASSI, MOHALI, PUNJAB','','',1,1,0,0,'advravinder','2019-03-11 22:12:35.000','advravinder','2019-03-11 22:12:35.000'),(366,1126,'1126',1388,'9f925b8d-3343-4247-ac11-f438350e37ab','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-01 11:04:46.000','Vijesh Jaiswal','vijesh44@gmail.com',9416001990,0,0,'D-44, Bawa Vihar','Sector-9',13,1,'134003','1','F-112, Orbit Apartments','VIP Road, Adjacent Metro Wholesale',28,507,'140603','Ashutosh Vig','sarassociates1211@gmail.com',9915882345,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE','Sh. Binder Pal Mittal, Chairman M/s Sushma Buildtech','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex, Ist Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex, Ist Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160002','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as the son of the applicants was suffering from celiac disease and for easy access to the good hospitals in Tricity, the applicants purchased Apartment No. G-1203 in Tower-G for a sale consideration of Rs. 45,77,100/- (Annexure A-2). Later on, the applicants requested the respondents to change the Apartment and the respondent allotted Apartment No. G-403 on 4th Floor in “G” Tower vide allotment letter dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-1) in exchange of G-1203 and adjusted the above-payment in G-403. The applicants paid full payment of the apartment i.e. G-1203 on 04.07.2016.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per the terms and condition of the lopsided agreement dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-3), the respondents were bound to deliver the possession within 12 months from the date of execution of Annexure A-3 but the respondents failed to deliver the actual physical possession of the Apartment by the due date. The relevant clause regarding the possession is reproduced hereunder:-&nbsp;</p><p>“14.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>POSSESSION :</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The Developer shall endeavor to give possession of the said unit to the buyer within a period of Twelve (12) months from the date of execution of this Agreement unless and until restrained by circumstances beyond its contemplation and control and subject to timely payment by the allottee. Besides, the Developer can take six months grace period for completing and handing over the said unit to the buyer.”</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That being aggrieved from the act and conduct of the respondents, the applicants made numerous representations (Annexure A-4) for delivering the possession of the apartment but to no effect.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4.&nbsp; The Ld. Tribunal permitted to file fresh complaint.&nbsp; The copy of the order dated 16.01.2019 Annexure A-5<br></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\"><br></span>5. That till today, the applicants are running from pillar to post to get the actual physical possession of the Apartment but the respondent did not paid any heed to the request of the applicants.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>6. Detailed Petition is attached herewith as (Annexure A-6)</p><div><br></div>','<p>(i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to pay compensationas per Section 12, 18 and 19 of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act amounting Rs. 2,50,000/- for mental &amp; physical harassment committed upon the applicants by the respondents on account of delay in handing over the possession of the Apartment, deficiency in the services and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents and on account of losses suffered by the applicants as the applicants have taken some other premises on rent because the respondent failed to deliver the possession of the Apartment on stipulated time.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>(ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Further directions may please be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on account of litigation charges to the applicant.</p><p><br></p><p>(iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>It is further prayed that this Hon\'bleCourt may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of justice, equity and fair play.</p>',4577100.00,4577100.00,'2017-09-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-09-15 00:00:00','2016-09-15 00:00:00','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE\r\nApartment No. G-403, 4th Floor\r\nBishangarh&Bishanpura,\r\nZirakpur, District S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali)','','',2,0,0,0,'VijeshJaiswal','2019-03-12 19:25:01.000','VijeshJaiswal','2019-03-12 19:25:01.000'),(367,1126,'1126',1388,'9f925b8d-3343-4247-ac11-f438350e37ab','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-12 20:07:08.000','Vijesh Jaiswal','vijesh44@gmail.com',9416001990,0,0,'D-44, Bawa Vihar','Sector-9',13,1,'134003','1','F-112, Orbit Apartments','VIP Road, Adjacent Metro Wholesale',28,507,'140603','Ashutosh Vig','sarassociates1211@gmail.com',9915882345,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE','Sh. Binder Pal Mittal, Chairman M/s Sushma Buildtech','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex, Ist Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex, Ist Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160002','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as the son of the applicants was suffering from celiac disease and for easy access to the good hospitals in Tricity, the applicants purchased Apartment No. G-1203 in Tower-G for a sale consideration of Rs. 45,77,100/- (Annexure A-2). Later on, the applicants requested the respondents to change the Apartment and the respondent allotted Apartment No. G-403 on 4th Floor in “G” Tower vide allotment letter dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-1) in exchange of G-1203 and adjusted the above-payment in G-403. The applicants paid full payment of the apartment i.e. G-1203 on 04.07.2016.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That as per the terms and condition of the lopsided agreement dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-3), the respondents were bound to deliver the possession within 12 months from the date of execution of Annexure A-3 but the respondents failed to deliver the actual physical possession of the Apartment by the due date. The relevant clause regarding the possession is reproduced hereunder:-&nbsp;</p><p>“14.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>POSSESSION :</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The Developer shall endeavor to give possession of the said unit to the buyer within a period of Twelve (12) months from the date of execution of this Agreement unless and until restrained by circumstances beyond its contemplation and control and subject to timely payment by the allottee. Besides, the Developer can take six months grace period for completing and handing over the said unit to the buyer.”</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That being aggrieved from the act and conduct of the respondents, the applicants made numerous representations (Annexure A-4) for delivering the possession of the apartment but to no effect.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4.&nbsp; The Ld. Tribunal permitted to file fresh complaint.&nbsp; The copy of the order dated 16.01.2019 Annexure A-5<br></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\"><br></span>5. That till today, the applicants are running from pillar to post to get the actual physical possession of the Apartment but the respondent did not paid any heed to the request of the applicants.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>6. Detailed Petition is attached herewith as (Annexure A-6)</p><div><br></div>','<p>(i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to pay compensationas per Section 12, 18 and 19 of Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act amounting Rs. 2,50,000/- for mental &amp; physical harassment committed upon the applicants by the respondents on account of delay in handing over the possession of the Apartment, deficiency in the services and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents and on account of losses suffered by the applicants as the applicants have taken some other premises on rent because the respondent failed to deliver the possession of the Apartment on stipulated time.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>(ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Further directions may please be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on account of litigation charges to the applicant.</p><p><br></p><p>(iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>It is further prayed that this Hon\'bleCourt may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of justice, equity and fair play.</p>',4577100.00,4577100.00,'2017-09-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-09-15 00:00:00','2016-09-15 00:00:00','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE\r\nApartment No. G-403, 4th Floor\r\nBishangarh&Bishanpura,\r\nZirakpur, District S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali)','','',1,0,0,0,'VijeshJaiswal','2019-03-12 19:25:45.000','VijeshJaiswal','2019-03-12 19:25:45.000'),(368,1140,'1140',1434,'818890d2-1971-40af-b480-ff1ace27c4f7','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-13 17:52:03.000','Indu Indu','mukesh_rai9@yahoo.com',9417573099,0,0,'House No. 8, Type-2, Panjab University Residential Complex','Sector-25',6,128,'160014','1','House No. 8, Type-2, Panjab University Residential Complex','Sector-25',6,128,'160014','Dr. Mukesh Kumar','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','Gateway City, Sector 118-119, Mohali, Project of PUDA','Chief Administrator PUDA, Mohali','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector-62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector-62',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Ms. Payal daughter of Sh. Amar Singh R/o  House No. 341, Street No. 3, Ekta Nagar, Malout-152107 had applied for 200 square yards plot in Gateway City, sector 118-119 in PUDA. Letter of Intent (LoI) Memo No. PUDA-E.O.-Gateway City/2015/24455 was issued to her 24-06-2015 Ms. Payal submitted an application for transfer of Letter of Intent in my (Indu) name after receiving the payments made by her to PUDA from me (ANNEXURE-2).\r\n</p><p>In response to her application the Letter of Intent No. 24455 was transferred in my favour vide No. 2818 Dated 09-09-2015 (ANNEXURE-3) under the terms and conditions of the original Letter of Intent. \r\n</p><p>Subsequently allotment letter No. PUDA-E.O.-Supdt-2 (689/118-119)/2016 44406 dated 21-09-2016 (ANNEXURE-4) was issued to me intimating the allotment of Plot number 689 measuring 211.19 square yards (11.19 square yards in excess). The requested amount was deposited on 21-10-2016 making the total amount paid to be 25 Percent of the total cost of the plot. The remaining 75 Percent of the total cost, after a rebate of 5 Percent as per the Section 3(IV) of the Allotment letter, was paid on 17-11-2016, and accordingly No Objection Certificate No. 778 dated 20-12-2016 ANNEXURE-5) was issued to me by PUDA.\r\n</p><p>As per section 4(I) of the allotment letter PUDA promised to hand over the possession of the said plot after the completion of the development work or 18 months after the date of issuance of the allotment letter, whichever is earlier. \r\n</p><p>Despite making the full payment of all the dues much before the scheduled time and even after the completion of nearly 30 months after issuance of allotment letter (12 months in excess to the promised possession delivery date) the possession of the plot has not been delivered to me.\r\n</p><p>The total amount paid for the plot constituted the following: 30.0 Lacs Plot loan taken from HDFC Ltd. ANNEXURE-6), 5.8 Lacs as maturity amount of PLI of my husband, 3.5 Lacs loan taken by my husband, 5.0 Lacs from household savings.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I\r\nwant to withdraw from the project with the refund of total amount paid along\r\nwith the interest of 12 Percent per annum from the date of deposit of the money\r\nto PUDA as per the Section 18 of The Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nAct, 2016. </span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">The detailed description of the amounts\r\npaid by me, and the detailed Desired Refund Amount/Desired Compensation are\r\ngiven in Annexure-1. The Desired Refund Amount/Desired Compensation are\r\nsummarized below:</span></p><ol><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Refund\r\nof Rs. 42,68,688 which was paid as the cost of the plot.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">12\r\nPercent interest on Rs. 42,68,688 from 17-11-2016 to till date i.e. from the\r\ndate of making full payment of the plot to PUDA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Refund\r\nof Rs. 88,700 paid as cancer cess to PUDA<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">12\r\nPercent interest on Rs.10,50,000 from 20-07-2015 to 17-09-2016 i.e. from the\r\ndate of completion of 25% payment to PUDA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">7000\r\nper month in lieu of the house rent being deducted by the employer of my\r\nhusband from 21-03-2018 i.e. promised date of possession of the plot to till\r\ndate.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">5.0 Lacs as\r\ncompensation for mental harassment and trauma we are going through from last so\r\nmany months in wait of a fully paid plot to reside in.</span><br></li></ol>',4268688.00,4268688.00,'2018-03-21 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-09-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No. 689, Gateway City, Sector 118-119, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'Indu','2019-03-13 17:00:53.000','Indu','2019-03-13 17:00:53.000'),(369,1140,'1140',1434,'818890d2-1971-40af-b480-ff1ace27c4f7','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-13 17:52:03.000','Indu Indu','mukesh_rai9@yahoo.com',9417573099,0,0,'House No. 8, Type-2, Panjab University Residential Complex','Sector-25',6,128,'160014','1','House No. 8, Type-2, Panjab University Residential Complex','Sector-25',6,128,'160014','Dr. Mukesh Kumar','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','Gateway City, Sector 118-119, Mohali, Project of PUDA','Chief Administrator PUDA, Mohali','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector-62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector-62',28,507,'160062','1','<ul><li>Ms. Payal daughter of Sh. Amar Singh R/o  House No. 341, Street No. 3, Ekta Nagar, Malout-152107 had applied for 200 square yards plot in Gateway City, sector 118-119 in PUDA. Letter of Intent (LoI)&nbsp; No. 24455 was issued to her on 24-06-201