\r\nAct, 2016. </span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">The detailed description of the amounts\r\npaid by me, and the detailed Desired Refund Amount/Desired Compensation are\r\ngiven in Annexure-1. The Desired Refund Amount/Desired Compensation are\r\nsummarized below:</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></p><ol><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Refund\r\nof Rs. 42,68,688 which was paid as the cost of the plot after availing rebate as per&nbsp;</span>Section 3(IV) of the Allotment letter.</li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Interest on Rs. 42,68,688 from 17-11-2016 to till date i.e. from the\r\ndate of making full payment of the plot to PUDA.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Refund\r\nof Rs. 88,700 paid as cancer cess to PUDA.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Interest on Rs.10,50,000 from 20-07-2015 to 17-09-2016 i.e. from the\r\ndate of completion of 25% payment to PUDA till the date of making final payment.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">7000\r\nper month in lieu of the house rent being deducted by the employer of my\r\nhusband from 21-03-2018 i.e. promised date of possession of the plot to till\r\ndate.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">5.0 Lacs as\r\ncompensation for mental harassment and trauma we are going through from last so\r\nmany months in wait of a fully paid plot to reside in.</span></li></ol>',4434990.00,4268688.00,'2018-03-21 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-09-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No. 689, Gateway City, Sector 118-119, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'Indu','2019-03-14 16:58:50.000','Indu','2019-03-14 16:58:50.000'),(371,1141,'1141',1094,'5307214d-513f-428e-a103-9ead98ac25bf','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-16 20:49:40.000','Karnail Singh Brar','londonksreracomplainant@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'Village Jawahar Singh Wala','Teh. Nihal Singh Wala',28,393,'142055','1','Tejwant Singh, R/o H.No. 2619,','Sector 70, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'160071','Rajesh Gupta for EMAAR MGF','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PB0231','The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Respectfully showeth&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;That the present complaint is being filed&nbsp; by allotee through his attorney. That the applicant had applied for the allotment of a unit &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;number H2GF GF02 in the project of the respondent in the year 2008 and &nbsp;was subsequently was issued an allotment on 01-04-2008. &nbsp;The unit was measuring 1350 Sq. Ft. of Super area.The total consideration &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;amount of the unit was Rs.&nbsp;4432619 (Rs. Forty Four Lakh Thirty Two Thousand Six Hundred Nineteen only). That the applicant has till date i.e 30-03-2010 has paid Rs. 4005708/- (Rs. Forty Lakh Five Thousand Seven Hundred Eight only). That an agreement dated 29-05-2008 was reduced into writing and as per clause number 21.1 of the agreement, the applicant &nbsp;was to get the possession of the said unit within the period of 36 months from the date of allotment, working out to be on 28-05- 2011. Till date the applicant has got no letter of handing over of the &nbsp; possession and for the best reasons known to the&nbsp;respondent. the applicant\'s money is being withheld by the respondent . That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction&nbsp; and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, the applicant has filed the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement. The applicant had filed an application under form \'N\', earlier, but the same could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab and after the decision of the said appeals, this fresh complaint is filed again, seeking the relief which this Hon\'ble Forum deems fit in the interest of Justice.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses&nbsp; apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p>',4432619.00,4005706.00,'2011-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-04-01 00:00:00','2008-05-29 00:00:00','H2GF GF02, The Views, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.\r\n','','',2,0,0,0,'london.ksrera','2019-03-15 19:21:25.000','london.ksrera','2019-03-15 19:21:25.000'),(372,1136,'1136',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-08 20:36:20.000','NAVDEEP SINGH ANAND','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Raj Guru Nagar','LUDHIANA',28,366,'141012','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','SANJEEV GUPTA','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','IREO WATERFRONT','M/S IREO WATERFRONT PVT LTD','Rera.Punjab@ireo.in',9810117993,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road opp Ferozepur Road','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road opp Ferozepur Road','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">On 22.9.15,Complainants booked (brochure &amp;\r\napplication as C-1 &amp; C-2) a built-up villa,Type B2,Unit No 104,2844 sq ft\r\nof built area,to be constructed on 287.04 sq yd plot.Allotment letter was\r\nissued to them(C-3).Complainants opted for construction linked plan.Total sale\r\nconsideration including all charges &amp; taxes was fixed as Rs.17000222.Buyer\r\nagreement (C-4) was executed on 26.11.15.As per clause 11.3,respondent was\r\nbound to handover the possession within 18 months from the date of execution of\r\nagreement.Said period has already expired on 25.05.17.Respondent has only\r\ncompleted the plinth level.There is no default on the part of complainants in\r\nmaking the payments.The payments which were due on 28.9.15, 28.10.15 &amp;\r\n27.12.15 were paid by complainants on 22.9.15, 26/28.11.15, 18/25.5.16\r\nrespectively.There was no delay attributed to the complainants and thus, no\r\ndelayed interest was demanded from the complainants since they were not at\r\nfault.A communication in this regard is attached as C-5.Thereafter vide demand\r\nletter (C-5) dt 3.9.17,a sum of Rs. 1859828 was demanded, which was duly paid\r\non 30.10.17 &amp; 5.11.17,under protest,since there was dispute about charging\r\nof GST &amp; also vide letter dt 9.10.17 &amp; 30.10.17(C-5),it was duly\r\nconveyed to respondents but respondent did not reply satisfactorily vide letter\r\ndt 30.10.17(C-5).A sum of Rs. 6001038.30(receipts &amp; documents C-5 colly)has\r\nalready been paid by the complainants.The next installment was due on the\r\ncasting of GF roof slab which has not been done &amp; consequently there has\r\nbeen no demand raised by the respondent.Respondent has also stopped the\r\ndevelopment work at the site.A letter was also sent to respondent in this\r\nregard on 14.12.18 &amp;16.12.18(C-6) but no reply has been received.Since there\r\nhas been delay in construction &amp; the respondent was bound to deliver the\r\npossession by 25.05.17,the complainants wishes to withdraw &amp; thus are\r\nseeking refund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; Compensation</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.05.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development. The complainants does not wish to remain in the project since there has been a huge delay on the part of the respondent.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To direct the respondent to pay compensation to the tune of Rs. 500000 lacs <span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">f<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">or causing mental and physical harassment\r\nand agony to the complainants on account of delay in possession, for not doing any development on the project site, keeping the hard earned money of the complainants for so many years. The complainant has also availed the loan for paying the installments to the respondent.</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -48px; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 46.6667px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">To pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</span><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><u><o:p></o:p></u></span></span><br></span><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:250%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1