\nagreement (C-4) was executed on 26.11.15.As per clause 11.3,respondent was\r\nbound to handover the possession within 18 months from the date of execution of\r\nagreement.Said period has already expired on 25.05.17.Respondent has only\r\ncompleted the plinth level.There is no default on the part of complainants in\r\nmaking the payments.The payments which were due on 28.9.15, 28.10.15 &amp;\r\n27.12.15 were paid by complainants on 22.9.15, 26/28.11.15, 18/25.5.16\r\nrespectively.There was no delay attributed to the complainants and thus, no\r\ndelayed interest was demanded from the complainants since they were not at\r\nfault.A communication in this regard is attached as C-5.Thereafter vide demand\r\nletter (C-5) dt 3.9.17,a sum of Rs. 1859828 was demanded, which was duly paid\r\non 30.10.17 &amp; 5.11.17,under protest,since there was dispute about charging\r\nof GST &amp; also vide letter dt 9.10.17 &amp; 30.10.17(C-5),it was duly\r\nconveyed to respondents but respondent did not reply satisfactorily vide letter\r\ndt 30.10.17(C-5).A sum of Rs. 6001038.30(receipts &amp; documents C-5 colly)has\r\nalready been paid by the complainants.The next installment was due on the\r\ncasting of GF roof slab which has not been done &amp; consequently there has\r\nbeen no demand raised by the respondent.Respondent has also stopped the\r\ndevelopment work at the site.A letter was also sent to respondent in this\r\nregard on 14.12.18 &amp;16.12.18(C-6) but no reply has been received.Since there\r\nhas been delay in construction &amp; the respondent was bound to deliver the\r\npossession by 25.05.17,the complainants wishes to withdraw &amp; thus are\r\nseeking refund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; Compensation</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.05.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development. The complainants does not wish to remain in the project since there has been a huge delay on the part of the respondent.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To direct the respondent to pay compensation to the tune of Rs. 500000 lacs <span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">f<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">or causing mental and physical harassment\r\nand agony to the complainants on account of delay in possession, for not doing any development on the project site, keeping the hard earned money of the complainants for so many years. The complainant has also availed the loan for paying the installments to the respondent.</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -48px; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 46.6667px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">To pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</span><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><u><o:p></o:p></u></span></span><br></span><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;\r\nmargin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:250%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:250%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></p></span></li></ol>',17000222.00,6001038.30,'2017-05-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2015-10-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 104, Type B-2, Built Up Villa','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-15 20:33:39.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-15 20:33:39.000'),(374,1136,'1136',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-08 20:36:20.000','NAVDEEP SINGH ANAND','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Raj Guru Nagar','LUDHIANA',28,366,'141012','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','SANJEEV GUPTA','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','IREO WATERFRONT','M/S IREO WATERFRONT PVT LTD','Rera.Punjab@ireo.in',9810117993,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road  OFF Ferozepur Road','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141102','1','Sidhwan Canal Road  OFF Ferozepur Road','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141102','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">On 22.9.15,Complainants booked (brochure &amp;\r\napplication as C-1 &amp; C-2) a built-up villa,Type B2,Unit No 104,2844 sq ft\r\nof built area,to be constructed on 287.04 sq yd plot.Allotment letter was\r\nissued to them(C-3).Complainants opted for construction linked plan.Total sale\r\nconsideration including all charges &amp; taxes was fixed as Rs.17000222.Buyer\r\nagreement (C-4) was executed on 26.11.15.As per clause 11.3,respondent was\r\nbound to handover the possession within 18 months from the date of execution of\r\nagreement.Said period has already expired on 25.05.17.Respondent has only\r\ncompleted the plinth level.There is no default on the part of complainants in\r\nmaking the payments.The payments which were due on 28.9.15, 28.10.15 &amp;\r\n27.12.15 were paid by complainants on 22.9.15, 26/28.11.15, 18/25.5.16\r\nrespectively.There was no delay attributed to the complainants and thus, no\r\ndelayed interest was demanded from the complainants since they were not at\r\nfault.A communication in this regard is attached as C-5.Thereafter vide demand\r\nletter (C-5) dt 3.9.17,a sum of Rs. 1859828 was demanded, which was duly paid\r\non 30.10.17 &amp; 5.11.17,under protest,since there was dispute about charging\r\nof GST &amp; also vide letter dt 9.10.17 &amp; 30.10.17(C-5),it was duly\r\nconveyed to respondents but respondent did not reply satisfactorily vide letter\r\ndt 30.10.17(C-5).A sum of Rs. 6001038.30(receipts &amp; documents C-5 colly)has\r\nalready been paid by the complainants.The next installment was due on the\r\ncasting of GF roof slab which has not been done &amp; consequently there has\r\nbeen no demand raised by the respondent.Respondent has also stopped the\r\ndevelopment work at the site.A letter was also sent to respondent in this\r\nregard on 14.12.18 &amp;16.12.18(C-6) but no reply has been received.Since there\r\nhas been delay in construction &amp; the respondent was bound to deliver the\r\npossession by 25.05.17,the complainants wishes to withdraw &amp; thus are\r\nseeking refund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; Compensation</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.05.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development. The complainants does not wish to remain in the project since there has been a huge delay on the part of the respondent.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To direct the respondent to pay compensation to the tune of Rs. 500000 lacs <span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">f<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">or causing mental and physical harassment\r\nand agony to the complainants on account of delay in possession, for not doing any development on the project site, keeping the hard earned money of the complainants for so many years. The complainant has also availed the loan for paying the installments to the respondent.</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\