efund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; Compensation</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.05.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development. The complainants does not wish to remain in the project since there has been a huge delay on the part of the respondent.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To direct the respondent to pay compensation to the tune of Rs. 500000 lacs <span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">f<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">or causing mental and physical harassment\r\nand agony to the complainants on account of delay in possession, for not doing any development on the project site, keeping the hard earned money of the complainants for so many years. The complainant has also availed the loan for paying the installments to the respondent.</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 250%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-va