round-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal,booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 30,000/- through RTGS on 10.01.2013 against which receipt Number HP 323 dated 20.01.2013 was issued by the respondent which is annexed herewith as C/I.The complainant made further payment of Rs. 1,00,000/- through RTGS on 14.01.2013 against which another receipt Number HP324 dated 20.01.2013 was issued which is annexed as C/II.Thereafter, further payment of Rs. 1,12,500/- was made vide cheque No 77953 dated 20.01.2013 &amp; a sum of Rs. 1,40,000/- was paid vide cheque No 52863 dated 20.01.2013 against which two receipts numbers HP325 &amp; HP 326 were issued by the respondent on 20.01.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III (Colly).Thus, total booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- was paid to the respondent which was acknowledged vide receipts dated 20.01.2013 issued by the respondent as above. That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/IV (Colly).That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession.That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent.Ann-V.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That\r\nthe complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan\r\naccount of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of\r\nRs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-,\r\n17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs.\r\n1,87,338/-.A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed\r\nherewith as annexure C/VI.</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That\r\ncomplainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an\r\namount of Rs.1,92,675/-which also acknowledged the payments made by the\r\ncomplainant of Rs. 25,05,517/- which <span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp;</span>is\r\nannexed herewith as Annexure C/VII.</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\noffer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter.The said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated\r\n7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy/completion certificate.These documents are\r\nannexed herewith as Annexure C/VIII(Colly).</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That\r\nthe respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make\r\npayment of Rs.1,82,869/- within 15days.The said legal notice was replied by\r\nthe complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the\r\ncompletion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the\r\ncomplainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018\r\ndemanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-.The documents are annexed herewith as\r\nAnnexure C/IX(Colly).</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nrespondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on\r\n17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount and further\r\nstated that the refund will be made after the deduction of the amount as per\r\nthe terms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the\r\ncomplainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as\r\nAnnexure C/X.The respondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within the specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the provisions of the Section 18 of the prayer-Compensation.</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><br></p>',2550000.00,2422000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NO-950,FLOOR NO-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI,DISTT. MOHALI,PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 14:34:43.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 14:34:43.000'),(382,1110,'1110',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-25 14:48:18.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SINGLA BUILDERS & PROMOTERS LTD','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal, resident of House No D-102, Arya Samaj Road, Uttam Nagar, New Delhi booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.&nbsp; The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- to the respondent as per details annexed at Annexure C/1(Colly). That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/II(Colly). That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-.&nbsp; As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession. That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent and a payment receipt No HP566 dated 19.04.2013 was issued which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III. That the complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan account of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of Rs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-, 17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs. 1,87,338/-. A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed herewith as annexure C/IV. That complainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an amount of Rs. 192,675/- which also acknowledged the payments made by the complainant of Rs. 25,05,517/-which&nbsp; is at C/V.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The offer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter. The said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated 7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy /completion certificate. These documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VI(Colly).&nbsp; That the respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make payment of Rs. 1,82,869/- within 15 days. The said legal notice was replied by the complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the completion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the complainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018 demanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-. The documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VII (Colly).&nbsp; The respondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on 17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount as per the terms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the complainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as Annexure C/VIII. The project “SBP housing Park” is a RERA registered Project(PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096),being an ongoing project. Therefore, the provisions of the Act would apply with respect to offer of possession, refund, interest and compensation etc in the present case. The respondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within the specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the provisions of the Section 18 of the Act. The complainant has lost faith in the project and promoters in view of the termination notice issued which is not tenable in law. The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project.&nbsp; It is humbly prayed that the respondent may be directed to refund the amount paid by the complainant, interest as per provisions of RERA Act/Rules from the respective dates of payments made by the complainant and compensation of Rs. 2,00,000/- on account of mental harassment.</p>',2550000.00,2422000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NO-950,FLOOR NO-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI,DISTT. MOHALI,PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:20:12.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:20:12.000'),(383,1110,'1110',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-25 14:48:18.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SINGLA BUILDERS & PROMOTERS LTD','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal, resident of House No D-102, Arya Samaj Road, Uttam Nagar, New Delhi booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.&nbsp; The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- to the respondent as per details annexed at Annexure C/1(Colly). That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/II(Colly). That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-.&nbsp; As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession. That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent and a payment receipt No HP566 dated 19.04.2013 was issued which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III. That the complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan account of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of Rs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-, 17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs. 1,87,338/-. A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed herewith as annexure C/IV. That complainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an amount of Rs. 192,675/- which also acknowledged the payments made by the complainant of Rs. 25,05,517/-which&nbsp; is at C/V.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The offer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter. The said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated 7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy /completion certificate. These documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VI(Colly).&nbsp; That the respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make payment of Rs. 1,82,869/- within 15 days. The said legal notice was replied by the complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the completion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the complainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018 demanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-. The documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VII (Colly).&nbsp; The respondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on 17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount as per the terms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the complainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as Annexure C/VIII. The project “SBP housing Park” is a RERA registered Project(PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096),being an ongoing project. Therefore, the provisions of the Act would apply with respect to offer of possession, refund, interest and compensation etc in the present case. The respondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within the specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the provisions of the Section 18 of the Act. The complainant has lost faith in the project and promoters in view of the termination notice issued which is not tenable in law. The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project.&nbsp; It is humbly prayed that the respondent may be directed to refund the amount paid by the complainant, interest as per provisions of RERA Act/Rules from the respective dates of payments made by the complainant and compensation of Rs. 2,00,000/- on account of mental harassment.</p>',2550000.00,2505517.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NO-950,FLOOR NO-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI,DISTT. MOHALI,PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:37:46.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:37:46.000'),(384,1110,'1110',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-25 14:48:18.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SINGLA BUILDERS & PROMOTERS LTD','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal, resident of House No D-102, Arya Samaj Road, Uttam Nagar, New Delhi booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.&nbsp; The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- to the respondent as per details annexed at Annexure C/1(Colly). That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/II(Colly). That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-.&nbsp; As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession. That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent and a payment receipt No HP566 dated 19.04.2013 was issued which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III. That the complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan account of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of Rs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-, 17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs. 1,87,338/-. A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed herewith as annexure C/IV. That complainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an amount of Rs. 192,675/- which also acknowledged the payments made by the complainant of Rs. 25,05,517/-which&nbsp; is at C/V.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The offer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter. The said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated 7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy /completion certificate. These documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VI(Colly).&nbsp; That the respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make payment of Rs. 1,82,869/- within 15 days. The said legal notice was replied by the complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the completion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the complainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018 demanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-. The documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VII (Colly).&nbsp; The respondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on 17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount as per the terms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the complainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as Annexure C/VIII. The project “SBP housing Park” is a RERA registered Project(PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096),being an ongoing project. Therefore, the provisions of the Act would apply with respect to offer of possession, refund, interest and compensation etc in the present case. The respondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within the specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the provisions of the Section 18 of the Act. The complainant has lost faith in the project and promoters in view of the termination notice issued which is not tenable in law. The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project.&nbsp; It is humbly prayed that the respondent may be directed to refund the amount paid by the complainant, interest as per provisions of RERA Act/Rules from the respective dates of payments made by the complainant and compensation of Rs. 2,00,000/- on account of mental harassment.</p>',2550000.00,2505517.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NO-950,FLOOR NO-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI,DISTT. MOHALI,PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:38:28.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:38:28.000'),(385,1110,'1110',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-17 16:39:09.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SINGLA BUILDERS & PROMOTERS LTD','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO146-148','1st floor ,sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal, resident of House No D-102, Arya Samaj Road, Uttam Nagar, New Delhi booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.&nbsp; The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- to the respondent as per details annexed at Annexure C/1(Colly). That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/II(Colly). That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-.&nbsp; As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession. That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent and a payment receipt No HP566 dated 19.04.2013 was issued which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III. That the complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan account of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of Rs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-, 17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs. 1,87,338/-. A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed herewith as annexure C/IV. That complainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an amount of Rs. 192,675/- which also acknowledged the payments made by the complainant of Rs. 25,05,517/-which&nbsp; is at C/V.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The offer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter. The said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated 7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy /completion certificate. These documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VI(Colly).&nbsp; That the respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make payment of Rs. 1,82,869/- within 15 days. The said legal notice was replied by the complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the completion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the complainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018 demanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-. The documents are annexed herewith as Annexure C/VII (Colly).&nbsp; The respondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on 17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount as per the terms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the complainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as Annexure C/VIII. The project “SBP housing Park” is a RERA registered Project(PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096),being an ongoing project. Therefore, the provisions of the Act would apply with respect to offer of possession, refund, interest and compensation etc in the present case. The respondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within the specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the provisions of the Section 18 of the Act. The complainant has lost faith in the project and promoters in view of the termination notice issued which is not tenable in law. The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project.&nbsp; It is humbly prayed that the respondent may be directed to refund the amount paid by the complainant, interest as per provisions of RERA Act/Rules from the respective dates of payments made by the complainant and compensation of Rs. 2,00,000/- on account of mental harassment.</p>',2550000.00,2505517.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NO-950,FLOOR NO-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI,DISTT. MOHALI,PUNJAB','','',1,1,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:39:04.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-17 16:39:04.000'),(386,1142,'1142',1442,'67d2e02c-e2aa-4692-ab9c-170f0f6a5bda','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SOURABH AGGARWAL','aggarwal.sourabh@gmail.com',9872765288,0,0,'HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','1','HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','CA DEEPAK GARG','cadeepakgarg@gmail.com',9855519149,9855519149,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA, ATS INFRABUILD PVT LTD','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','EMAIL@ATSGREENS.COM',0,0,'ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','<p>FACT<br></p>','<p>FACT<br></p>',14111000.00,12463121.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','APARTMENT NO 11211 21ST FLOOR, TOWER 11, ATS CASA ESPANA, SECTOR 121, NEAR VERKA PLANT MOHALI','','',2,0,0,0,'sourabh','2019-03-19 15:34:00.000','sourabh','2019-03-19 15:34:00.000'),(387,1142,'1142',1442,'67d2e02c-e2aa-4692-ab9c-170f0f6a5bda','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SOURABH AGGARWAL','aggarwal.sourabh@gmail.com',9872765288,0,0,'HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','1','HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','CA DEEPAK GARG','cadeepakgarg@gmail.com',9855519149,9855519149,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA, ATS INFRABUILD PVT LTD','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','EMAIL@ATSGREENS.COM',0,0,'ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','<p>ON MARCH 31ST 2015 COMPLAINANT MR SOURABH AGGARWAL AND HIS WIFE SHVETA AGGARWAL HAD BOOKED A RESIDENTIAL FLAT IN TOWER NO 1, ON 21ST FLOOR BY GIVING AN AMOUNT OF RS. 22,00,000 AS ADVANCE.AGREEMENT TO SELL WAS DULY EXECUTED IN DUE COURSE WHERE IN DATE OF COMPLETION WAS MENTIONED AS 42 MONTHS FROM SIGNING OF AGREEMENT. BUT MEANTIME DUE TO NON DEVEOPMENT AND DETAILED DISCUSSION THE COMPLAINANT OPT FOR TOWER NO 11, APARTMENT NO 11211 AND NEW AGREEMENT TO SELL WAS EXECUTED WHEREIN BY MISTAKE THE SAME CLAUSE 42 MONTHS WAS MENTIONED. WHEN THE BUYER RAISED HIS CONCERN OVER IT MR DEEPAK MAKHIJA (GENERAL MANAGER SALES) GIVE WRITTEN COMMUNICATION THAT DATE OF POSSESSION WILL BE 31ST MARCH 2018 + 3 MONTHS OF GRACE.</p><p>PAYMENT WAS MADE TILL DATE IS RS.12463161 INCLUDING TAX, EDC, EXTRA CAR PARKING ETC.</p><p>POSSESSION IS LATE BY APPORXIMATELY ONE YEAR AND THERE IS STILL NO CHANCE OF POSSESSION IN NEAR BY.<br></p>','<p>FACT<br></p>',14111000.00,12463121.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','APARTMENT NO 11211 21ST FLOOR, TOWER 11, ATS CASA ESPANA, SECTOR 121, NEAR VERKA PLANT MOHALI','','',2,0,0,0,'sourabh','2019-03-19 15:40:22.000','sourabh','2019-03-19 15:40:22.000'),(388,1142,'1142',1442,'67d2e02c-e2aa-4692-ab9c-170f0f6a5bda','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SOURABH AGGARWAL','aggarwal.sourabh@gmail.com',9872765288,0,0,'HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','1','HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','CA DEEPAK GARG','cadeepakgarg@gmail.com',9855519149,9855519149,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA, ATS INFRABUILD PVT LTD','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','EMAIL@ATSGREENS.COM',0,0,'ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','<p>FACT OF THE CASE:<br></p><p>ON MARCH 31ST 2015 COMPLAINANT MR SOURABH AGGARWAL AND HIS WIFE SHVETA AGGARWAL HAD BOOKED A RESIDENTIAL FLAT IN TOWER NO 1, ON 21ST FLOOR BY GIVING AN AMOUNT OF RS. 22,00,000 AS ADVANCE. AGREEMENT TO SELL WAS DULY EXECUTED IN DUE COURSE WHERE IN DATE OF COMPLETION WAS MENTIONED AS 42 MONTHS FROM SIGNING OF AGREEMENT. </p><p>BUT MEANTIME DUE TO NON DEVEOPMENT AND DETAILED DISCUSSION WITH BUILDER REGARDING THIS, THE COMPLAINANT OPT FOR TOWER NO 11, APARTMENT NO 11211 AND NEW AGREEMENT TO SELL WAS EXECUTED WHEREIN BY MISTAKE THE SAME CLAUSE 42 MONTHS WAS MENTIONED- FROM THE DATE OF EXECUTION OF NEW AGREEMENT, INSTEAD OF DATE OF EXECUTION OF OLD AGREEMENT.</p><p>WHEN THE BUYER RAISED HIS CONCERN OVER IT MR DEEPAK MAKHIJA (GENERAL MANAGER SALES) GIVE WRITTEN COMMUNICATION THAT DATE OF POSSESSION WILL BE 31ST MARCH 2018 + 3 MONTHS OF GRACE.</p><p>PAYMENT WAS MADE TILL DATE IS RS.12463161 INCLUDING TAX, EDC, EXTRA CAR PARKING ETC.</p><p>POSSESSION IS LATE BY APPORXIMATELY ONE YEAR AND THERE IS STILL NO CHANCE OF POSSESSION IN NEAR BY.</p><p>THE COMPLAINANT RAISED CONCERN TO ATS SEVERAL TIMES (APPROX 15 MAILS WERE SENT BY BUYER) BUT THERE IS NO CONCRETE REPLY FROM BUILDER SIDE. </p><p>GROUNDS OF APPEAL:</p><p>1. EVEN AFTER PASSING 11 MONTHS FROM THE DATE OF POSSESSION I.E. 31ST MARCH 2018, BUILDER IS FAILED TO HANDOVER THE FLAT.</p><p>2. COMPLAINANT HAD&nbsp;MADE RS.12463161 TILL DTAE (&nbsp;INCLUDING TAX, EDC, EXTRA CAR PARKING ETC.)</p><p>3. COMPLAINANT HAD RAISED A HOUSING LOAN OF RS. 8092761 AND PAYING AN INSTALMENT OF RS. 41593 CURRENTY.<br></p><p>4. IT CAUSES GREAT MENTAL AND FINANCIAL STRESS TO BUYER AND HIS FAMILY.<br></p>','<p>GROUNDS OF RELIEF:</p><p>1. <br></p>',14111000.00,12463121.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','APARTMENT NO 11211 21ST FLOOR, TOWER 11, ATS CASA ESPANA, SECTOR 121, NEAR VERKA PLANT MOHALI','','',2,0,0,0,'sourabh','2019-03-19 15:46:49.000','sourabh','2019-03-19 15:46:49.000'),(389,1142,'1142',1442,'67d2e02c-e2aa-4692-ab9c-170f0f6a5bda','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-20 12:22:22.000','SOURABH AGGARWAL','aggarwal.sourabh@gmail.com',9872765288,0,0,'HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','1','HOUSE NO A-12','NEW GENERATION INDEPENDENT DUPLEX DHAKOLI, MOHALI',28,507,'140603','CA DEEPAK GARG','cadeepakgarg@gmail.com',9855519149,9855519149,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA, ATS INFRABUILD PVT LTD','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','EMAIL@ATSGREENS.COM',0,0,'ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','711/92 DEEPALI NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','<p>FACT OF THE CASE:<br></p><p>ON MARCH 31ST 2015 COMPLAINANT MR SOURABH AGGARWAL AND HIS WIFE SHVETA AGGARWAL HAD BOOKED A RESIDENTIAL FLAT IN TOWER NO 1, ON 21ST FLOOR BY GIVING AN AMOUNT OF RS. 22,00,000 AS ADVANCE. AGREEMENT TO SELL WAS DULY EXECUTED IN DUE COURSE WHERE IN DATE OF COMPLETION WAS MENTIONED AS 42 MONTHS FROM SIGNING OF AGREEMENT. </p><p>BUT MEANTIME DUE TO NON DEVEOPMENT AND DETAILED DISCUSSION WITH BUILDER REGARDING THIS, THE COMPLAINANT OPT FOR TOWER NO 11, APARTMENT NO 11211 AND NEW AGREEMENT TO SELL WAS EXECUTED WHEREIN BY MISTAKE THE SAME CLAUSE 42 MONTHS WAS MENTIONED- FROM THE DATE OF EXECUTION OF NEW AGREEMENT, INSTEAD OF DATE OF EXECUTION OF OLD AGREEMENT.</p><p>WHEN THE BUYER RAISED HIS CONCERN OVER IT MR DEEPAK MAKHIJA (GENERAL MANAGER SALES) GIVE WRITTEN COMMUNICATION THAT DATE OF POSSESSION WILL BE 31ST MARCH 2018 + 3 MONTHS OF GRACE.</p><p>PAYMENT WAS MADE TILL DATE IS RS.12463161 INCLUDING TAX, EDC, EXTRA CAR PARKING ETC.</p><p>POSSESSION IS LATE BY APPORXIMATELY ONE YEAR AND THERE IS STILL NO CHANCE OF POSSESSION IN NEAR BY.</p><p>THE COMPLAINANT RAISED CONCERN TO ATS SEVERAL TIMES (APPROX 15 MAILS WERE SENT BY BUYER) BUT THERE IS NO CONCRETE REPLY FROM BUILDER SIDE. </p><p>GROUNDS OF APPEAL:</p><p>1. EVEN AFTER PASSING 11 MONTHS FROM THE DATE OF POSSESSION I.E. 31ST MARCH 2018, BUILDER IS FAILED TO HANDOVER THE FLAT.</p><p>2. COMPLAINANT HAD&nbsp;MADE RS.12463161 TILL DTAE (&nbsp;INCLUDING TAX, EDC, EXTRA CAR PARKING ETC.)</p><p>3. COMPLAINANT HAD RAISED A HOUSING LOAN OF RS. 8092761 AND PAYING AN INSTALMENT OF RS. 41593 CURRENTY.<br></p><p>4. IT CAUSES GREAT MENTAL AND FINANCIAL STRESS TO BUYER AND HIS FAMILY.<br></p>','<p>COMPENSTATION AND RELIEF:</p><p>1. LUMPSUM INTEREST U/S 18(1) FROM APRIL 2018 TILL THE DECISION OF CASE: INTEREST US 18(1) OF THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) ACT 2016 ON AMOUNT PAID OF RS.12463161/- AT THE RATE SPECIFIED IN CLAUSE 16 AND 17 OF THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) RULES. ALSO IN REFRERENCE TO VARIOUS CASES ALREADY DECIDED BY AUTHOIRTY - (SUPRA) NIKHIL KAWATRA AND RANJINI G VS. MR KULWANT SINGH MD OF M/S JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD.</p><p>2.&nbsp;MONTHLY INTEREST U/S 18(1) FROM&nbsp;THE DECISION OF CASE TILL ACTUAL HANDOVER OF PHYSICAL POSSESSION OF FLAT: INTEREST US 18(1) OF THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) ACT 2016 ON AMOUNT PAID OF RS.12463161/- AT THE RATE SPECIFIED IN CLAUSE 16 AND 17 OF THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) RULES. ALSO IN REFRERENCE TO VARIOUS CASES ALREADY DECIDED BY AUTHOIRTY - (SUPRA) NIKHIL KAWATRA AND RANJINI G VS. MR KULWANT SINGH MD OF M/S JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD.</p><p>3. COMPENSATION OF RS. 10,00,000/- IN LIEU OF MENTAL AND FINANCIAL AGONY U/S 18(1) OF THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT)ACT 2016 </p><p>4. ANY OTHER RELEIF AS FEEL THINKS FIT BY HON\'BLE AUTHORITY<br></p>',14111000.00,12463121.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','APARTMENT NO 11211 21ST FLOOR, TOWER 11, ATS CASA ESPANA, SECTOR 121, NEAR VERKA PLANT MOHALI','','',1,1,0,0,'sourabh','2019-03-19 15:52:26.000','sourabh','2019-03-19 15:52:26.000'),(390,1143,'1143',1331,'8b292055-1541-4c28-810a-ccc6e9a24878','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-19 20:16:53.000','Sameer Madan','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 2123,','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','1','F-1403, 14th Flr., Tower \"F\", Sushma Chandigarh Grande','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande at BishanGarh & Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur\r\n','Bharat Mittal, Authorised Signatory, Sushma BuildTech Ltd.','sushmagrande@gmail.com',0,0,'Plot No. 381','Phase I, Industrial Area',6,128,'160002','1','Plot No. 381','Phase I, Industrial Area',6,128,'160002','1','<p>Respectfully showeth,That the present complaint is being filed by allotee as applicant. That the\r\n applicant had applied for the allotment of a unit number F 1403, 14th Floor, Tower \'F\',in the year 2011, in \'Sushma Chandigarh Grande\' at Bishangarh &amp; Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur. The applicant was subsequently&nbsp; issued an allotment on 14-02 2012 a residential unit measuring 1885 Sq. Ft. of Super Area.The total&nbsp; consideration amount of the unit was Rs. 5990530/-(Rs. Fifty Nine Lakh Ninety Thousand Five Hundred&nbsp; Thirty only). That the applicant had opted for Construction Linked Plan and has paid Rs. 5655261/- (Rs. Fifty Six Lakh Fifty Five Thousand  Two Hundred Sixty One only). That as per clause 14(d) of agreement&nbsp; dated 03-04-2012, the applicant was to get the possession of the said unit within the maximum period of&nbsp; 48 months (inclusive of grace period) from date of agreement. The applicant was to get the possession&nbsp; latest by 02-04-2016, the applicant has not got the possession of the unit for the best reasons known&nbsp; to the respondent. The applicant\'s money is being withheld by the respondent and is being used without&nbsp; any interest. That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project\r\n in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the Appeal Number 53 of 2018 (along with other&nbsp; appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the\r\n jurisdiction and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, the applicant has filed the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement. The applicant had filed an application under form \'N\', earlier, but the same could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab and after the decision of the said appeals,&nbsp; hence this fresh application.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses</p><p>apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified</p><p>explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that</p><p>the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the</p><p>respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without</p><p>delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p>',5990530.00,5655261.00,'2016-04-02 00:00:00.000','2016-04-02 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-02-14 00:00:00','2012-04-03 00:00:00','F-1403, 14th Flr., Tower \"F\", Sushma Chandigarh Grande','','',1,1,0,0,'madaansameer08012019','2019-03-19 19:59:03.000','madaansameer08012019','2019-03-19 19:59:03.000'),(391,1088,'1088',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-24 11:51:32.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','1','Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA Homes','Bhola Ram Goyal','casahomes2016@gmail.com',0,0,'Future City developers pvt. ltd, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','',28,507,'140307','1','Future City developers pvt. ltd, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4)	That as per clause 7 of the agreement, the possession of the flat was to be handed over to the allottee by 31st March 2018 after obtaining OC, but the OC is still to be produced to us for taking possession of the flat which is clearly an event of default by promoter.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"text-indent: -0.25in;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Casa Homes have charged us GST @12% which has\r\nincreased the cost of our flat. As per the government notification, the cost of\r\nflat should come down even after levying the GST and that extra burden should\r\nnot be passed on the buyers. As we have already paid the GST@12% on approx. 90%\r\nof the cost of Flat, please provide us the receipt of GST paid to the\r\ngovernment so that we can take up the matter separately with the department\r\nconcerned for pursuing our case of GST</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->3)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span><!--[endif]-->Casa Homes have sold this flat on the pretext of\r\ngiving Subvention benefit. The same however has been started in July 2018 but stopped\r\nwef 1<sup>st</sup> Sept 2018 whereas the possession of flat is still not given\r\nto us without assigning any reason thereof</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]-->4)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span><!--[endif]-->That as per the clause ( G ) of the agreement,\r\nCarpet area of the Flat is 1350 SqFt , type 2 BHK on second floor in block D.\r\nFurther Clause 1.2 states that that “the total price for the apartment based on\r\nthe carpet area is 2893340 “and having per sqft rate of INR 2143.21. Further\r\nclause 1.7 states that the promoter shall furnish the details of the carpet\r\narea to ascertain the total price of the apartment. Please furnish the required\r\ndetails so that the final price of the flat can be arrived based on the carpet\r\narea.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">1)&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><o:p><br></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><o:p><br></o:p></p>','<p>1. Compensation on account of delayed possession from 1st April 2018 till the date of producing the occupation certificate as per the Rera rules.</p><p>2. Compensation on account of subvention scheme till the time possession has not been accepted , for which payment has been made by promoter till 31st August 2018 but stopped after that.</p><p>3. Actual carpet area to be measured jointly by promoter and allotee and accordingly refund / demand balance payment. The carpet area mentioned in the agreement is 1350 Sqft and the same to be handed over to allotee.</p><p>4. Current state of flat portrays substandard quality and workmanship. All substandard material to be replaced like wooden doors/ Tiles/ etc or compensation to be paid.</p><p>5. Decision of GST demanded by promoter.</p>',2893340.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-10-08 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','DDD-3 , Second Foor ,CASA Homes, Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307','','',1,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2019-03-19 22:06:19.000','Ravikant','2019-03-19 22:06:19.000'),(392,1141,'1141',1094,'5307214d-513f-428e-a103-9ead98ac25bf','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-16 20:49:40.000','Karnail Singh Brar Through Tejwant Singh','londonksreracomplainant@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'Village Jawahar Singh Wala','Teh. Nihal Singh Wala',28,393,'142055','1','Tejwant Singh, R/o H.No. 2619,','Sector 70, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'160071','Rajesh Gupta for EMAAR MGF','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PB0231','The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Respectfully showeth&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;That the present complaint is being filed&nbsp; by allotee through his attorney. That the applicant had applied for the allotment of a unit &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;number H2GF GF02 in the project of the respondent in the year 2008 and &nbsp;was subsequently was issued an allotment on 01-04-2008. &nbsp;The unit was measuring 1350 Sq. Ft. of Super area.The total consideration &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;amount of the unit was Rs.&nbsp;4432619 (Rs. Forty Four Lakh Thirty Two Thousand Six Hundred Nineteen only). That the applicant has till date i.e 30-03-2010 has paid Rs. 4005708/- (Rs. Forty Lakh Five Thousand Seven Hundred Eight only). That an agreement dated 29-05-2008 was reduced into writing and as per clause number 21.1 of the agreement, the applicant &nbsp;was to get the possession of the said unit within the period of 36 months from the date of allotment, working out to be on 28-05- 2011. Till date the applicant has got no letter of handing over of the &nbsp; possession and for the best reasons known to the&nbsp;respondent. the applicant\'s money is being withheld by the respondent . That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction&nbsp; and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, the applicant has filed the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement. The applicant had filed an application under form \'N\', earlier, but the same could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab and after the decision of the said appeals, this fresh complaint is filed again, seeking the relief which this Hon\'ble Forum deems fit in the interest of Justice.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses&nbsp; apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p>',4432619.00,4005706.00,'2011-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-04-01 00:00:00','2008-05-29 00:00:00','H2GF GF02, The Views, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.\r\n','','',2,0,0,0,'london.ksrera','2019-03-20 17:41:39.000','london.ksrera','2019-03-20 17:41:39.000'),(393,1141,'1141',1094,'5307214d-513f-428e-a103-9ead98ac25bf','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-25 19:38:22.000','Karnail Singh Brar Through Tejwant Singh','londonksreracomplainant@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'Village Jawahar Singh Wala','Teh. Nihal Singh Wala',28,393,'142055','1','Tejwant Singh Sidhu, R/o H.No. 2619,','Sector 70, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'160071','Rajesh Gupta for EMAAR MGF','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PB0231','The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Respectfully showeth&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;That the present complaint is being filed&nbsp; by allotee through his attorney. That the applicant had applied for the allotment of a unit &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;number H2GF GF02 in the project of the respondent in the year 2008 and &nbsp;was subsequently was issued an allotment on 01-04-2008. &nbsp;The unit was measuring 1350 Sq. Ft. of Super area.The total consideration &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;amount of the unit was Rs.&nbsp;4432619 (Rs. Forty Four Lakh Thirty Two Thousand Six Hundred Nineteen only). That the applicant has till date i.e 30-03-2010 has paid Rs. 4005708/- (Rs. Forty Lakh Five Thousand Seven Hundred Eight only). That an agreement dated 29-05-2008 was reduced into writing and as per clause number 21.1 of the agreement, the applicant &nbsp;was to get the possession of the said unit within the period of 36 months from the date of allotment, working out to be on 28-05- 2011. Till date the applicant has got no letter of handing over of the &nbsp; possession and for the best reasons known to the&nbsp;respondent. the applicant\'s money is being withheld by the respondent . That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction&nbsp; and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, the applicant has filed the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement. The applicant had filed an application under form \'N\', earlier, but the same could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab and after the decision of the said appeals, this fresh complaint is filed again, seeking the relief which this Hon\'ble Forum deems fit in the interest of Justice.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses&nbsp; apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p>',4432619.00,4005706.00,'2011-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-04-01 00:00:00','2008-05-29 00:00:00','H2GF GF02, The Views, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.\r\n','','',2,0,0,0,'london.ksrera','2019-03-20 18:26:47.000','london.ksrera','2019-03-20 18:26:47.000'),(394,1144,'1144',1133,'6c60c5a1-9072-497b-9240-435da1d8fb69','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-22 18:41:37.000','Harpreet Singh Gill','gill.harpreet2809@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 65,  sector 05,','Chandigarh',6,128,'160015','1','H.No. 65,  sector 05,','Chandigarh',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119',' \"The Views\" at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory Rajesh Gupta','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'SCO 120-122, First Floor,','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 120-122, First Floor,','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Respectfully showeth,That the present complaint is being filed by NRI allotee as co-applicant , as the father of the co-applicant has expired.That the applicant (s) had applied for the allotment\r\n of a unit/apartment No.J1-F10-1004, Tower \'J\',in the year 2008,in \'The Veiws\' in \"Mohali Hills,Sec-105, SAS Nagar Mohali. The applicant(s) were subsequently issued an allotment on 31-01-2008 of a residential unit measuring 1750 Sq. Ft. of Super Area.The total consideration amount of the unit was Rs.5118516/-(Rs. Fifty One Lakhh Eeighteen Thousand Five Hundred Sixteen only).&nbsp; That the applicant had opted pay 95% of the amount mentioned above and paid Rs.4840807/- (Rs.Forty Eight Lakh Forty Thousand Eight Hundred and Seven only) on 04-01-2008. That as per&nbsp; clause 21.1 of agreement, the applicant(s) were to get the possession of the said unit within the maximum period of 39 months (inclusive of grace period) from date of agreement. The applicant(s) were to get the possession by 27-May-2011, but have not got the possession of the unit for the reasons known to the respondent. The applicant(s)\' money is being withheld by&nbsp; the respondent and used without any interest. That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, The earlier application under form \'N\' could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab. Now applicant(s) has refiled the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement as well as any other relief that this forum deems fit in the interest of justice.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses</p><p>apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified</p><p>explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that</p><p>the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the</p><p>respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without</p><p>delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p>',5118516.00,4840807.00,'2011-05-27 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-01-31 00:00:00','2008-02-28 00:00:00','J1-F10-1004, Tower \'J\', \"The Views\" at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, S