orm \'N\'&nbsp; could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab. Now applicant(s) has refiled the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement as well as any other relief that this forum deems fit in the interest of justice.</p><div><br></div>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p><div><br></div>',5118516.00,4840807.00,'2011-04-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-01-31 00:00:00','2008-01-31 00:00:00','K3-F07-701, The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali\r\n','','',1,1,0,0,'harpreetvarun.gill','2019-03-26 21:47:37.000','harpreetvarun.gill','2019-03-26 21:47:37.000'),(412,1141,'1141',1094,'5307214d-513f-428e-a103-9ead98ac25bf','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-26 21:52:28.000','Karnail Singh Brar Through Tejwant Singh','londonksreracomplainant@gmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'Village Jawahar Singh Wala','Teh. Nihal Singh Wala',28,393,'142055','1','H.No. 2123,','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','Tejwant Singh Sidhu ','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PB0231','The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,1724688888,'SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO No. 120-122, First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Respectfully showeth&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;That the present complaint is being filed&nbsp; by allotee through his attorney. That the applicant had applied for the allotment of a unit &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;number H2GF GF02 in the project of the respondent in the year 2008 and &nbsp;was subsequently was issued an allotment on 01-04-2008. &nbsp;The unit was measuring 1350 Sq. Ft. of Super area.The total consideration &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;amount of the unit was Rs.&nbsp;4432619 (Rs. Forty Four Lakh Thirty Two Thousand Six Hundred Nineteen only). That the applicant has till date i.e 30-03-2010 has paid Rs. 4005708/- (Rs. Forty Lakh Five Thousand Seven Hundred Eight only). That an agreement dated 29-05-2008 was reduced into writing and as per clause number 21.1 of the agreement, the applicant &nbsp;was to get the possession of the said unit within the period of 36 months from the date of allotment, working out to be on 28-05- 2011. Till date the applicant has got no letter of handing over of the &nbsp; possession and for the best reasons known to the&nbsp;respondent. the applicant\'s money is being withheld by the respondent . That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction&nbsp; and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, the applicant has filed the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement. The applicant had filed an application under form \'N\', earlier, but the same could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab and after the decision of the said appeals, this fresh complaint is filed again, seeking the relief which this Hon\'ble Forum deems fit in the interest of Justice.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 500000/- (Rs. Five Lakh only) for monetary losses&nbsp; apart from interest on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justified explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and use the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement.</p>',4432619.00,4005706.00,'2011-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-04-01 00:00:00','2008-05-29 00:00:00','H2GF GF02, The Views, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, SAS Nagar Mohali.\r\n','','',1,1,0,0,'london.ksrera','2019-03-26 21:52:21.000','london.ksrera','2019-03-26 21:52:21.000'),(413,1132,'1132',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Amar Chand','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9988247548,0,0,'House No. 1185','Sector-35 B, D.A.D Colony',6,128,'160035','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0091','Posh City','BABA BANDA SINGH BAHADUR ENTERPRISE','bbsbikpmohali@gmail.com',9915322330,0,'Village Chaper Chiri Kalan','SECTOR 91-92',28,507,'160056','1','Village Chaper Chiri Kalan','SECTOR 91-92',28,507,'160056','0','<p>The complainants booked a residential plot measuring 112.5 sq yards vide application form&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (C-1)dated 29.12.2017. It was assured by the respondent that it has all the approvals and license for the development of project and further assured that the possession will be delivered within 1 year.A total of Rs. 472000/- was paid by the complainants by January, 2018.Copy of receipt is attached as C-2. The location of the plot which was initially shown by the respondent was later on changed by the respondent. There was no high tension wires over the plot when the location of the said plot was shown by the respondent. When the complainants visited the office of respondent for signing the agreement on 16.7.2018, it was informed to them that there are high tension wires over the plot and the layout is still not final. The complainant then asked the respondent to change the location of the plot but the respondent refused to change the plot. Moreover the copy of the agreement given to complainant was not as per RERA. The complainant asked the respondent to refund the amount along with interest. But the respondent only refunded the principal amount vide draft dated 22.11.18 Inspite of number of visits and requests, the respondent has not paid any interest on the refunded amount. Also, the respondent is liable to pay compensation to the complainants. When the plot was sold to the complainants, the respondent was not registered under RERA and also it was not having any license for the development of colony.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>ABC</p>','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 100000/- w.e.f. 29.12.2017 upto 22.11.2018</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 136000/- w.e.f. 02.01.2018 upto 22.11.2018.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 236000/- w.e.f. 10.02.2018 upto 22.11.2018</li><li>&nbsp;To direct the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 50000/- to the complainants.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 20000/-</li></ol><p><br></p>',2360000.00,472000.00,'2018-12-28 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-01-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no. 210','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2019-03-26 22:06:14.000','rerafilingformn','2019-03-26 22:06:14.000'),(418,1132,'1132',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Amar Chand','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9988247548,0,0,'House No. 1185','Sector-35 B, D.A.D Colony',6,128,'160035','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0091','Posh City','BABA BANDA SINGH BAHADUR ENTERPRISE','bbsbikpmohali@gmail.com',9915322330,0,'Village Chaper Chiri Kalan','SECTOR 91-92',28,507,'160056','1','Village Chaper Chiri Kalan','SECTOR 91-92',28,507,'160056','0','<p>The complainants booked a residential plot measuring 112.5 sq yards vide application form (C-1)dated 29.12.2017. It was assured by the respondent that they are duly registered under RERA &amp; it has all the approvals and license for the development of project and further assured that the possession will be delivered within 1 year.A total of Rs. 472000/- was paid by the complainants by January, 2018.Copy of receipt &amp; Cheques is attached as C-2 &amp; C-3 resp. The location of the plot which was initially shown by the respondent was later on changed by the respondent. There was no high tension wires over the plot when the location of the said plot was shown by the respondent. When the complainants visited the office of respondent for signing the agreement on 16.7.2018, it was informed to them that there are high tension wires over the plot and the layout is still not final. The complainant then asked the respondent to change the location of the plot but the respondent refused to change the plot. Moreover the copy of the agreement given to complainant was not as per RERA.The complainant asked the respondent to refund the amount along with interest (C-4). But the respondent only refunded the principal amount vide draft dated 22.11.18(C-5)&nbsp; Inspite of number of visits and requests, the respondent has not paid any interest on the refunded amount. Also, the respondent is liable to pay compensation to the complainants. When the plot was sold to the complainants, the respondent was not registered under RERA and also it was not having any license for the development of colony. The respondent is guilty of making false statement about the location of plot and also of misrepresenting the complainant about its registration under RERA and about the obtaining all the approvals and sanctions for the project. The respondent also made false assurance of delivering the possession within 1 year</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>ABC</p>','<ol><li>The respondent is liable to pay interest on the refunded amount of Rs. 472000/- and compensation to the complainant as it was obligatory for it under Section 12 to disclose true facts and by making false statements in respect of location of plot, about delivery of possession within 1 year, about its registration under RERA and about having all the approvals and sanctions, the respondent had allured the complainant to pay money and thus has failed to discharge its obligation as provided under Section 12 of RERA and therefore following necessary directions be issued;</li><li>to direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 100000/- w.e.f. 29.12.2017 upto 22.11.2018</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 136000/- w.e.f. 02.01.2018 upto 22.11.2018.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 236000/- w.e.f. 10.02.2018 upto 22.11.2018</li><li>&nbsp;To direct the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 50000/- to the complainants for mental &amp; physical harassment to the complainants. The respondent is liable to compensate the complainants for the pain &amp; sufferings suffered by them due to false promises and misrepresentation by&nbsp; the respondent. there is no fault on the part of complainants, as they got sanctioned a loan of Rs. 2000000/- (C-6) for making payment to respondent and also paid Rs. 1180/- whih is liable to be refunded by the respondent.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 20000/-</li></ol><p><br></p>',2360000.00,472000.00,'2018-12-28 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-01-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no. 210','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2019-03-26 22:52:09.000','rerafilingformn','2019-03-26 22:52:09.000'),(419,1132,'1132',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Amar Chand','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9988247548,0,0,'House No. 1185','Sector-35 B, D.A.D Colony',6,128,'160035','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0091','Posh City','BABA BANDA SINGH BAHADUR ENTERPRISE','bbsbikpmohali@gmail.com',9915322330,0,'Village Chaper Chiri Kala