e complainants booked a residential plot measuring 112.5 sq yards vide application form (C-1)dated 29.12.2017. It was assured by the respondent that they are duly registered under RERA &amp; it has all the approvals and license for the development of project and further assured that the possession will be delivered within 1 year.A total of Rs. 472000/- was paid by the complainants by January, 2018.Copy of receipt &amp; Cheques is attached as C-2 &amp; C-3 resp. The location of the plot which was initially shown by the respondent was later on changed by the respondent. There was no high tension wires over the plot when the location of the said plot was shown by the respondent. When the complainants visited the office of respondent for signing the agreement on 16.7.2018, it was informed to them that there are high tension wires over the plot and the layout is still not final. The complainant then asked the respondent to change the location of the plot but the respondent refused to change the plot. Moreover the copy of the agreement given to complainant was not as per RERA.The complainant asked the respondent to refund the amount along with interest (C-4). But the respondent only refunded the principal amount vide draft dated 22.11.18(C-5)&nbsp; Inspite of number of visits and requests, the respondent has not paid any interest on the refunded amount. Also, the respondent is liable to pay compensation to the complainants. When the plot was sold to the complainants, the respondent was not registered under RERA and also it was not having any license for the development of colony. The respondent is guilty of making false statement about the location of plot and also of misrepresenting the complainant about its registration under RERA and about the obtaining all the approvals and sanctions for the project. The respondent also made false assurance of delivering the possession within 1 year</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>ABC</p>','<ol><li>The respondent is liable to pay interest on the refunded amount of Rs. 472000/- and compensation to the complainant as it was obligatory for it under Section 12 &amp; 18(3) to disclose true facts and by making false statements in respect of location of plot, about delivery of possession within 1 year, about its registration under RERA and about having all the approvals and sanctions, the respondent had allured the complainant to pay money and thus has failed to discharge its obligation as provided under Section 12&nbsp; &amp; Section 18 (3) of RERA and therefore following necessary directions be issued;</li><li>to direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 100000/- w.e.f. 29.12.2017 upto 22.11.2018</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 136000/- w.e.f. 02.01.2018 upto 22.11.2018.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest&nbsp; as prescribed under Rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, 2017 , on the refunded amount of Rs. 236000/- w.e.f. 10.02.2018 upto 22.11.2018</li><li>&nbsp;To direct the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 50000/- to the complainants for mental &amp; physical harassment to the complainants. The respondent is liable to compensate the complainants for the pain &amp; sufferings suffered by them due to false promises and misrepresentation by&nbsp; the respondent. There is no fault on the part of complainants, as they got sanctioned a loan of Rs. 2000000/- (C-6) for making payment to respondent and also paid Rs. 1180/- towards sanctioning of loan, which is also liable to be refunded by the respondent.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 20000/-</li></ol><p><br></p>',2360000.00,472000.00,'2018-12-28 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2018-01-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no. 210','','',1,1,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2019-03-26 23:08:45.000','rerafilingformn','2019-03-26 23:08:45.000'),(422,1153,'1153',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Suresh Kumar Rawal','jeetendracapricon@gmail.com',9814482802,0,0,'H.No.412,first floor, Phase 2','',28,507,'160055','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0125','RKM CITY','Kawaljit Singh Ahluwalia','rkmhousing@gmail.com',9876240145,0,'sco 1-4, behind chandigarh engineering college, sector 112, landran, sas nagar, mohali','',28,507,'140307','1','sco 1-4, behind chandigarh engineering college, sector 112, landran, sas nagar, mohali','',28,507,'140307','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',1696000.00,700000.00,'2016-09-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-12-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no 53, sector 111 , mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-03-27 05:23:18.000','AdvSaksham','2019-03-27 05:23:18.000'),(423,1154,'1154',1447,'2575c5ff-b349-4eb9-9d11-d1069a0d780b','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswinder  Kaur','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',8360380893,0,0,'#644 Ward No 6 Raman Cinema Road Mansa','Tehsil Mansa',28,386,'151505','1','Jagtar Singh Advocate Chamber No.41 District Courts  Complex  Mansa','',28,386,'151505','Jagtar Singh','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',9815092193,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-MNS50-PM0031','PUDA Enclave Mansa','Estate Officer PUDA','cabdabti@gmail.com',0,0,'estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',3675000.00,3417750.00,'2018-01-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','309','','',2,0,0,0,'punjab','2019-03-27 10:17:36.000','punjab','2019-03-27 10:17:36.000'),(425,1154,'1154',1447,'2575c5ff-b349-4eb9-9d11-d1069a0d780b','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswinder  Kaur','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',8360380893,0,0,'#644 Ward No 6 Raman Cinema Road Mansa','Tehsil Mansa',28,386,'151505','1','Jagtar Singh Advocate Chamber No.41 District Courts  Complex  Mansa','',28,386,'151505','Jagtar Singh','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',9815092193,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-MNS50-PM0031','PUDA Enclave Mansa','Estate Officer PUDA','cabdabti@gmail.com',0,0,'estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','i. that the scheme was opened on 18-11-2013. and closed on 17-12-2013. And applicant paid Rs. 3.5/- lakh.','<p>abc</p>',3675000.00,3417750.00,'2018-01-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','309','','',2,0,0,0,'punjab','2019-03-27 20:42:58.000','punjab','2019-03-27 20:42:58.000'),(443,1154,'1154',1447,'2575c5ff-b349-4eb9-9d11-d1069a0d780b','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswinder  Kaur','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',8360380893,0,0,'#644 Ward No 6 Raman Cinema Road Mansa','Tehsil Mansa',28,386,'151505','1','Jagtar Singh Advocate Chamber No.41 District Courts  Complex  Mansa','',28,386,'151505','Jagtar Singh','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',9815092193,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-MNS50-PM0031','PUDA Enclave Mansa','Estate Officer PUDA','cabdabti@gmail.com',0,0,'estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','<p>The scheme Annexure A1 was opened on 18-11-2013 and closed on 17-12-2013 regarding development of residential plots at the rate of Rs 7000 per sq yard. The applicant applied for a plot of 500 sq yard in general category vide application no 0456 on 17 December 2013 by depositing Rs 350000 (10 percent of the plot money) as the total plot money was 35 lacs. Then the respondent issued Letter of Intent Annexure A2 on 24 March 2014 demanding Rs 525000 (15 percent of the plot money) within 30 days which was deposited vide receipt Annexure A3 on 23-04-2014. Then Allotment letter dated 11 July 2016 regarding plot no 309 (park facing) Annexure A4 was issued and enhanced the total plot money by 5 percent to Rs 3675000 demanding further Rs 43750 within 30 days to complete the 25 percent of the plot money which was deposited vide receipt Annexure A5. The remaining 75 percent amount was demanded in six half yearly installments starting the first installment after one year from the date of Allotment letter in prospectus of the scheme Letter of Intent and Allotment letter and promised to hand over the possession of the plot within 18 months from the date of Allotment letter or at the completion of the development works at the site whichever is earlier. The applicant is regularly depositing the installments as per schedule i.e. Rs 790125 vide receipt Annexure A6 Rs 597187 vide receipt Annexure A7 Rs 569625 vide receipt Annexure A8 Rs 542063 vide receipt Annexure A9. But the respondent failed to hand over the possession of the plot with completion of the development works by the due date which lapsed on 11 January 2018. The applicant was planning to construct her dream house in the project of the respondent had the development works completed in time.</p><p>Now she is no more interested in the project as the respondent failed to provide even basic amenities like electricity water supply and sewage till date but to talk about other facilities and there is no hope in near future.<br></p>','<p>That in view of the above stated facts the applicant prays for the refund of her investment money of Rs.3417750/- along with interest under section 18(1)(3) and compensation for mental agony, harassment and litigation expenses under section 71 (1) to (3) of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016 read with rules 36 and 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development Rules) 2017.</p>',3675000.00,3417750.00,'2018-01-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','309','','',2,0,0,0,'punjab','2019-03-28 06:46:07.000','punjab','2019-03-28 06:46:07.000'),(444,1154,'1154',1447,'2575c5ff-b349-4eb9-9d11-d1069a0d780b','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswinder  Kaur','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',8360380893,0,0,'#644 Ward No 6 Raman Cinema Road Mansa','Tehsil Mansa',28,386,'151505','1','Jagtar Singh Advocate Chamber No.41 District Courts  Complex  Mansa','',28,386,'151505','Jagtar Singh','jagtardhaliwal13477@gmail.com',9815092193,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-MNS50-PM0031','PUDA Enclave Mansa','Estate Officer PUDA','cabdabti@gmail.com',0,0,'estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','estate officer PUDA ','PUDA Complex , Bhagu Road , Bhatinda',28,84,'151001','1','<p>The scheme Annexure A1 was opened on 18-11-2013 and closed on 17-12-2013 regarding development of residential plots at the rate of Rs 7000 per sq yard. The applicant applied for a plot of 500 sq yard in general category vide application no 0456 on 17 December 2013 by depositing Rs 350000 (10 percent of the plot money) as the total plot money was 35 lacs. Then the respondent issued Letter of Intent Annexure A2 on 24 March 2014 demanding Rs 525000 (15 percent of the plot money) within 30 days which was deposited vide receipt Annexure A3 on 23-04-2014. Then Allotment letter dated 11 July 2016 regarding plot no 309 (park facing) Annexure A4 was issued and enhanced the total plot money by 5 percent to Rs 3675000 demanding further Rs 43750 within 30 days to complete the 25 percent of the plot money which was deposited vide receipt Annexure A5. The remaining 75 percent amount was demanded in six half yearly installments starting the first installment after one year from the date of Allotment letter in prospectus of the scheme Letter of Intent and Allotment letter and promised to hand over the possession of the plot within 18 months from the date of Allotment letter or at the completion of the development works at the site whichever is earlier. The applicant is regularly depositing the installments as per schedule i.e. Rs 790125 vide receipt Annexure A6 Rs 597187 vide receipt Annexure A7 Rs 569625 vide receipt Annexure A8 Rs 542063 vide receipt Annexure A9. But the respondent failed to hand over the possession of the plot with completion of the development works by the due date which lapsed on 11 January 2018. The applicant was planning to construct her dream house in the project of the respondent had the development works completed in time.</p><p>Now she is no more interested in the project as the respondent failed to provide even basic amenities like electricity water supply and sewage till date but to talk about other facilities and there is no hope in near future.<br></p>','<p>That in view of the above stated facts the applicant prays for the refund of her investment money of Rs.3417750/- along with interest under section 18(1)(3) and compensation for mental agony, harassment and litigation expenses under section 71 (1) to (3) of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016 read with rules 36 and 37 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development Rules) 2017.</p>',3675000.00,3417750.00,'2018-01-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','309','','',2,0,0,0,'punjab','2019-03-28 06:47:54.000','punjab','2019-03-28 06:47:54.000'),(445,1153,'1153',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Suresh Kumar Rawal','jeetendracapricon@gmail.com',9814482802,0,0,'H.No.412,first floor, Phase 2','',28,507,'160055','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0125','RKM CITY','Kawaljit Singh Ahluwalia','rkmhousing@gmail.com',9876240145,0,'H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',1696000.00,700000.00,'2016-09-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-12-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no 53, sector 111 , mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-03-28 07:48:59.000','AdvSaksham','2019-03-28 07:48:59.000'),(446,1153,'1153',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Suresh Kumar Rawal','jeetendracapricon@gmail.com',9814482802,0,0,'H.No.412,first floor, Phase 2','',28,507,'160055','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0125','RKM CITY','Kawaljit Singh Ahluwalia','rkmhousing@gmail.com',9876240145,0,'H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','<p>The Owner of the land in dispute which measures 106 sq. yards had got the</p><p>Memorandum of understanding for their land on 7-oct-2016, stating the</p><p>various terms and conditions for the land. The complainant had purchased</p><p>this land through an Agent named Tapan Deewan. At the time of presentation</p><p>the ops had shown a different piece of land but at the time of Allotment</p><p>another location was allocated with no mark or number for identification. At</p><p>the time of purchasing the OP 1 and 2 made several promises but nothing</p><p>ever came into effect. The CEO Mr. Kanwal Ahluwalia met the complainant</p><p>during the time of payment and assured a safe investment. The complainant</p><p>did several correspondences, even in person but nothing concrete was ever</p><p>achieved. The OP’s barely replied and in which they gave some assurances in</p><p>regards to the refund but again nothing only disappointment was received. A</p><p>mail Dated 31.05.2018 also consists of the surrender letter given on the</p><p>advice of the CEO with an assurance of Refund. Like any other time this also</p><p>proved to be just another faulty claim. This inhuman treatment of the OP’S</p><p>has affected the family’s health both physically and mentally. This project</p><p>involves Manohar Group vide item 486 of RERA list.</p>','<p>i. Refund of Rs. 7,00,000 so paid with an interest of 18% of the cost</p><p>of plot per annum from the date of Memorandum of</p><p>Understanding till the date of pronouncing of final judgment.</p><p>ii. Compensation of Rs. 2,00,000 towards mental agony,</p><p>harassment, inconvenience and medical bills in the interest of</p><p>justice.</p><p>iii. Refund of Rs. 25,000 towards legal expenses.</p><p>iv. Instructions to the OPS be directed keeping in mind the</p><p>safety of the complainant in the interest of justice.</p><p>v. Any other order or relief as this authority may feel</p><p>appropriate in the interest of justice.</p>',1696000.00,700000.00,'2016-09-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-12-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no 53, sector 111 , mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-03-28 12:01:40.000','AdvSaksham','2019-03-28 12:01:40.000'),(447,1153,'1153',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-01 20:01:40.000','Suresh Kumar Rawal','jeetendracapricon@gmail.com',9814482802,0,0,'H.No.412,first floor, Phase 2','',28,507,'160055','1','sco 117-118, 2nd floor , sector 17 B','',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0125','RKM CITY','Kawaljit Singh Ahluwalia','rkmhousing@gmail.com',9876240145,0,'H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','<p>The Owner of the land in dispute which measures 106 sq. yards had got the</p><p>Memorandum of understanding for their land on 7-oct-2016, stating the</p><p>various terms and conditions for the land. The complainant had purchased</p><p>this land through an Agent named Tapan Deewan. At the time of presentation</p><p>the ops had shown a different piece of land but at the time of Allotment</p><p>another location was allocated with no mark or number for identification. At</p><p>the time of purchasing the OP 1 and 2 made several promises but nothing</p><p>ever came into effect. The CEO Mr. Kanwal Ahluwalia met the complainant</p><p>during the time of payment and assured a safe investment. The complainant</p><p>did several correspondences, even in person but nothing concrete was ever</p><p>achieved. The OP’s barely replied and in which they gave some assurances in</p><p>regards to the refund but again nothing only disappointment was received. A</p><p>mail Dated 31.05.2018 also consists of the surrender letter given on the</p><p>advice of the CEO with an assurance of Refund. Like any other time this also</p><p>proved to be just another faulty claim. This inhuman treatment of the OP’S</p><p>has affected the family’s health both physically and mentally. This project</p><p>involves Manohar Group vide item 486 of RERA list.</p>','<p>i. Refund of Rs. 7,00,000 so paid with an interest of 18% of the cost</p><p>of plot per annum from the date of Memorandum of</p><p>Understanding till the date of pronouncing of final judgment.</p><p>ii. Compensation of Rs. 2,00,000 towards mental agony,</p><p>harassment, inconvenience and medical bills in the interest of</p><p>justice.</p><p>iii. Refund of Rs. 25,000 towards legal expenses.</p><p>iv. Instructions to the OPS be directed keeping in mind the</p><p>safety of the complainant in the interest of justice.</p><p>v. Any other order or relief as this authority may feel</p><p>appropriate in the interest of justice.</p>',1696000.00,700000.00,'2016-09-07 00:00:00.0