 within 18 months from the date of Allotment letter or at the completion of the development works at the site whichever is earlier. The applicant is regularly depositing the installments as per schedule i.e. Rs 790125 vide receipt Annexure A6 Rs 597187 vide receipt Annexure A7 Rs 569625 vide receipt Annexure A8 Rs 542063 vide receipt Annexure A9. But the respondent failed to hand over the possession of the plot with completion of the development works by the due date which lapsed on 11 January 2018. The applicant was planning to construct her dream house in the project of the respondent had the development works completed in time.</p><p>Now she is no more interested in the project as the respondent failed to provide even basic amenities like electricity water supply and sewage till date but to talk about other facilities and there is no hope in near future.<br></p>','<p>That in view of the above stated facts the applicant prays for the refund of her investment money of Rs.3417750/- along with interest under section 18(1a)(3),Section 31 and compensation for mental agony, harassment and litigation expenses under section 71 (1) of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016 read with rules 37 of the Punjab EState Real Estate (Regulation and Development Rules) 2017.</p>',3675000.00,3417750.00,'2018-01-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-07-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','309','','',1,1,0,0,'punjab','2019-03-28 17:04:33.000','punjab','2019-03-28 17:04:33.000'),(449,1155,'1155',1457,'850bbb82-e04e-4f42-8bac-26b7e59a463c','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Harpreet Singh Dalbir Singh Barjinderpaul Gill Gill','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 65','Sector 5 ,',6,128,'160015','1','F-1403, 14th Flr., Tower \"F\", Sushma Chandigarh Grande','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PRO231_','The Villas, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills,  SAS Nagar','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'SCO 160-162,  First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 160-162,  First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>That the present complaint is being filed by NRI allotee(s) as co-applicant(s), as the father of the applicant(s) has expired. That the applicant(s)had applied for the allotment\r\n</p><p>of a Villa No.131/Augusta Park, in the year 2008, by the name of residential project \'The Villas\' in \"Mohali Hills,Sec-109,SAS Nagar Mohali. The applicant(s) were subsequently issued an allotment on 07-05-2008 of a residential\r\n</p><p>Plot area of Villa measuring 400 Sq. Yrds. The total consideration amount of the unit was Rs.16073472/-(Rs. One Crore Sixty Lakh Seventy Three Thousand Four Hundred Seventy Two only). That the applicant \r\n</p><p>had opted to pay 95% of the amount mentioned above and paid Rs.15222198/- (Rs. One Crore Fifty Two Lakh Twenty Two Thousand One Hundred and Ninety Eight only) on 15-04-2008. That as per clause 8 of agreement, the applicant(s)were to get the possession of the said unit within the maximum period of 30 months(inclusive of grace period)from date of agreement. The applicant(s) were to get the possession by 03-June-2010,but have not got the possession of the unit for the reasons known to the respondent. The applicant(s)\' money is being withheld by the respondent and used without any interest. That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, The earlier application under form \'N\' could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab. Now applicant(s) has refiled the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed in the agreement as well as any other relief that this forum d</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 2500000/- (Rs. Twenty Five Lakh only) for monetary losses apart from the interest @18% p.a. on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justifiable explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. that the compensation as paid apart from interest is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent has played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and used the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement and any other relief in addition to above said compensation that this Hon\'ble court deems fit in the interest of justice.<br></p>',16073472.00,15222198.00,'2011-01-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-05-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Villa No. 131, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills, Sector 109, SAS Nagar Mohali\r\n','','',2,0,0,0,'harbardal.gill','2019-03-30 11:49:28.000','harbardal.gill','2019-03-30 11:49:28.000'),(450,1155,'1155',1457,'850bbb82-e04e-4f42-8bac-26b7e59a463c','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-30 12:49:29.000','Harpreet Singh Dalbir Singh Barjinderpaul Gill Gill','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,0,'H.No. 65','Sector 5 ,',6,128,'160015','1','F-1403, 14th Flr., Tower \"F\", Sushma Chandigarh Grande','Sector 15 C,',6,128,'160015','Advocate Varun Luthra','advocate_varunl@hotmail.com',9815998858,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PRO231_','The Villas, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills,  SAS Nagar','Emaar MGF Land Ltd. Through authorised signatory','mohalihills@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'SCO 160-162,  First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 160-162,  First Floor','Sector 17C, ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>That the present complaint is being filed by NRI allotee(s) as co-applicant(s), as the father of the applicant(s) has expired. That the applicant(s)had applied for the allotment of a Villa No.131/Augusta Park, in the year 2008, by the name of residential project \'The Villas\' in \"Mohali Hills,Sec-109,SAS Nagar Mohali. The applicant(s) were subsequently issued an allotment on 07-05-2008 of a residential Plot area of Villa measuring 400 Sq. Yrds. The total consideration amount of the unit was Rs.16073472/-(Rs. One Crore Sixty Lakh Seventy Three Thousand Four Hundred Seventy Two only). That the applicant(s) had opted to pay 95% of the amount mentioned above and paid Rs.15222198/- (Rs. One Crore Fifty Two Lakh Twenty Two Thousand One Hundred and Ninety Eight only) on 15-04-2008. That as per clause 8 of agreement, the applicant(s)were to get the possession of the said unit within the maximum period of 30 months(inclusive of grace period)from date of agreement. The applicant(s) were to get the possession by 03-June-2010,but have not got the possession of the unit for the reasons known to the respondent. The applicant(s)\' money is being withheld by the respondent and used without any interest. That keeping the track record of the respondent in view, the applicant seeks to withdraw from this project in consonance with the Section 18 (1)(a) of RERA and the appeal number 53 of 2018 (along with other appeals) decided by the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab on 27-Feb-2019 regarding the jurisdiction and powers of Adjudicating Officer of RERA Punjab, The earlier application under form \'N\' could not be decided as the appeals were pending before the Hon\'ble RERA Appellate Authority, Punjab. Now applicant(s) has refiled the present complaint seeking refund, compensation and interest on the money withheld by the respondent till realization as the developer has not been able to fulfil its part of promise as agreed, as well as any other relief that this forum deems fit.</p>','<p>That the applicant seeks the compensation of of Rs. 2500000/- (Rs. Twenty Five Lakh only) for monetary losses apart from the interest @18% p.a. on the money withheld by the respondent without any sufficient reasons and justifiable explanation. The applicant further prays for Rs. 50000/- (Rs. Fifty Thousand only) as litigation costs. That the respondent be further directed to pay compensation , apart from the interest on the amount with held&nbsp; by the respondent, as it is necessary to be imposed upon the respondent, as the respondent have played a fraud upon the applicant by extracting money and used the same without delivering the unit well in time as per the agreement and any other relief in addition to above said compensation that this Hon\'ble court deems fit in the interest of justice. That great prejudice has been caused to the applicant(s) in terms of the interest on the investment, which would have a handsome return had the applicant(s) would have not blocked their money with the respondent for the last 10 years(approx.). The respondents time and again used to make lame excuses about the development of the project and kept the applicant(s) in dark. In toatality the decision of the applicant(s) has turned out not only a wrong one, but a harsh lesson in life for not falling prey to false promises of such companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>',16073472.00,15222198.00,'2011-01-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2008-05-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Villa No. 131, Augusta Park, Mohali Hills, Sector 109, SAS Nagar Mohali\r\n','','',1,1,0,0,'harbardal.gill','2019-03-30 12:47:17.000','harbardal.gill','2019-03-30 12:47:17.000'),(451,1046,'1046',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-31 12:08:18.000','DAKSHA','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'H. NO. 1/3 BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','1','H. NO. 1/3 BIJAI PALACE','MANDI',14,106,'175001','RAVINDER PAL SINGH','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0076','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT. LTD.','info@ansalapi.com',0,0,'SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','<p>Respondents came up with commercial project as CITI CENTRE at Sector 115 Mohali which is registered with RERA as ORCHARD COUNTY II Commercial project.</p><p>Husband of the complainant approached the Respondents for booking of one showroom floated by the Respondent. </p><p>Respondents also allured the Complainant of ASSURED RETURNS on the amount invested till the date of possession. </p><p>Initially complainant booked one showroom bearing No. 6UGF measuring 1772 sq. ft. @ Rs.30,12,400/-. </p><p>Agreement executed on 09.02.2010 (A-2) </p><p>Complainant deposited Rs.28,61,780/- on 30.01.2010.</p><p>Agreement executed on 09.02.2010 promising possession within 42 months maximum.&nbsp;</p><p> </p><p>Respondent was liable to pay Rs.53,847/- per month which was paid by 31.03.2012. </p><p>Since the construction of the showroom was very slow complainant decided to shift in other showroom in same project.</p><p> Respondent offered two showrooms bearing no. 03SF and 04SF.</p><p>Complainant paid Rs.20,00,000/- more on 25.05.2012. </p><p>Price of each showroom was fixed as Rs.25,00,000/-. Each unit is measuring 1588 sq. ft. </p><p>Complainant paid total Rs.48,61,780/- till date for both showrooms.</p><p>New Agreement of SF03 and SF04 showrooms executed on 08.06.2012&nbsp; wherein possession was to be given within 42 months maximum which expired on 08.12.2016.</p><p>Construction has been stopped in between. Possession not offered till date.</p><p>Assured Returns stopped after JULY, 2016 violating the terms of the agreement as well as provisions of RERA Act.</p><p>Respondents are in arrears of Rs.19,89,176/- (01.07.2016 to 31.10.2018) for both showrooms as ASSURED RETURN and they may be directed to deposit the said amount as interim measure.</p><p>Present application filed seeking possession of the Unit No.03SF and 04SF alongwith assured returns till actual possession of unit and compensation for harrassment, and cost of litigation.</p>','<p>SEEKING POSSESSION OF THE UNIT NO. 03SF and 04Sf, CITI&nbsp; CENTRE PROJECT (ORCHARD COUNTY - II), SECTOR 115 MOHALI </p><p>ASSURED RETURN AMOUNTING TO RS.19,89,176/- DUE W.E.F. 01.07.2016 TILL 31.10.2018 </p><p>FUTURE ASSURED RETURNS TILL ACTUAL POSSESSION OF SHOWROOM No. 03SF and 04SF. </p><p>COMPENSATION OF RS.15,00,000/- AND RS,1,10,000/- AS COST OF LITIGATION.&nbsp;</p>',2500000.00,2430890.00,'2015-06-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2012-06-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','03 SF, CITY CENTRE, SECTOR 115 MOHALI, ANSAL LOTUS MELANGE PROJECTS PVT LTD','','',1,1,0,0,'advravinder','2019-03-31 11:38:13.000','advravinder','2019-03-31 11:38:13.000'),(452,1156,'1156',1367,'5dd7625b-2bb2-4b5e-8466-b20eef3fe061','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sanjeev Sharma','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,0,'386','sector15',13,15,'134113','1','386','sector15',13,15,'134113','Sanjeev Sharma','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0084','Wave Estates','Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd','estate@thewwavegroup.com',0,0,'C-1 Sector-3, Noida','',33,218,'201301','1','C-1 Sector-3, Noida','',33,218,'201301','1','That complainants are seeking refund of amount paid by then alongwith interest, as per provision of the Act under section 28 of act read with rule 15 of Punjab state Real Estate (Regulation of developers) rules, 2017. That complainants are also seeking compensation for actual loss suffered in payment of EMI\'s without getting possession and also for \'rent paid by them due to non delivery&nbsp; of floor/unit as per agreement. litigation cost of Rs. 55,000/- are also sought from respondents','<p>that complainants entered into agreement with Respondents for buying of Residential Floor in \'Wave Estate\' sector-85, 99 Mohali. Punjab. That agreement was executed on 16-4-2014 and as per clause 5.1 of agreement, possession was to be delivered in 30 months i.e. 15-10-2016. That as per agreed date possession was not delivered. That unit No. 177, First floor Block-A, Sector-85, 99 in \'Wave Estate\' was allotted to complainants. That complainants paid Rs.57,64442/- to Respondents but respondents seeking more money without handing over possession. no completion /occupation Certificate of project/ Unit&nbsp; allotted to respondents. Complainants burdened with EMI\'s as well as payment of Rent,as possession mot handed on time. so refund prayed for.</p>',60960005757.00,5764442.00,'2016-10-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-10-15 00:00:00','2014-04-16 00:00:00','177/FF wave floor','','',2,0,0,0,'rajinder112','2019-04-01 18:41:11.000','rajinder112','2019-04-01 18:41:11.000'),(453,1156,'1156',1367,'5dd7625b-2bb2-4b5e-8466-b20eef3fe061','FormTypeN',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jasbir Singh/ Sweety Bawa','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,0,'386','sector15',13,15,'134113','1','386','sector15',13,15,'134113','Sanjeev Sharma','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0084','Wave Estates','Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd','estate@thewwavegroup.com',0,0,'C-1 Sector-3, Noida','',33,218,'201301','1','C-1 Sector-3, Noida','',33,218,'201301','1','That complainants are seeking refund of amount paid by then alongwith interest, as per provision of the Act under section 28 of act read with rule 15 of Punjab state Real Estate (Regulation of developers) rules, 2017. That complainants are also seeking compensation for actual loss suffered in payment of EMI\'s without getting possession and also for \'rent paid by them due to non delivery&nbsp; of floor/unit as per agreement. litigation cost of Rs. 55,000/- are also sought from respondents','<p>that complainants entered into agreement with Respondents for buying of Residential Floor in \'Wave Estate\' sector-85, 99 Mohali. Punjab. That agreement was executed on 16-4-2014 and as per clause 5.1 of agreement, possession was to be delivered in 30 months i.e. 15-10-2016. That as per agreed date possession was not delivered. That unit No. 177, First floor Block-A, Sector-85, 99 in \'Wave Estate\' was allotted to complainants. That complainants paid Rs.57,64442/- to Respondents but respondents seeking more money without handing over possession. no completion /occupation Certificate of project/ Unit&nbsp; allotted to respondents. Complainants burdened with EMI\'s as well as payment of Rent,as possession mot handed on time. so refund prayed for.</p>',60960005757.00,5764442.00,'2016-10-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2016-10-15 00:00:00','2014-04-16 00:00:00','177/FF wave floor','','',1,0,0,0,'rajinder112','2019-04-01 18:43:45.000','rajinder112','2019-04-01 18:43:45.000'),(454,1153,'1153',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-01 20:01:40.000','Suresh Kumar Rawal','jeetendracapricon@gmail.com',9814482802,0,0,'H.No.412,first floor, Phase 2','',28,507,'160055','1','726 sector 10','',13,1,'134113','Saksham Arora','advocatesaksham@gmail.com',9872628189,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0125','RKM CITY','Kawaljit Singh Ahluwalia','rkmhousing@gmail.com',9876240145,0,'H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','H. No. 1568 , Sector-34 D  Chandigarh , Chandigarh ','',6,128,'160012','1','<p>The Owner of the land in dispute which measures 106 sq. yards had got the</p><p>Memorandum of understanding for their land on 7-oct-2016, stating the</p><p>various terms and conditions for the land. The complainant had purchased</p><p>this land through an Agent named Tapan Deewan. At the time of presentation</p><p>the ops had shown a different piece of land but at the time of Allotment</p><p>another location was allocated with no mark or number for identification. At</p><p>the time of purchasing the OP 1 and 2 made several promises but nothing</p><p>ever came into effect. The CEO Mr. Kanwal Ahluwalia met the complainant</p><p>during the time of payment and assured a safe investment. The complainant</p><p>did several correspondences, even in person but nothing concrete was ever</p><p>achieved. The OP’s barely replied and in which they gave some assurances in</p><p>regards to the refund but again nothing only disappointment was received. A</p><p>mail Dated 31.05.2018 also consists of the surrender letter given on the</p><p>advice of the CEO with an assurance of Refund. Like any other time this also</p><p>proved to be just another faulty claim. This inhuman treatment of the OP’S</p><p>has affected the family’s health both physically and mentally. This project</p><p>involves Manohar Group vide item 486 of RERA list.</p>','<p>i. Refund of Rs. 7,00,000 so paid with an interest of 18% of the cost</p><p>of plot per annum from the date of Memorandum of</p><p>Understanding till the date of pronouncing of final judgment.</p><p>ii. Compensation of Rs. 2,00,000 towards mental agony,</p><p>harassment, inconvenience and medical bills in the interest of</p><p>justice.</p><p>iii. Refund of Rs. 25,000 towards legal expenses.</p><p>iv. Instructions to the OPS be directed keeping in mind the</p><p>safety of the complainant in the interest of justice.</p><p>v. Any other order or relief as this authority may feel</p><p>appropriate in the interest of justice.</p>',1696000.00,700000.00,'2016-09-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','','1','','2017-12-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','plot no 53, sector 111 , mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'AdvSaksham','2019-04-02 15:23:04.000','AdvSaksham','2019-04-02 15:23:04.000'),(455,1153,'1153',1368,'06cc119c-147e-47df-9860-9a89e157b105','FormTypeN',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-01 20:01:40.000','Suresh Kumar Rawal','jeetendracapricon@gmail.com',9814482802,0,0,'H.No.412,first floor, Phase 2','',28,507,'160055','1','726 sector 10','',13,1,'134113','Saksham Aro